MGFmNDAyN2EyNWVkZmVhY2I2OTRjNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/module-management-community/commit/33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85","sha":"33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/commits/33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85"}],"sha":"7f254c5373228d04f0af4027a25edfeacb694c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/commits/7f254c5373228d04f0af4027a25edfeacb694c42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/commits/33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:07:24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:07:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: remediate Dependabot alerts across frontend and test harness (#14)\n\nResolves the open Dependabot alerts in the root module tree and the\nCypress test harness.\n\nRoot (runtime + build deps):\n- Runtime: dompurify 3.4.11, lodash 4.18.1, lodash-es 4.18.1,\n  node-fetch 2.7.0, yaml 1.10.3, @babel/runtime 7.29.7\n- Build: @babel/core 7.29.7, @babel/plugin-transform-modules-systemjs\n  7.29.7, fast-uri 3.1.3, flatted 3.4.2, form-data 3.0.5, glob 10.5.0,\n  immutable 5.1.9, ip-address 10.2.0, minimatch 3.1.5/9.0.9,\n  serialize-javascript 7.0.7, tar 7.5.19, tar-fs 2.1.5, tmp 0.2.7,\n  ws 7.5.11, @tootallnate/once 2.0.1, webpack 5.108.4, picomatch\n  2.3.2/4.0.5, postcss 8.5.16\n- js-yaml: bumped xmlbuilder2 to 4.x (uses js-yaml ^4.1.1) to drop the\n  exact-pinned vulnerable js-yaml 3.14.1; @cyclonedx SBOM still builds\n\nMulti-major transitives (glob, flatted, minimatch, picomatch, js-yaml,\npostcss) resolved per-major so each major keeps a working API.\n\nTest harness (tests/): form-data 2.5.6/4.0.6, tmp 0.2.7, js-yaml\n3.15.0/4.3.0, qs 6.15.3, uuid 11.1.1; converted the lockfile config to\nYarn Classic (removed stale .yarnrc.yml).\n\nLeft open (no non-breaking fix; all development scope):\n- postcss 7.0.39 — required by 9+ postcss-7 plugins; 7->8 is a breaking\n  plugin-API change\n- libxmljs2 0.35.0 — no patched version published (native lib)\n\nTest plan: mvn clean install (Java 17) green; Cypress 116/116 pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9fddbcfbf48b720e7a7db68f0c22fc9d64e9997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/git/trees/e9fddbcfbf48b720e7a7db68f0c22fc9d64e9997"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/git/commits/33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85","verification":{"payload":"tree e9fddbcfbf48b720e7a7db68f0c22fc9d64e9997\nparent b044ad547bb73d02418ac20196c97d7fe940e973\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783537644 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783537644 +0200\n\nfix: remediate Dependabot alerts across frontend and test harness (#14)\n\nResolves the open Dependabot alerts in the root module tree and the\nCypress test harness.\n\nRoot (runtime + build deps):\n- Runtime: dompurify 3.4.11, lodash 4.18.1, lodash-es 4.18.1,\n  node-fetch 2.7.0, yaml 1.10.3, @babel/runtime 7.29.7\n- Build: @babel/core 7.29.7, @babel/plugin-transform-modules-systemjs\n  7.29.7, fast-uri 3.1.3, flatted 3.4.2, form-data 3.0.5, glob 10.5.0,\n  immutable 5.1.9, ip-address 10.2.0, minimatch 3.1.5/9.0.9,\n  serialize-javascript 7.0.7, tar 7.5.19, tar-fs 2.1.5, tmp 0.2.7,\n  ws 7.5.11, @tootallnate/once 2.0.1, webpack 5.108.4, picomatch\n  2.3.2/4.0.5, postcss 8.5.16\n- js-yaml: bumped xmlbuilder2 to 4.x (uses js-yaml ^4.1.1) to drop the\n  exact-pinned vulnerable js-yaml 3.14.1; @cyclonedx SBOM still builds\n\nMulti-major transitives (glob, flatted, minimatch, picomatch, js-yaml,\npostcss) resolved per-major so each major keeps a working API.\n\nTest harness (tests/): form-data 2.5.6/4.0.6, tmp 0.2.7, js-yaml\n3.15.0/4.3.0, qs 6.15.3, uuid 11.1.1; converted the lockfile config to\nYarn Classic (removed stale .yarnrc.yml).\n\nLeft open (no non-breaking fix; all development scope):\n- postcss 7.0.39 — required by 9+ postcss-7 plugins; 7->8 is a breaking\n  plugin-API change\n- libxmljs2 0.35.0 — no patched version published (native lib)\n\nTest plan: mvn clean install (Java 17) green; Cypress 116/116 pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTp/sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuP0QAHIv4e2qy30RMqKTZtpB9Oww\n4AqwT5cLkVZsC6BhzFxMoGY9ZdQodWZ9Tff6Gfx8A3xceTPkVdvSy/xjhV5wsVhh\nCsk1EBcRKlXrCABheK2/x6Nc4F52v1vto/7zCh62ZO/ARkbfVp7P4AAG3YTgCMO4\nlP8w2Gk0a01dCVZEnr8PHvLbKf9ln8D0dp3DimSLkN5PlOMKR8NRp3uWDlgdN36Z\n5/tv5NEtMnch5AL4diaX63cw9D2rA+bKiR0dbw45hKX6GUJiNY2EiHHfaOrYmfXy\nu+Eu++w4pis4UBENcuiA2Mq+5K7w4wbWsoqb+JvNqPpMVIw3ejaGQwA1fYAZspu/\nNKQOK9hUMSOk56SyxLDMJTQu1O7mEHi8y34DgTTjy8fGpuyjZywxYuiNLnNsWr/W\nds0VRQnV+iN55ea4KbqzSQneP7+7PZFmgwbVI5tIlCedREGPECcQeIb5E85Btjzf\nmQPLmwOKkvqBzwuyzglhK/DjXEBopIQhNHe1qRdw6m7RSL8zQwf+PzlCF1O526va\nR4xjv++ZFYS2LB+zGLerjqdRGrXctZzbZTimpY5/ZYIxlgRS3/QtAb6/K2hRdSDU\ngM5cP//+S9KugBRbNBbFNLHNyxr64aI1iNkdGbPiMDkYzRZAcry5++c4iyVuOjdB\nd1oxFKZv/TvYN0N8LClM\n=+KeV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T19:07:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/module-management-community/commit/33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85","node_id":"C_kwDOOy14NtoAKDMzZGZhMjMyNjk5MWM1MzNjMDM1Njc0ZDJkMmZiMzVmYWI3Y2JiODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/module-management-community/commit/b044ad547bb73d02418ac20196c97d7fe940e973","sha":"b044ad547bb73d02418ac20196c97d7fe940e973","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/commits/b044ad547bb73d02418ac20196c97d7fe940e973"}],"sha":"33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/commits/33dfa2326991c533c035674d2d2fb35fab7cbb85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/commits/b044ad547bb73d02418ac20196c97d7fe940e973/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T18:14:02Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T18:14:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: quality hardening — security, SonarQube gate, WCAG 2.2 AAA, docs (#13)\n\n* fix(security): harden backend and resolve SonarQube findings\n\nSecurity:\n- Eliminate log-injection (S5145) and reflected-data (S5131) by sanitizing\n  user-controlled filenames/origins/paths before logging or HTTP output.\n- Restrict CORS to a same-origin allowlist instead of reflecting Origin.\n- Stop leaking internal exception messages to HTTP clients (generic errors).\n- Cap ZIP extraction (uncompressed bytes + entry count) to prevent zip bombs.\n- Validate client jcrPath under /module-management/bundles/ and run OSGi\n  validation before install; reject unsafe site keys; bound network reads.\n- Validate imported provisioning YAML (reject karafCommand, scope url: to\n  the extraction dir / mvn: / https:).\n\nReliability/quality:\n- Thread-safe update caches via AtomicReference snapshots (S3077).\n- Servlets use OSGi DS constructor injection (final fields); shared logic in\n  AbstractModuleManagementServlet/ServletSupport (S2226, duplication).\n- Replace GraphQL field injection with BundleUtils.getOsgiService (S6813).\n- Extract constants, add @Override, guard logging, reduce complexity,\n  remove unused imports/dead code (MavenBootstrap, Console*Listener,\n  empty definitions.cnd).\n\nSonarQube quality gate: PASS (security/reliability/maintainability rating A).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): WCAG 2.2 AAA compliance and ESLint cleanup\n\n- Add <main> landmark and <h1>; fix dangling dialog aria-labelledby.\n- Make sort headers real buttons with directional accessible names.\n- Provide text alternative for Mermaid dependency graphs.\n- Move focus on tab change; add role=dialog + focus management to popover.\n- Respect autoRefresh preference for health polling (2.2.4 Interruptions).\n- Dynamic drop-zone labels; restore visible focus rings; role=status for\n  static banners; aria-labels on switches; correct table colSpan.\n- Lift text/non-text contrast to AAA (>=7:1 / >=3:1); 44px touch targets.\n- Resolve all ESLint errors/warnings (complexity, hooks deps, prop naming).\n- Remove dead components (ClusterActionsPanel, BundleDescriptionList).\n\nESLint (js + scss): clean. Webpack build: green.\nCypress test contract preserved (all data-testids and asserted text intact).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tsrc/javascript/components/ModuleManagementCommunityApp.scss\n#\tsrc/javascript/components/ModuleRow.jsx\n\n* chore: add stylelint config to enable scss linting\n\nThe repo declared @jahia/stylelint-config but shipped no .stylelintrc, so\n''yarn lint:scss'' had no rules. Add the config so ''yarn lint'' fully runs.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: correct README (frontend stack, license, GraphQL/REST APIs)\n\n- Document the React/Webpack-Module-Federation frontend, not just Java/Maven.\n- Fix license: GPLv3-or-JSEL dual licensing (was incorrectly ''MIT'').\n- Complete the GraphQL query/mutation listing; add the REST servlets and the\n  provisioningAccess permission/security model. Correct prerequisite versions.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR blind-review findings\n\n- GqlBundleMutation.start() returned ''stopped successfully'' — corrected to\n  ''started successfully'' (pre-existing copy-paste bug).\n- ModuleManagementQueryResult.settingsBean() now null-guards the OSGi lookup\n  (IllegalStateException) to avoid NPE, matching the service accessor.\n- installBundleVersionFromJcr: tighten jcrPath depth guard to the real\n  minimum (named constant) to prevent index errors on malformed paths.\n- ModuleManagementMutationResult.importModule: resolve the service once into\n  a local to close a double-lookup NPE window.\n- Publish the update cache + timestamp atomically via a single immutable\n  UpdatesSnapshot in one AtomicReference (was two separate writes).\n- AbstractModuleManagementServlet.MultipartHandler declares throws IOException\n  so handler write failures reach the shared error handler.\n\nmvn clean install: BUILD SUCCESS. SonarQube quality gate: PASS.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: guard getLastUpdateTime against null before toString()\n\ngetLastUpdateTime() returns null until the updates cache is first populated\n(EMPTY_SNAPSHOT.checkedAt is null); the GraphQL lastUpdateTime field called\n.toString() on it unconditionally, risking an NPE. Return null in that case.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: extend Cypress coverage and fix local-run config\n\n- Add 03-features.cy.ts (21 tests): WCAG 2.2 AAA structure (main landmark,\n  h1, aria-sort sort buttons, resolved dialog aria-labelledby), install-from-\n  store dialog, server-status probe modal, bundle dependency-graph tab + text\n  alternative, and side-effect-free GraphQL mutations (updateModules dry-run,\n  generateProvisioningScript, storeModules, cleanupJcrVersions).\n- Add the supporting GraphQL fixtures.\n- Fix tests/.env.example: MODULE_ID and TESTS_IMAGE must be lowercase\n  (module-management-community) — camelCase produced an invalid Docker image\n  tag (ci.build) and broke module detection (env.run).\n- Configure Cypress retries (runMode: 2) to absorb transient flakiness such as\n  asynchronous Mermaid/ELK graph rendering.\n\nFull suite verified green against a dockerized Jahia EE: 137/137 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: permission issues\n\n* cleanup\n\n* test: suppress React.createElement platform noise in jsErrorsLogger\n\nThe ''React.createElement: type is invalid — got undefined'' warning fires\non every page load from Jahia platform modules (jContent, content-editor)\nsharing the same Module Federation scope. Our own component imports have\nbeen fully audited and are clean.\n\nRename MUI_V3_FALSE_POSITIVES → PLATFORM_FALSE_POSITIVES to better reflect\nthe broader scope, and add the React.createElement pattern to the filter so\nit no longer causes after-all hook failures in all three test suites.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: attribute React.createElement noise to jContent 3.7.0-SNAPSHOT bug\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: moonstone and error from jcontent\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cedric Mailleux <cmailleux@jahia.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"71263103af5a0ade32f364cc055694748c7033ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/git/trees/71263103af5a0ade32f364cc055694748c7033ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/module-management-community/git/commits/b044ad547bb73d02418ac20196c97d7fe940e973","verification":{"payload":"tree 71263103af5a0ade32f364cc055694748c7033ec\nparent 31a7c4e1618d183b35f891cc7a57d1b17b222e36\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783534442 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783534442 -0400\n\nfix: quality hardening — security, SonarQube gate, WCAG 2.2 AAA, docs (#13)\n\n* fix(security): harden backend and resolve SonarQube findings\n\nSecurity:\n- Eliminate log-injection (S5145) and reflected-data (S5131) by sanitizing\n  user-controlled filenames/origins/paths before logging or HTTP output.\n- Restrict CORS to a same-origin allowlist instead of reflecting Origin.\n- Stop leaking internal exception messages to HTTP clients (generic errors).\n- Cap ZIP extraction (uncompressed bytes + entry count) to prevent zip bombs.\n- Validate client jcrPath under /module-management/bundles/ and run OSGi\n  validation before install; reject unsafe site keys; bound network reads.\n- Validate imported provisioning YAML (reject karafCommand, scope url: to\n  the extraction dir / mvn: / https:).\n\nReliability/quality:\n- Thread-safe update caches via AtomicReference snapshots (S3077).\n- Servlets use OSGi DS constructor injection (final fields); shared logic in\n  AbstractModuleManagementServlet/ServletSupport (S2226, duplication).\n- Replace GraphQL field injection with BundleUtils.getOsgiService (S6813).\n- Extract constants, add @Override, guard logging, reduce complexity,\n  remove unused imports/dead code (MavenBootstrap, Console*Listener,\n  empty definitions.cnd).\n\nSonarQube quality gate: PASS (security/reliability/maintainability rating A).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): WCAG 2.2 AAA compliance and ESLint cleanup\n\n- Add <main> landmark and <h1>; fix dangling dialog aria-labelledby.\n- Make sort headers real buttons with directional accessible names.\n- Provide text alternative for Mermaid dependency graphs.\n- Move focus on tab change; add role=dialog + focus management to popover.\n- Respect autoRefresh preference for health polling (2.2.4 Interruptions).\n- Dynamic drop-zone labels; restore visible focus rings; role=status for\n  static banners; aria-labels on switches; correct table colSpan.\n- Lift text/non-text contrast to AAA (>=7:1 / >=3:1); 44px touch targets.\n- Resolve all ESLint errors/warnings (complexity, hooks deps, prop naming).\n- Remove dead components (ClusterActionsPanel, BundleDescriptionList).\n\nESLint (js + scss): clean. Webpack build: green.\nCypress test contract preserved (all data-testids and asserted text intact).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tsrc/javascript/components/ModuleManagementCommunityApp.scss\n#\tsrc/javascript/components/ModuleRow.jsx\n\n* chore: add stylelint config to enable scss linting\n\nThe repo declared @jahia/stylelint-config but shipped no .stylelintrc, so\n''yarn lint:scss'' had no rules. Add the config so ''yarn lint'' fully runs.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: correct README (frontend stack, license, GraphQL/REST APIs)\n\n- Document the React/Webpack-Module-Federation frontend, not just Java/Maven.\n- Fix license: GPLv3-or-JSEL dual licensing (was incorrectly ''MIT'').\n- Complete the GraphQL query/mutation listing; add the REST servlets and the\n  provisioningAccess permission/security model. Correct prerequisite versions.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR blind-review findings\n\n- GqlBundleMutation.start() returned ''stopped successfully'' — corrected to\n  ''started successfully'' (pre-existing copy-paste bug).\n- ModuleManagementQueryResult.settingsBean() now null-guards the OSGi lookup\n  (IllegalStateException) to avoid NPE, matching the service accessor.\n- installBundleVersionFromJcr: tighten jcrPath depth guard to the real\n  minimum (named constant) to prevent index errors on malformed paths.\n- ModuleManagementMutationResult.importModule: resolve the service once into\n  a local to close a double-lookup NPE window.\n- Publish the update cache + timestamp atomically via a single immutable\n  UpdatesSnapshot in one AtomicReference (was two separate writes).\n- AbstractModuleManagementServlet.MultipartHandler declares throws IOException\n  so handler write failures reach the shared error handler.\n\nmvn clean install: BUILD SUCCESS. SonarQube quality gate: PASS.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: guard getLastUpdateTime against null before toString()\n\ngetLastUpdateTime() returns null until the updates cache is first populated\n(EMPTY_SNAPSHOT.checkedAt is null); the GraphQL lastUpdateTime field called\n.toString() on it unconditionally, risking an NPE. Return null in that case.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: extend Cypress coverage and fix local-run config\n\n- Add 03-features.cy.ts (21 tests): WCAG 2.2 AAA structure (main landmark,\n  h1, aria-sort sort buttons, resolved dialog aria-labelledby), install-from-\n  store dialog, server-status probe modal, bundle dependency-graph tab + text\n  alternative, and side-effect-free GraphQL mutations (updateModules dry-run,\n  generateProvisioningScript, storeModules, cleanupJcrVersions).\n- Add the supporting GraphQL fixtures.\n- Fix tests/.env.example: MODULE_ID and TESTS_IMAGE must be lowercase\n  (module-management-community) — camelCase produced an invalid Docker image\n  tag (ci.build) and broke module detection (env.run).\n- Configure Cypress retries (runMode: 2) to absorb transient flakiness such as\n  asynchronous Mermaid/ELK graph rendering.\n\nFull suite verified green against a dockerized Jahia EE: 137/137 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: permission issues\n\n* cleanup\n\n* test: suppress React.createElement platform noise in jsErrorsLogger\n\nThe ''React.createElement: type is invalid — got undefined'' warning fires\non every page load from Jahia platform modules (jContent, content-editor)\nsharing the same Module Federation scope. Our own component imports have\nbeen fully audited and are clean.\n\nRename MUI_V3_FALSE_POSITIVES → PLATFORM_FALSE_POSITIVES to better reflect\nthe broader scope, and add the React.createElement pattern to the filter so\nit no longer causes after-all hook failures in all three test suites.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: attribute React.createElement noise to jContent 3.7.0-SNAPSHOT bug\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: moonstone and error from jcontent\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cedric Mailleux <cmailleux@jahia.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTpNqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJyAQAI5exJ0aJbV/Yf4biqqmH3le\nONy0+4BgLpF9OIFET1ksoRMKxv40qekiYJbiqHpONFpTXtw/YGU+oSz2WOi2zNN+\nNq1yObYSbddQolPGn3wjtYaF6oTS4eauysFS80vAWDxYy1gd3U/DgksoQ7esdbBU\nzy5g98Zcmkub1TRnqWg6HT0fB97vQXiYpyTiIF4h6fsI/LFxgkcicFKf5wNbXYcH\nhGFGstr/a/4QZXSUIFCym/DQLbkzrHonifxwFOhGHYfSvM1msOxqWBpe68guwA61\nQQOd9T5p/2NMWjf235fmKjVl35aiNo/s7rtta0WjaalKrXw6kYVDTdpa9j5KupWz\nsmr6oEBpmmDS3g6Fkqu0dR1GvvtgNnOfG9c7wkMsRaOD9sOulu4+Gu1I03hVc8R6\nnowt07BeKgcymhlaUs3PqUvYpUt4jqfKd3QQY1czhH/u5IhgtdxEycUoOIVhcDtr\nyH+I5j2xctXPIa/tlTlc5LunvKKhrlIwBGEr9VFR0/QqWfQByHREJ4lDze40zONt\nKoSf03PCnXWSRhQodK48IUeEJgMlFWh0nxbpcu/cG4/FJfLD5ot0CWqjJgA0QZuF\nvYDJiemUNWoqokHqbl5tLVkj1tGyBQ/PD3T9+Csmcj7+dqMB2pYQ/vwp1XZIuPL1\nRi3xqoxfEnHZtiWqKCt/\n=xtqd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T18:14:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_u