"4e2beff60e7c76a69b25ece62f7905af9d5092de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/4e2beff60e7c76a69b25ece62f7905af9d5092de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/9cbc8ad28334e7f42688844d162282be05c0e716/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:24:08Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:24:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(release): identify credential health preflight HTTP client (#1393)\n\nProduction FuzeKeys is healthy and advertises google-shared-v1, but the\ndefault Python urllib user-agent receives HTTP 403. Identify the release\nprobe as FuzeFront-release-preflight/1.0 so the exact health endpoint is\nreachable. All health, PostgreSQL and protocol validation remains\nenforced.\n\nValidation: four preflight tests passed; the patched probe passed\nagainst real production; uploaded Git blob hashes verified against local\nfiles.","tree":{"sha":"4a488e0565848c902391b6c07ef6af4aa6276b06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/4a488e0565848c902391b6c07ef6af4aa6276b06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/9cbc8ad28334e7f42688844d162282be05c0e716","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a488e0565848c902391b6c07ef6af4aa6276b06\nparent 042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791401048 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791401048 +0300\n\nfix(release): identify credential health preflight HTTP client (#1393)\n\nProduction FuzeKeys is healthy and advertises google-shared-v1, but the\ndefault Python urllib user-agent receives HTTP 403. Identify the release\nprobe as FuzeFront-release-preflight/1.0 so the exact health endpoint is\nreachable. All health, PostgreSQL and protocol validation remains\nenforced.\n\nValidation: four preflight tests passed; the patched probe passed\nagainst real production; uploaded Git blob hashes verified against local\nfiles.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxpxYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXvsQAHweJr5Zr7n7MVsKgJe2lREO\nrw+LmIFrrKrAh5KXnQR6dPbvWwafhTpoUXsgzeWhn2NM6CbO0sVtrLYdfU3qLBXn\nf70iqVu2jz9htiwtmBqzMYr/rozWgQe11p0j5NJTL0lp/YCdhBmCczWZsvXvB8Nx\nYbaaRoKOkpysSsC9huP15BTPAULzLVG6CqO8Kb6sw/4/yxbQKEW/T3eBpl3L5iqX\nZsDcD9ZMIdWxOsVyUAz+gz51Y83iQdGGXHUCG+jYTw8/JjZEYkgUkQnP4yAimC2k\nCavCbjuezifk9bgaN2evKlEbC3fhWmu1vW0tKvOvEciSsT5lHlrgWdFdv8Nnjz10\nZcduGzO58uKdEUT0X57ZD5X9CD1kHW4g1tFsWkGb2X9ifKzDDfYoeFqPv1TrMYA/\nPODB0GCP0Zk0YNT36PCNcFE/F/ynKouuP70xpfxOjpOlE+5ifPEu8WUhLiXGHd9x\nKsXHIBG0kYvq6Ft75eqbm93XcJpTbdYzc02/Nxsem2F6MwaeHQkYyLnzjfNzKud1\nMcGn2V3Vsvd8X8UnjjMGOJrtjrQnE5vD2ttxx7dVvFix9DYB12zq9P+ZASCLjxzY\n2lvuqmUI3jLOkcTxelST3CkwVa+WF/0HWuHzD0ihryaSGIyycGmQv4o4nbmyiKk4\nun20wbhgmmhhwGdjtYC0\n=/zbD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:24:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/9cbc8ad28334e7f42688844d162282be05c0e716","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDljYmM4YWQyODMzNGU3ZjQyNjg4ODQ0ZDE2MjI4MmJlMDVjMGU3MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5","sha":"042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5"}],"sha":"9cbc8ad28334e7f42688844d162282be05c0e716","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/9cbc8ad28334e7f42688844d162282be05c0e716"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:09:32Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:09:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(connectors): render catalog immediately and verify production UX (#1392)\n\nThe production connector page still runs image d89b32610185 and shows\nonly Gmail. This change renders generic catalog cards as soon as the\ncatalog resolves, loads Gmail and provider statuses independently,\nbounds requests with abort timeouts, and offers a read-only retry\nwithout reporting failed status requests as disconnected. Older\nresponses cannot overwrite a later retry.\n\nThe live post-production Playwright journey requires Gmail plus all 25\nimplemented generic providers, checks each status route and UI controls,\nand exports screenshots, video and a safe inventory. The first live run\nfailed on the old Gmail-only page; no successful production rollout is\nclaimed.\n\nFuzeFront''s custom review caller now forwards CODEX_AUTH_JSON and treats\nthat secret as sufficient readiness, using the existing published\nFuzeSDLC isolated no-tools subscription reviewer. OpenAI/Gemini API\ncoding keys remain absent, checkout credentials remain unpersisted,\nnamed bot restrictions and sensitive-path review protections remain\nenabled. No secret values are changed by this PR.\n\nFresh CI exposed a race between two real Postgres event integration\nsuites, both deleting the same event_outbox table. Each now owns a\nprivate schema while retaining real Postgres/Kafka assertions and\nparallel execution.\n\nValidation:\n- Frontend Lint & Test job 112932456164 passed: 46 test files / 278\ntests, including five recovery regressions and two authorization-pending\ntests.\n- Local strict frontend and core-test type checks passed.\n- Eight read-only reviewer safety tests passed; Codex-only readiness and\nsecret passthrough verified.\n- Git blob hashes and exact uploaded source content verified.\n- Fresh CI for head 56df4e8dc8a4da7b62df12eeb8c920f590763bd1 is running;\nreal event integration results are pending.\n- The shared reviewer Ruff corrections remain in FuzeSDLC #481; consumer\nrefresh must follow ordinary review, merge and publication.\n\nProduction diagnostics on October 7: Front backend/frontend remain\nd89b32610185. Argo''s Front synchronization failed at\nbilling-s2s-register (PreSyncFailed / Job BackoffLimitExceeded); its\nexpired pod logs are unavailable, so the underlying hook error is\nunverified. FuzeKeys backend/frontend run 0.1.18 with ready replicas;\npublic GET protocol health remains unverified. Deployment and successful\npost-production evidence remain prerequisites for the next connector\nbatch.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"585f36f27104bc70537c74bb3df3fa08983e07d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/585f36f27104bc70537c74bb3df3fa08983e07d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5","verification":{"payload":"tree 585f36f27104bc70537c74bb3df3fa08983e07d8\nparent fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791400172 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791400172 +0300\n\nfix(connectors): render catalog immediately and verify production UX (#1392)\n\nThe production connector page still runs image d89b32610185 and shows\nonly Gmail. This change renders generic catalog cards as soon as the\ncatalog resolves, loads Gmail and provider statuses independently,\nbounds requests with abort timeouts, and offers a read-only retry\nwithout reporting failed status requests as disconnected. Older\nresponses cannot overwrite a later retry.\n\nThe live post-production Playwright journey requires Gmail plus all 25\nimplemented generic providers, checks each status route and UI controls,\nand exports screenshots, video and a safe inventory. The first live run\nfailed on the old Gmail-only page; no successful production rollout is\nclaimed.\n\nFuzeFront''s custom review caller now forwards CODEX_AUTH_JSON and treats\nthat secret as sufficient readiness, using the existing published\nFuzeSDLC isolated no-tools subscription reviewer. OpenAI/Gemini API\ncoding keys remain absent, checkout credentials remain unpersisted,\nnamed bot restrictions and sensitive-path review protections remain\nenabled. No secret values are changed by this PR.\n\nFresh CI exposed a race between two real Postgres event integration\nsuites, both deleting the same event_outbox table. Each now owns a\nprivate schema while retaining real Postgres/Kafka assertions and\nparallel execution.\n\nValidation:\n- Frontend Lint & Test job 112932456164 passed: 46 test files / 278\ntests, including five recovery regressions and two authorization-pending\ntests.\n- Local strict frontend and core-test type checks passed.\n- Eight read-only reviewer safety tests passed; Codex-only readiness and\nsecret passthrough verified.\n- Git blob hashes and exact uploaded source content verified.\n- Fresh CI for head 56df4e8dc8a4da7b62df12eeb8c920f590763bd1 is running;\nreal event integration results are pending.\n- The shared reviewer Ruff corrections remain in FuzeSDLC #481; consumer\nrefresh must follow ordinary review, merge and publication.\n\nProduction diagnostics on October 7: Front backend/frontend remain\nd89b32610185. Argo''s Front synchronization failed at\nbilling-s2s-register (PreSyncFailed / Job BackoffLimitExceeded); its\nexpired pod logs are unavailable, so the underlying hook error is\nunverified. FuzeKeys backend/frontend run 0.1.18 with ready replicas;\npublic GET protocol health remains unverified. Deployment and successful\npost-production evidence remain prerequisites for the next connector\nbatch.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxpjsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACn0QAAzARUeo6pBd1hE1lE+VqqI/\nG+xTm8CWy9SEHYYFks8RFgriir9/HjR4FhjutXEie7oGmtCcmrfkBOHFrNI49VBd\nlG60lZkRHpxcu2WF/9+ltTQfNgUlZ39newpqdypyleDGs3jIVijaKx4d06X7IqyV\n4ESRPpmWKwZSwFkn2cjjrLvm3seCI3yFN9o4PhZN0YZVKwYxmJR/8PyHIoqnMdo0\n5tP92DfHQEJx5itGfYKPBC4+na8I2ji6SXqPIXd9CDJ7IP4XUcgQbnR1iwPhqWIo\nybh3au8sSfeT9lrYG2vxaWRSSvfseMMFq+KdQLQLcu7q/j99W4lPJQpFZtyEt7So\nTW+FyDasdP7mbnd15qFbBYB97NmgRrH3oQuBi6rFvL/7SvXtiW6xwHq2aHjSTs8Z\nSa79T+pM/vG1jij+pruMvQQPb9vNTQ6GqG34VeeEmZCo8zDssXbBgIRPeFfdLuxR\nrz4JHjjW+rBi5Xvk7UWz1DI6j5Txs3ngX1hVT0d4Zel2CYdxLMqAFk/h/E/Y58Cp\nFlh9eXdr/eqruEDFVaYqNeGMdnyfYi1XFDy6bDPhxuV/rxv3CeDE0sgAb5n8OSKb\n8/+BNradl+dP0f43MQoXE7WdmXoWSnhVEuGBH/NYaydCMqP5j4fx2TyUPdc7qMQy\nXpYPSu31X8VDQkofZvj5\n=XL4i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:09:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDA0MmVlMDNiN2YyZDYwMTA1NjliNDYzNTQ4ODg5ZGYwMzBmNmJlYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17","sha":"fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17"}],"sha":"042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/042ee03b7f2d6010569b463548889df030f6beb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:09:23Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:09:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(release): require checked GitOps PRs without deploy-key bypass (#1391)\n\n## Release safety fix\n\nThe current release workflow writes image-tag updates directly to master\nwith RELEASE_BUMP_SSH_KEY and a DeployKey ruleset bypass. This PR\nremoves that path. No release is claimed from this PR.\n\n- Use the existing fuze-agent App installation identity to publish a\nnon-forced release branch whose PR runs normal CI. Mint the token after\nimage builds.\n- Open/reuse an exact single-file GitOps PR, request ordinary auto-merge\nwith an expected head SHA, and wait for actual MERGED state. No --admin,\nsynthetic owner approval, direct default-branch push or [skip ci].\n- Fail closed on divergent branch contents, unexpected files,\ntransport/push failure, closed PR, changed source/head or pending review\ntimeout. Disable late auto-merge when the source changes or the wait\nends.\n- Guard tag-only merges for both push and workflow_dispatch to avoid the\nauto-merge dispatch recursion. Preserve image build-success/tag rewrite\nguards and the deployed FuzeKeys protocol prerequisite.\n- Dispatch post-deploy verification only after confirmed merge or exact\nno-op. GitOps merge remains distinct from actual deployment/smoke\nsuccess.\n- Reuse the canonical FuzeSDLC v1 verdict reader and tests verbatim\n(blobs 2172983e5b7bcac2e7d6cc6901fccf0cf4b39cd8 and\n844415b0059fe0e620d18431676fdd95bc57d3ef), fixing the result_text_b64\ntransport mismatch without changing central reviewer policy.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Python script suite: 395 tests run; 394 passed, one pre-existing skip.\nIncludes 11 new executable release publication tests and 67 shared\nverdict tests.\n- Node deployable-path suite: 20 passed; generated trigger paths\nvalidated.\n- All 92 workflow YAML files parsed, bash -n passed and git diff --check\npassed.\n- All six uploaded Git blobs were re-fetched byte-for-byte; remote tree\n0b809048dc3776e0ff3e344c0f95f01c1ca9f1dc exactly matches the tested\nlocal tree, based on current master\n3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40.\n\n## Remaining prerequisites\n\nOrdinary repository checks and independent sensitive-workflow approval\nremain required. FuzeKeys #210 still needs ordinary review/check\ncompletion for the non-destructive Vault immutable-template fix. After\nboth land, verify actual FuzeKeys credential protocol, release Front,\nand validate production connector catalog/connection smoke before\nlaunching the next batch. No credentials were copied or printed, and no\nproduction deployment or marketplace publication is asserted.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e20d97373c6478217618b52c9425d3e78955c224","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/e20d97373c6478217618b52c9425d3e78955c224"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17","verification":{"payload":"tree e20d97373c6478217618b52c9425d3e78955c224\nparent 3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791400163 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791400163 +0300\n\nfix(release): require checked GitOps PRs without deploy-key bypass (#1391)\n\n## Release safety fix\n\nThe current release workflow writes image-tag updates directly to master\nwith RELEASE_BUMP_SSH_KEY and a DeployKey ruleset bypass. This PR\nremoves that path. No release is claimed from this PR.\n\n- Use the existing fuze-agent App installation identity to publish a\nnon-forced release branch whose PR runs normal CI. Mint the token after\nimage builds.\n- Open/reuse an exact single-file GitOps PR, request ordinary auto-merge\nwith an expected head SHA, and wait for actual MERGED state. No --admin,\nsynthetic owner approval, direct default-branch push or [skip ci].\n- Fail closed on divergent branch contents, unexpected files,\ntransport/push failure, closed PR, changed source/head or pending review\ntimeout. Disable late auto-merge when the source changes or the wait\nends.\n- Guard tag-only merges for both push and workflow_dispatch to avoid the\nauto-merge dispatch recursion. Preserve image build-success/tag rewrite\nguards and the deployed FuzeKeys protocol prerequisite.\n- Dispatch post-deploy verification only after confirmed merge or exact\nno-op. GitOps merge remains distinct from actual deployment/smoke\nsuccess.\n- Reuse the canonical FuzeSDLC v1 verdict reader and tests verbatim\n(blobs 2172983e5b7bcac2e7d6cc6901fccf0cf4b39cd8 and\n844415b0059fe0e620d18431676fdd95bc57d3ef), fixing the result_text_b64\ntransport mismatch without changing central reviewer policy.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Python script suite: 395 tests run; 394 passed, one pre-existing skip.\nIncludes 11 new executable release publication tests and 67 shared\nverdict tests.\n- Node deployable-path suite: 20 passed; generated trigger paths\nvalidated.\n- All 92 workflow YAML files parsed, bash -n passed and git diff --check\npassed.\n- All six uploaded Git blobs were re-fetched byte-for-byte; remote tree\n0b809048dc3776e0ff3e344c0f95f01c1ca9f1dc exactly matches the tested\nlocal tree, based on current master\n3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40.\n\n## Remaining prerequisites\n\nOrdinary repository checks and independent sensitive-workflow approval\nremain required. FuzeKeys #210 still needs ordinary review/check\ncompletion for the non-destructive Vault immutable-template fix. After\nboth land, verify actual FuzeKeys credential protocol, release Front,\nand validate production connector catalog/connection smoke before\nlaunching the next batch. No credentials were copied or printed, and no\nproduction deployment or marketplace publication is asserted.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxpjjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAykAQAEs07QhJvhSWkStfZd6Q20cR\ndMCuhzT5m9+2jTKDTheRBLq3P5/jFiwV6dA9vXp4mLG/r2bAkHVPRwDRJcNVMv4h\naI9aOInsVchLMcqh9qX/W4KUMixjCYWADJ1alnxQi8QyuPeVVsSZ77YRFchV6kho\na5OI5wlZJ+KCfm1QmGnqt3ytXITaatB5Bj6wXDgZe404yJar+yWZPhmGpBlrFBD3\nSPLxcvoo5gWLo7jXtkNpvqN0S0Z5kJF0xieR4XrI1bo2hYY0PDabPm4n2qC4MsM/\nsaEkqYPpcpssbhpgTzDr5TrGdY2Oly4aJetNpZpydZjH5DGP4IRMxPDSpjTonzss\nhT7cQZGHP+nejZ0HM7waLPxsxUV2obFeUg4gmdVUWnpPSS+F1drPHgMLnZZMIWxz\naUDWXXvg2j+eEsbMlfsTjEjomGhLRvoz+cw/slSG4GGOAne8cPQ8O8W90V8JKHvh\nP0HglXJOu+arpRWR6vc0gbD8cIKox80P2PE1j5uefVTJ7mTtDdiWRKPoUMZ7ixhw\nAUnjHTAlSQMJTNsJVCxSMCIQgEazWLEgc/5qRu/VXgo5cZehlsFzkgk82tGlXtEn\n4xBWui4zsDesHXzO8/Q+rqG09xSqXc/To7RKWmyH4i/TTudic3/kQY0VCR5SdMhP\nzoIu+E8ZyDMoHv/I3CSz\n=0tUb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:09:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKGZlMDM3Y2QyYWJlY2FjYmUzYTM0YjM5N2EwZTAyNWVlN2ExYWZhMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40","sha":"3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40"}],"sha":"fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/fe037cd2abecacbe3a34b397a0e025ee7a1afa17"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:47:31Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:47:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gitops): retire cluster-scoped workload RBAC, unfreeze Argo sync (closes #1137) (#1380)\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #1137. The symptom (\"applications-service migrations 013/014 not\ntaking effect in prod\") was never a migration-runner bug —\n`runMigrations()` already runs correctly before `httpServer.listen()` on\nevery boot (`backend/applications/src/index.ts`). The actual cause is\nthat **no new `applications-service` pod — or any other FuzeFront pod —\nhas been created since ~2026-09-30/10-02**, because the `fuzefront` Argo\nApplication''s sync has been failing outright.\n\nThis chart rendered a cluster-scoped `ClusterRole`/`ClusterRoleBinding`\n(`fuzefront-workload-authenticator`, for the security service''s\nTokenReview calls), while the `fuzefront` AppProject''s\n`clusterResourceWhitelist` only ever permitted `Namespace`. Argo does\nnot skip an unpermitted resource in a sync — it invalidates the whole\nsync task and **aborts every other resource in the Application along\nwith it**, including plain image-tag bumps. That froze every FuzeFront\nrollout, so migrations 013/014 (and everything merged since) never ran\nanywhere — not because they''re broken, but because the pods that would\nrun them were never created.\n\nConfirmed against today''s CI: the `Portal federation health` census (run\n37276037910, 2026-10-05 07:08Z) reported\n`DEPLOY DRIFT: values-prod.yaml requests applications-service image\ncb3b372f527a, but the pod answering /api/v1/app-registry reports build\n2f5edffb80f4` — a pod from **2026-09-30**, five days stale.\n\n## FuzeInfra has already landed its half (izzywdev/FuzeInfra, verified\non `main`)\n\n- **FuzeInfra#1306** (merged 2026-10-04) adopted the same-named\n`ClusterRole`/`ClusterRoleBinding` into FuzeInfra''s own prod chart\n(`helm/fuzeinfra/values-contabo.yaml`) and narrowed them to\n`tokenreviews: create` only. The live grant in prod is unchanged — only\nownership moved off this chart.\n- **FuzeInfra#1308** (merged 2026-10-04) deleted FuzeInfra''s stale\nduplicate copy of the `fuzefront` AppProject — the other, independent\ncause of the same symptom (two repos racing to write the same object,\nlast-write-wins) — and now **gates registration**\n(`validate_consumer_appproject.py`, rule R3) so a ClusterRole-permitting\n`fuzefront` AppProject can never be re-applied.\n\nBoth commits say explicitly that they \"alone do not unblock FuzeFront\"\nand name the matching FuzeFront-side patch as the other half. **This PR\nis that patch.**\n\n## This change (FuzeFront side)\n\n- `deploy/helm/fuzefront/values.yaml` —\n`securityService.workloadIdentity.clusterRbac.enabled` now defaults to\n`false`, so the chart stops rendering the\n`ClusterRole`/`ClusterRoleBinding` anywhere. Local kind (plain `helm\nupgrade --install`, no Argo involved) can still override with `--set\nsecurityService.workloadIdentity.clusterRbac.enabled=true` to exercise\n`POST /api/v1/security/tokens/workload` locally — FuzeInfra''s adoption\nis prod-only.\n- `deploy/argocd/project.yaml` — `clusterResourceWhitelist` narrowed\nback to `Namespace`-only, matching what FuzeInfra''s registration gate\nnow requires unconditionally. Header comment rewritten from \"armed\nre-freeze, pending FuzeInfra action\" to the resolved state, with the\nfull chain of issues for anyone reconstructing this later.\n- `deploy/helm/fuzefront/templates/workload-identity.yaml` — doc\ncomments updated to describe the retired state rather than the pending\none.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nhelm lint deploy/helm/fuzefront -f values-local.yaml   # clean\nhelm lint deploy/helm/fuzefront -f values-prod.yaml    # clean\n\nhelm template ... (same --set flags helm-validate.yml uses, every optional workload on)\n  values-local.yaml -> renders cleanly, 0 occurrences of ClusterRole/ClusterRoleBinding\n  values-prod.yaml  -> renders cleanly, 0 occurrences of ClusterRole/ClusterRoleBinding\n\nkubeconform -strict -kubernetes-version 1.29.0 (skip CRD/Middleware/SealedSecret, same as CI)\n  values-local.yaml: 50/51 valid, 0 invalid, 0 errors\n  values-prod.yaml:  86/91 valid, 0 invalid, 0 errors\n\ndeploy/scripts/check-cluster-scoped-whitelist.sh --self-test\n  8/8 cases pass, including proving the probe still FAILS on the original\n  ClusterRole-vs-Namespace-only regression — the guard itself is not weakened.\n\ndeploy/scripts/check-cluster-scoped-whitelist.sh against both rendered overlays\n  \"the chart''s cluster-scoped kinds and the AppProject whitelist agree exactly\"\n  for BOTH values-local.yaml and values-prod.yaml.\n```\n\n## What is NOT in this PR (already done upstream, not FuzeFront''s to do)\n\nFuzeInfra#1306 and FuzeInfra#1308 are prerequisites this PR assumes are\nlive — they''re merged to `izzywdev/FuzeInfra` `main` already, verified\nby reading that repo directly (no FuzeInfra files edited from here). If\na future portal-federation-health census still shows deploy drift after\nthis merges and Argo syncs, the next thing to check is whether\nFuzeInfra''s ClusterRole adoption actually reached the **live cluster**\n(not just its repo) — that''s a `cluster-query` read-only check, not a\nFuzeFront code change.\n\n## Issue done-criteria from #1137\n\n- [x] Root cause found, with evidence (today''s census DEPLOY DRIFT\nannotation + FuzeInfra#1306/#1308 commit history)\n- [ ] `clock` loads / `fuzesales`/`fuzeservice` duplicates suspended /\ncensus rows green — gated on this merging, Argo actually syncing, and\nmigrations 013/014 finally executing on a pod that stays up. Cannot be\nconfirmed from this repo alone (no cluster access); next census run\nafter this deploys will show it.\n- [x] Serving + unregistered failures (fuzehub, fuzeagent, picker,\ncontact, call, fuzex, fuzemerchandize, plan) — already routed to their\nowning repos in earlier comments on #1137, unchanged by this PR.\n- [ ] Census failure escalation decision — still an open ask from the\nissue, not addressed here (orthogonal to the root-cause fix, and a prior\nsession already flagged it as needing an owner decision before\nbuilding).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_013tMciHkPE8To7V67CsgKKc\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_013tMciHkPE8To7V67CsgKKc)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"160a04cece7b92aac98eec6a57689762831dea49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/160a04cece7b92aac98eec6a57689762831dea49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/3f165af29000293c755f8f903e3bc7303eecaa40","verification":{"payload":"tree 160a04cece7b92aac98eec6a57689762831dea49\nparent fc381ea53a164278a94576f91558616e8318fc8b\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791370051 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791370051 +0300\n\nfix(gitops): retire cluster-scoped workload RBAC, unfreeze Argo sync (closes #1137) (#1380)\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #1137. The symptom (\"applications-service migrations 013/014 not\ntaking effect in prod\") was never a migration-runner bug —\n`runMigrations()` already runs correctly before `httpServer.listen()` on\nevery boot (`backend/applications/src/index.ts`). The actual cause is\nthat **no new `applications-service` pod — or any other FuzeFront pod —\nhas been created since ~2026-09-30/10-02**, because the `fuzefront` Argo\nApplication''s sync has been failing outright.\n\nThis chart rendered a cluster-scoped `ClusterRole`/`ClusterRoleBinding`\n(`fuzefront-workload-authenticator`, for the security service''s\nTokenReview calls), while the `fuzefront` AppProject''s\n`clusterResourceWhitelist` only ever permitted `Namespace`. Argo does\nnot skip an unpermitted resource in a sync — it invalidates the whole\nsync task and **aborts every other resource in the Application along\nwith it**, including plain image-tag bumps. That froze every FuzeFront\nrollout, so migra