ate":"2026-10-06T19:43:14Z","email":"release-bump@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuzefront-release"},"message":"release: fuzefront images d89b32610185 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"21acbcc76dfc68aa67e94631b4f479b427c63415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/21acbcc76dfc68aa67e94631b4f479b427c63415"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/fc381ea53a164278a94576f91558616e8318fc8b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/fc381ea53a164278a94576f91558616e8318fc8b","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKGZjMzgxZWE1M2ExNjQyNzhhOTQ1NzZmOTE1NTg2MTZlODMxOGZjOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33","sha":"c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33"}],"sha":"fc381ea53a164278a94576f91558616e8318fc8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/fc381ea53a164278a94576f91558616e8318fc8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:23:24Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:23:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Connector platform: first two waves and API key providers (#1203)\n\nImplements the first two ten-provider connector waves, retaining Gmail,\nplus API-key read integrations for OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Vercel and\nLovable. Base44 and Replit remain pending transport work. The shared\nruntime handles OAuth state/nonce protection, delegated workload\nauthentication and FuzeKeys credential custody. The roadmap lists all 57\nplanned connectors with implemented entries marked ✅. Publisher review\npackets are prepared; no provider listing was published.\n\nMerged current master with an exact verified tree, preserving catalog\nauthorization, transactional quotas and newer access/JWT fixes. Pinned\nthe shared TypeScript compiler to 5.9.3, patched\nAxios/Nodemailer/Morgan/fast-uri, and made Docker workspace installs use\ncomplete manifests and committed lockfiles. Added scoped selection-list\ngrants and projected workload owner bootstrap, active account token\ninjection, asynchronous flag handling, and the published selection UI\nversion bump. Focused Security tests (140), selection-service tests (486\nplus five DB skips), builds/typechecks and identifier checks pass\nlocally; current CI remains authoritative.\n\nEight Google connectors now share one verified account/client credential\nthrough FuzeKeys, while their metadata/configuration remain independent.\nGmail refresh uses configured OAuth credentials and verifies\nidentity/scope continuity. Existing unbound connections require the\ndocumented upgrade/reauthorization; account conflicts are not silently\ncombined. See docs/connectors/google-account-upgrade.md.\n\nRelease order: FuzeFront Security bootstrap #1389 and verified\nresource-organization policy/instance grant provisioning must precede\nFuzeKeys #205/#206, followed by this connector Front release. FuzeKeys\nmust expose verified protocol health before this release. The release\nworkflow now checks its public health, connected PostgreSQL and\ngoogle-shared-v1 protocol before publishing any images or bumping GitOps\ntags. State-key ciphertext is merged separately in #1210; cluster\napplication has not been verified. OAuth clients/callbacks, migration\n028 and live account reads/refresh still require verification. Do not\nequate merge with live provider connectivity.\n\nAdds optional trusted tenant proof to GET /security/session: canonical\nIDs, active SQL membership and active organization are required; the\nexisting response without the query is unchanged. FuzeKeys account\nlinking depends on this endpoint. 133 proof/session tests pass.\nAdditional focused validation passes: 240 identity UI tests, 151\nsecurity/OIDC tests, 15 billing acceptance tests and 44 merged access\ntests; clean installs, declaration builds and email build/tests pass.\nPostgreSQL integration and fresh CI remain required.\n\nPublisher readiness now separates metadata packets from evidence for\nprovider checks. Slack''s native app/adoption requirements, Google\nMarketplace setup and Atlassian Forge readiness are documented; no\npublication or eligibility is claimed.\n\nLatest organization/approval compatibility: initial exchanges supply the\nexplicit server FUZE_CONNECTOR_AUTHZ_TENANT or shared-router\nresourceTenant option. No default resource organization exists; Security\nverifies active SQL membership. Directory tid, email and\nrequest-selected organization are not proof. Both shared-provider and\nGmail transports treat Keys HTTP 202 authorization_pending as awaiting\napproval, never connected. OAuth callbacks redirect with the pending\nstatus; API-key UI clears the input and asks the user to contact their\nadministrator and connect again. Only Keys HTTP 200 updated confirms\ncredential storage. Secrets are not cached for pending retry.\n\nLatest focused validation: 8 resource-organization configuration tests,\n7 fail-closed credential-outcome cases and 2 rendered React\npending-approval regressions pass. Shared TypeScript delegation SDK\nforwarding tests pass (the identical source passed its 38-test SDK\nsuite). Modified routes/UI pass syntax transpilation; full\nbackend/frontend tests/typechecks were not rerun for these latest\nchanges. service-auth 0.1.4, backend pin and two root-lock entries\nalign; Security-client 0.9.x development dependency stays unchanged\nuntil #1389 merges and its 0.10.0 package is available. Fresh head CI\nremains required. Current source head\naeda9fa3dbe4e69d826d4f0d07ffd577666501d3. All latest uploaded blobs\nmatched read-back hashes. No production tenant value, grant, deployment\nor provider publication was invented.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7013be3fdb545006cf4c8eb0780fa77be864dabe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/7013be3fdb545006cf4c8eb0780fa77be864dabe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33","verification":{"payload":"tree 7013be3fdb545006cf4c8eb0780fa77be864dabe\nparent d89b3261018500e6e8ba237c514d6246c6a1eba6\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791314604 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791314604 +0300\n\nConnector platform: first two waves and API key providers (#1203)\n\nImplements the first two ten-provider connector waves, retaining Gmail,\nplus API-key read integrations for OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Vercel and\nLova