fresh still require verification. Do not\nequate merge with live provider connectivity.\n\nAdds optional trusted tenant proof to GET /security/session: canonical\nIDs, active SQL membership and active organization are required; the\nexisting response without the query is unchanged. FuzeKeys account\nlinking depends on this endpoint. 133 proof/session tests pass.\nAdditional focused validation passes: 240 identity UI tests, 151\nsecurity/OIDC tests, 15 billing acceptance tests and 44 merged access\ntests; clean installs, declaration builds and email build/tests pass.\nPostgreSQL integration and fresh CI remain required.\n\nPublisher readiness now separates metadata packets from evidence for\nprovider checks. Slack''s native app/adoption requirements, Google\nMarketplace setup and Atlassian Forge readiness are documented; no\npublication or eligibility is claimed.\n\nLatest organization/approval compatibility: initial exchanges supply the\nexplicit server FUZE_CONNECTOR_AUTHZ_TENANT or shared-router\nresourceTenant option. No default resource organization exists; Security\nverifies active SQL membership. Directory tid, email and\nrequest-selected organization are not proof. Both shared-provider and\nGmail transports treat Keys HTTP 202 authorization_pending as awaiting\napproval, never connected. OAuth callbacks redirect with the pending\nstatus; API-key UI clears the input and asks the user to contact their\nadministrator and connect again. Only Keys HTTP 200 updated confirms\ncredential storage. Secrets are not cached for pending retry.\n\nLatest focused validation: 8 resource-organization configuration tests,\n7 fail-closed credential-outcome cases and 2 rendered React\npending-approval regressions pass. Shared TypeScript delegation SDK\nforwarding tests pass (the identical source passed its 38-test SDK\nsuite). Modified routes/UI pass syntax transpilation; full\nbackend/frontend tests/typechecks were not rerun for these latest\nchanges. service-auth 0.1.4, backend pin and two root-lock entries\nalign; Security-client 0.9.x development dependency stays unchanged\nuntil #1389 merges and its 0.10.0 package is available. Fresh head CI\nremains required. Current source head\naeda9fa3dbe4e69d826d4f0d07ffd577666501d3. All latest uploaded blobs\nmatched read-back hashes. No production tenant value, grant, deployment\nor provider publication was invented.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUqsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5eEQAHNREc5BJAIeFBt+4WkWc8vN\nGiMsSGT5jWnfyFRS4aiGv9SZbWSMy4iyaDuRK8cuEZB441P7tXCKDbmUSGC7G2ok\nn8beO+QrfQlpMb81ajMy35hkYBbArWL7VpM8Jd0qSFtcGXoyI72pARX8qZcjm1fH\n48quxLfVp++KoVYGmmjVDj3hDFUrSvMU+bUFKQq+q+h7qqFG2W0LwwicOhtMgCs6\noLn/XCHuAoHWcq/pFCW9y99EzG82q9KFDU8Ki1dWWN7HcA4cClqcsH5uuZmtUvou\njla4RZY+/ES8eD/kk3Niu2uZszyQodBvzniYJknN7O49VxIA2SAGy2sp4tqWYeOj\n7zBj+LKXZh0a6yvdauFR5+DuzZzFVhs2IrlvqusK0RwtXDo49e3v5FbtdvCAvZHH\nZpbr4HnaKnbibuLTL78JqtvUBDE3GKGWmneFeg5MpVH5i1BNnUK3K1O7Yt07u5DE\nY1qt6NVWcty+x82pTR2C2z8frwUwnjdjxO86GGqKkLvbW4WAcocY9gOzU2eVg3Fw\nLff8m0srdhVYfRrr6+SHwPQSBbtH2IZD7Wwreetpl45qg/hiTidasy4XET+RPz68\nPPQZy2MJHiCm8fY+Z2/Fl+DsksFodBpEKgAM0OPh5VHfecOrNegpv+NC8nihbZrF\nWFG9wVnZ0eqD/RaNGALf\n=vjwX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T19:23:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKGMzM2Y4Y2QxM2YzMDQ2YTRmNGIzOGRlOGQ0MTEyMWJhNDg4ZWNmMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/d89b3261018500e6e8ba237c514d6246c6a1eba6","sha":"d89b3261018500e6e8ba237c514d6246c6a1eba6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/d89b3261018500e6e8ba237c514d6246c6a1eba6"}],"sha":"c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c33f8cd13f3046a4f4b38de8d41121ba488ecf33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/d89b3261018500e6e8ba237c514d6246c6a1eba6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:15:57Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:15:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Release Security identity and scoped ownership bootstrap before FuzeKeys (#1389)\n\nFuzeKeys authorization needs trusted organization membership and\ninstance policies before its connector protocol deploys. This\nmaster-based Security bootstrap releases additive scoped policies, SQL\nmembership proof, verified workload callers and exact owner-grant\nvalidation independently of connector #1203.\n\nToken exchange now requires an explicit canonical organization selector\nfor initial user sessions, verifies active SQL membership and session\nrevocation before signing, and preserves/rechecks signed organization\nmembership for chained delegation. Chained exchanges cannot change\ntenant, expand scopes or use an audience other than their immediate\nworkload actor. TypeScript and Python shared delegation clients forward\nthe optional tenant selector. FuzeFront connector callers must provide\nthe actual configured resource organization; Authentik directory tid and\nuser email are not organization proof. FuzeKeys must preserve the\nverified SDK tenant_id and implement its Connector resource\npolicy/inventory/grant lifecycle before enforcing that family; this PR\ndoes not invent those grants.\n\nInstance roles remain scoped. Registered-product sync uses canonical\nunderscore keys; the dormant Security CLI retains legacy dot keys. No\nautomatic resource rename or ownership backfill is enabled. Security\nruntime/spec/package is 0.10.0 and unpublished consumer service-auth\npackage remains 0.1.4 with aligned dependencies.\n\nValidation: 139 Security tests pass (125 AuthN route tests, 8 real\nmembership-helper cases and 6 new delegation organization regressions);\nSecurity typecheck passes. Shared delegation selector forwarding tests\npass in TypeScript and Python. Earlier 34 membership/workload tests\npassed before the latest exchange changes; latest CI and ordinary\nrequired review must pass before merge. All seven uploaded source/test\nblobs were read back and matched exact hashes. Current source head\n994168ba7735f508300539b712fda89515ed1ea3.\n\nRelease order remains Security bootstrap, live canonical policy and\nreviewed grant provisioning, FuzeKeys #205 protocol, connector FuzeFront\n#1203. Verified production deployment, tenant mappings, exact instance\ngrants and live smoke tests remain required; none are claimed complete.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ccd924ecc315f19ebf83dd1550767caa8efbf0bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/ccd924ecc315f19ebf83dd1550767caa8efbf0bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/d89b3261018500e6e8ba237c514d6246c6a1eba6","verification":{"payload":"tree ccd924ecc315f19ebf83dd1550767caa8efbf0bb\nparent 3664fa8cd810d5346976b5c91e3efe3e02567b27\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791314157 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791314157 +0300\n\nRelease Security identity and scoped ownership bootstrap before FuzeKeys (#1389)\n\nFuzeKeys authorization needs trusted organization membership and\ninstance policies before its connector protocol deploys. This\nmaster-based Security bootstrap releases additive scoped policies, SQL\nmembership proof, verified workload callers and exact owner-grant\nvalidation independently of connector #1203.\n\nToken exchange now requires an explicit canonical organization selector\nfor initial user sessions, verifies active SQL membership and session\nrevocation before signing, and preserves/rechecks signed organization\nmembership for chained delegation. Chained exchanges cannot change\ntenant, expand scopes or use an audience other than their immediate\nworkload actor. TypeScript and Python shared delegation clients forward\nthe optional tenant selector. FuzeFront connector callers must provide\nthe actual configured resource organization; Authentik directory tid and\nuser email are not organization proof. FuzeKeys must preserve the\nverified SDK tenant_id and implement its Connector resource\npolicy/inventory/grant lifecycle before enforcing that family; this PR\ndoes not invent those grants.\n\nInstance roles remain scoped. Registered-product sync uses canonical\nunderscore keys; the dormant Security CLI retains legacy dot keys. No\nautomatic resource rename or ownership backfill is enabled. Security\nruntime/spec/package is 0.10.0 and unpublished consumer service-auth\npackage remains 0.1.4 with aligned dependencies.\n\nValidation: 139 Security tests pass (125 AuthN route tests, 8 real\nmembership-helper cases and 6 new delegation organization regressions);\nSecurity typecheck passes. Shared delegation selector forwarding tests\npass in TypeScript and Python. Earlier 34 membership/workload tests\npassed before the latest exchange changes; latest CI and ordinary\nrequired review must pass before merge. All seven uploaded source/test\nblobs were read back and matched exact hashes. Current source head\n994168ba7735f508300539b712fda89515ed1ea3.\n\nRelease order remains Security bootstrap, live canonical policy and\nreviewed grant provisioning, FuzeKeys #205 protocol, connector FuzeFront\n#1203. Verified production deployment, tenant mappings, exact instance\ngrants and live smoke tests remain required; none are claimed complete.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUjtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmK8QAH7b+6sf/hDrOXe9yJX49uQQ\n8rHgbzkA9mNKp0oUH4ofVijjdDLocVf4DwQMcg2cm3B5lGi5PIYfhE9TZm+EHR8A\nQFaTAbRULibm/Fnmm6qt3By