://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/ce1b7a4fcfa4965b0c6dcfb9b9540145cdd37035"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/5f2a39a0880075b59ae9a1007908df86e24e0af1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/5f2a39a0880075b59ae9a1007908df86e24e0af1","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDVmMmEzOWEwODgwMDc1YjU5YWU5YTEwMDc5MDhkZjg2ZTI0ZTBhZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/c629973ac4ae37d95d526148c79ad54580a0b2c0","sha":"c629973ac4ae37d95d526148c79ad54580a0b2c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c629973ac4ae37d95d526148c79ad54580a0b2c0"}],"sha":"5f2a39a0880075b59ae9a1007908df86e24e0af1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/5f2a39a0880075b59ae9a1007908df86e24e0af1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c629973ac4ae37d95d526148c79ad54580a0b2c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:48:29Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:48:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: narrow code-review outage exception, truthful auto-approve text, skip closed PRs (#1266)\n\n## Summary\nThree tightening-only CI changes. `fuze-code-review` is NOT added to\n`required_now`; bot auto-approval and who may ship are unchanged.\n\n1. **Outage exception narrowed by path**\n(`scripts/fuze_code_review_verdict.py`, `fuze-code-review.yml`): outage\n(availability or step-never-reported) on a PR hitting\n`SENSITIVE_PATTERN` or the new `DEPLOY_SENSITIVE_PATTERN` =>\n`outage_blocking` (comment, `::error`, `exit 1`). Other paths still exit\n0 but emit `::warning` + a step-summary line \"NO REVIEW WAS PERFORMED\".\nOutage comments carry `<!-- fuze-code-review-outage -->` and are PATCHed\nin place instead of re-posted. `AVAILABILITY_PATTERNS` untouched; no `||\ntrue` / `continue-on-error`. Tests added:\n`outage_on_sensitive_path_blocks`, `outage_on_plain_path_passes`,\n`task_failure_still_abstains` (+ hang, marker, never-approves cases).\n2. **Truthful auto-approve text** (`auto-merge.yml`): approval body now\nstates it is posted at PR-open, auto-merge is armed, and merge happens\nonly when required checks pass. Approval retained.\n3. **Skip closed PRs** (`a2a-maintain.yml`, `fuze-code-review.yml`):\npre-checkout `gh api .../pulls/$N --jq .state`; if not open, a\n`::notice` is emitted and later steps are skipped via real `if:`\nconditions. An API error fails the step loudly.\n\n## Mirror into FuzeSDLC (not edited here)\n- `scripts/fuze_code_review_verdict.py`\n- `scripts/__tests__/test_fuze_code_review_verdict.py`\n- `.github/workflows/fuze-code-review.yml`\n\n`auto-merge.yml` and `a2a-maintain.yml` are repo-local in intent; mirror\nonly if FuzeSDLC carries the same templates.\n\n## Verification\n- `python -m unittest` on the verdict tests: 49 pass locally.\n- `gate_workflow_yaml.py`, `gate_vacuous_check.py`,\n`gate_workflow_policy.py`: clean for the three touched workflows.\n- Not verified: `actionlint` (not installed) and live behaviour of the\ncomment-upsert and PR-state steps; they only run on a real workflow run.\nExpected-red non-required checks: `fuze-code-review` outage skip,\n`a2a-maintain` (provider credits). Note this PR touches\n`.github/workflows/**`, so an outage here will itself be\n`outage_blocking`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01SYyHwr9DhVeeYzqufc3Yes\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01SYyHwr9DhVeeYzqufc3Yes)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f051680ba5891c302e06f8ce56de52635db0a914","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/f051680ba5891c302e06f8ce56de52635db0a914"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/c629973ac4ae37d95d526148c79ad54580a0b2c0","verification":{"payload":"tree f051680ba5891c302e06f8ce56de52635db0a914\nparent 86ccadee14578475032d67fcf42b8faaa43b3bda\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791186509 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791186509 +0300\n\nci: narrow code-review outage exception, truthful auto-approve text, skip closed PRs (#1266)\n\n## Summary\nThree tightening-only CI changes. `fuze-code-review` is NOT added to\n`required_now`; bot auto-approval and who may ship are unchanged.\n\n1. **Outage exception narrowed by path**\n(`scripts/fuze_code_review_verdict.py`, `fuze-code-review.yml`): outage\n(availability or step-never-reported) on a PR hitting\n`SENSITIVE_PATTERN` or the new `DEPLOY_SENSITIVE_PATTERN` =>\n`outage_blocking` (comment, `::error`, `exit 1`). Other paths still exit\n0 but emit `::warning` + a step-summary line \"NO REVIEW WAS PERFORMED\".\nOutage comments carry `<!-- fuze-code-review-outage -->` and are PATCHed\nin place instead of re-posted. `AVAILABILITY_PATTERNS` untouched; no `||\ntrue` / `continue-on-error`. Tests added:\n`outage_on_sensitive_path_blocks`, `outage_on_plain_path_passes`,\n`task_failure_still_abstains` (+ hang, marker, never-approves cases).\n2. **Truthful auto-approve text** (`auto-merge.yml`): approval body now\nstates it is posted at PR-open, auto-merge is armed, and merge happens\nonly when required checks pass. Approval retained.\n3. **Skip closed PRs** (`a2a-maintain.yml`, `fuze-code-review.yml`):\npre-checkout `gh api .../pulls/$N --jq .state`; if not open, a\n`::notice` is emitted and later steps are skipped via real `if:`\nconditions. An API error fails the step loudly.\n\n## Mirror into FuzeSDLC (not edited here)\n- `scripts/fuze_code_review_verdict.py`\n- `scripts/__tests__/test_fuze_code_review_verdict.py`\n- `.github/workflows/fuze-code-review.yml`\n\n`auto-merge.yml` and `a2a-maintain.yml` are repo-local in intent; mirror\nonly if FuzeSDLC carries the same templates.\n\n## Verification\n- `python -m unittest` on the verdict tests: 49 pass locally.\n- `gate_workflow_yaml.py`, `gate_vacuous_check.py`,\n`gate_workflow_policy.py`: clean for the three touched workflows.\n- Not verified: `actionlint` (not installed) and live behaviour of the\ncomment-upsert and PR-state steps; they only run on a real workflow run.\nExpected-red non-required checks: `fuze-code-review` outage skip,\n`a2a-maintain` (provider credits). Note this PR touches\n`.github/workflows/**`, so an outage here will itself be\n`outage_blocking`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01SYyHwr9DhVeeYzqufc3Yes\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01SYyHwr9DhVeeYzqufc3Yes)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <4189