68e41da4c6f89d3a877609e2b1479f3fd1bff1a4"}],"sha":"86ccadee14578475032d67fcf42b8faaa43b3bda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/86ccadee14578475032d67fcf42b8faaa43b3bda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/68e41da4c6f89d3a877609e2b1479f3fd1bff1a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:34:19Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:34:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(helm): expose A2A and MCP SSE gateway publicly via Ingress (#1277)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add conditional `Ingress` + Traefik `StripPrefix` Middleware for the\n**A2A pod** (`/a2a → a2a-fuzefront:8080`) so it is reachable from the\npublic internet at `https://app.fuzefront.com/a2a/*`\n- Add conditional `Ingress` + Traefik `StripPrefix` Middleware for the\n**MCP SSE gateway** (`/mcp → fuzefront-mcp:8081`) so it is reachable at\n`https://app.fuzefront.com/mcp/{sse,messages,tools.json,healthz}`\n- Both are `enabled: false` in `values.yaml`; `enabled: true` in\n`values-prod.yaml`\n\n## Auth model\n\n**A2A** — no auth middleware at the Ingress layer is needed. The A2A pod\nvalidates OIDC tokens itself (`audience: a2a`, `callerClaim: repo`,\ndiscovery via in-cluster Authentik). Requests with invalid or absent\ntokens are rejected by the pod before any RPC processing.\n\n**MCP SSE** — no ForwardAuth middleware is added, by design. The gateway\nforwards the **caller''s** bearer token to the upstream app-registry\n(Authentik + Permit validates it there). Calls with no `Authorization`\nheader fail closed at the first tool invocation\n(`MissingIdentityError`). Adding a Traefik ForwardAuth would intercept\nthe token before it reaches the gateway and break the pass-through\ndesign.\n\nThe tool surface (`/tools.json`, `listTools`) is intentionally public —\nit exposes API shape only, matching the published OpenAPI spec. No data\nis ever returned without a valid token.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] `helm lint` passes (verified locally: 0 failures)\n- [ ] `helm template` renders 9 `Ingress` resources including\n`fuzefront-a2a` and `fuzefront-mcp` with correct Traefik middleware\nannotations\n- [ ] After Argo sync: `curl https://app.fuzefront.com/mcp/healthz`\nreturns `{\"status\":\"ok\",...}`\n- [ ] After Argo sync: `curl\nhttps://app.fuzefront.com/a2a/.well-known/agent.json` returns the agent\ncard\n- [ ] MCP tool call without `Authorization` header returns\n`MissingIdentityError`\n- [ ] MCP tool call with valid Authentik JWT returns actual app-registry\ndata\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WEuriU3M9tXxBbzYNr5FZW\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WEuriU3M9tXxBbzYNr5FZW)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef4217757d6b41346d366a5e6ee681d8f402935b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/ef4217757d6b41346d366a5e6ee681d8f402935b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/68e41da4c6f89d3a877609e2b1479f3fd1bff1a4","verification":{"payload":"tree ef4217757d6b41346d366a5e6ee681d8f402935b\nparent dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791185659 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791185659 +0300\n\nfeat(helm): expose A2A and MCP SSE gateway publicly via Ingress (#1277)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add conditional `Ingress` + Traefik `StripPrefix` Middleware for the\n**A2A pod** (`/a2a → a2a-fuzefront:8080`) so it is reachable from the\npublic internet at `https://app.fuzefront.com/a2a/*`\n- Add conditional `Ingress` + Traefik `StripPrefix` Middleware for the\n**MCP SSE gateway** (`/mcp → fuzefront-mcp:8081`) so it is reachable at\n`https://app.fuzefront.com/mcp/{sse,messages,tools.json,healthz}`\n- Both are `enabled: false` in `values.yaml`; `enabled: true` in\n`values-prod.yaml`\n\n## Auth model\n\n**A2A** — no auth middleware at the Ingress layer is needed. The A2A pod\nvalidates OIDC tokens itself (`audience: a2a`, `callerClaim: repo`,\ndiscovery via in-cluster Authentik). Requests with invalid or absent\ntokens are rejected by the pod before any RPC processing.\n\n**MCP SSE** — no ForwardAuth middleware is added, by design. The gateway\nforwards the **caller''s** bearer token to the upstream app-registry\n(Authentik + Permit validates it there). Calls with no `Authorization`\nheader fail closed at the first tool invocation\n(`MissingIdentityError`). Adding a Traefik ForwardAuth would intercept\nthe token before it reaches the gateway and break the pass-through\ndesign.\n\nThe tool surface (`/tools.json`, `listTools`) is intentionally public —\nit exposes API shape only, matching the published OpenAPI spec. No data\nis ever returned without a valid token.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] `helm lint` passes (verified locally: 0 failures)\n- [ ] `helm template` renders 9 `Ingress` resources including\n`fuzefront-a2a` and `fuzefront-mcp` with correct Traefik middleware\nannotations\n- [ ] After Argo sync: `curl https://app.fuzefront.com/mcp/healthz`\nreturns `{\"status\":\"ok\",...}`\n- [ ] After Argo sync: `curl\nhttps://app.fuzefront.com/a2a/.well-known/agent.json` returns the agent\ncard\n- [ ] MCP tool call without `Authorization` header returns\n`MissingIdentityError`\n- [ ] MCP tool call with valid Authentik JWT returns actual app-registry\ndata\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WEuriU3M9tXxBbzYNr5FZW\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WEuriU3M9tXxBbzYNr5FZW)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw1L7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe4sQACHYVM5CwEi2UtBFz5dspZt9\nEP7+jaD5gfLe7jBgVayE+SbF3YgRyXCLpDCory3INQgGuMefxmPej6J+DnMhOc7x\nFjeLLjUFhKxUxUAhTl8c52WHgwxtHgWKhnUhjZNuhs3AjjBMeL1E7aKLz3We+Jm1\nAQ1eph0xsiPeFogCfijAbdlNS9JKiUKH3V8MdNHaCRcgkfeIhl0y6oTV3qQp+x3p\nwAhKUjOKqtdxBL638005sTdVlLRVr4vE68fd99iSoxozU7ldq98a5KnGsrWeINzA\n3+KNl0KQscUldo2rwR2Pb3VaQMx7yOZtBcuVyqY04SfzX2YZD9LKEt99dxAO9sSF\nGNDgwXzv8fmNfY6CimRCzpCSoNbg7q7dAmRvjvdAegyZ9NbLgiL0hlDqMm3jS7Lw\nSUFUz6SC3vqdpgnosETcVSNpfmgQJ4IIUf7GO+GWD1QUz5BB1qiPaaiRHAaSnNdM\nRgSXRkmPiBTVQEDZaN+bNr3LuPuC5F4CFzwkaJnUwywSgnKqOmolA92/z7gCLTYx\nDcVGG08EjA/f8EXtNsMPmdP6T/xDA6C28fur6xfPSn4QeVn8x5ie6p5M7reHPS1M\nvEs0uTTbdjj8tTjkKNJe27jJ7a2v5W5cgjh9SRPTdbvDv6cJ+usKbaJWUae4lxEB\nsoKrp9rFUiRC5iCpJkho\n=18b9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T07:34:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/68e41da4c6f89d3a877609e2b1479f3fd1bff1a4","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDY4ZTQxZGE0YzZmODlkM2E4Nzc2MDllMmIxNDc5ZjNmZDFiZmYxYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784","sha":"dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784"}],"sha":"68e41da4c6f89d3a877609e2b1479f3fd1bff1a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/68e41da4c6f89d3a877609e2b1479f3fd1bff1a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:31:20Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:31:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(portal-census): stop blaming the disabled register-hook for Plan''s MISSING row (#1249)\n\n## Summary\nCorrects two annotations in `scripts/expected-portal-apps.json` (the\n`plan` entry''s `source`, and `_meta.genuinelyAbsentAtLastReview`) that\nattribute Plan''s MISSING census row to FuzePlan''s `register-hook.yaml`.\n\nThat was wrong against FuzePlan''s own repo:\n- The hook is **disabled** (`register.enabled: false`, including in\n`values-prod.yaml`) and is dead code.\n- The chart registers through the fail-closed **`registration` init\ncontainer** on the backend Deployment (authenticated, slug `plan`), so\n\"the init container is not wired into that chart\" was false.\n\n## What is actually established\n- Plan''s manifest declares `visibility: organization`; the census\ncredential is not a platform admin, so a non-public row is invisible to\nit. `MISSING` cannot distinguish \"absent\" from \"not visible to the\ncaller\" (see the COVERAGE CAVEAT in\n`check-portal-federation-health.mjs`).\n- Plan''s dedicated `frontend-mfe` remote only reached prod on 2026-10-04\n(FuzePlan #324 / #330 unblocked the Release image build).\n- So Plan''s registration is now recorded as **UNMEASURED**, with the\nthree things someone with cluster/admin access must confirm: the\n`fuzefront-registration` Secret exists in namespace `fuzeplan`, the init\ncontainer completed, and an admin-credentialed `GET\n/api/v1/app-registry/apps` returns `plan`.\n\nNo slug or name is changed (slug immutability rule).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `node --test scripts/__tests__/expected-portal-apps.test.mjs` — 5\npassed\n- [x] File still parses as valid JSON\n- [ ] CI gates\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6df982b9530a5e8bdb2d55033777f99c55468ea6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/6df982b9530a5e8bdb2d55033777f99c55468ea6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784","verification":{"payload":"tree 6df982b9530a5e8bdb2d55033777f99c55468ea6\nparent 4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791185480 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791185480 +0300\n\ndocs(portal-census): stop blaming the disabled register-hook for Plan''s MISSING row (#1249)\n\n## Summary\nCorrects two annotations in `scripts/expected-portal-apps.json` (the\n`plan` entry''s `source`, and `_meta.genuinelyAbsentAtLastReview`) that\nattribute Plan''s MISSING census row to FuzePlan''s `register-hook.yaml`.\n\nThat was wrong against FuzePlan''s own repo:\n- The hook is **disabled** (`register.enabled: false`, including in\n`values-prod.yaml`) and is dead code.\n- The chart registers through the fail-closed **`registration` init\ncontainer** on the backend Deployment (authenticated, slug `plan`), so\n\"the init container is not wired into that chart\" was false.\n\n## What is actually established\n- Plan''s manifest declares `visibility: organization`; the census\ncredential is not a platform admin, so a non-public row is invisible to\nit. `MISSING` cannot distinguish \"absent\" from \"not visible to the\ncaller\" (see the COVERAGE CAVEAT in\n`check-portal-federation-health.mjs`).\n- Plan''s dedicated `frontend-mfe` remote only reached prod on 2026-10-04\n(FuzePlan #324 / #330 unblocked the Release image build).\n- So Plan''s registration is now recorded as **UNMEASURED**, with the\nthree things someone with cluster/admin access must confirm: the\n`fuzefront-registration` Secret exists in namespace `fuzeplan`, the init\ncontainer completed, and an admin-credentialed `GET\n/api/v1/app-registry/apps` returns `plan`.\n\nNo slug or name is changed (slug immutability rule).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `node --test scripts/__tests__/expected-portal-apps.test.mjs` — 5\npassed\n- [x] File still parses as valid JSON\n- [ ] CI gates\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw1JICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzTcQAHlYd0Xbj5vd/Wdl4BgIf9d0\ncrAgqIGPWE3SB67xLzTOOAD2iKr7HgPmi1btpNud7o0+8LlgdfecMg5JMAcQtw1/\nARundUR8f719TIx93DnE9YhbyjF0V5zuKO45nLumqKFLO0vEaQNtVoaJ/reOT5OD\nILNhvEQ4Rnh7ew245ZFdrY9EAC/idG/qENDVgesNMzL0VyFteH3yCaBPBKozKJTM\nFq0zbIGcgBk+Z6+mr9/OVRWpocj+MEF3y9VySuio5GcXy319u+Kw4hQMEO9w2XN1\nUeIzy8KAb4XQZHG6arV0ZDK4L0LZM19TC2XtnmTcL7D6jQKAA3g/v4vvUqnhfspl\nluk864keFEpsrOJUF2DhltSRiftuGSDlQejvU0aICCcdaPpW0b0Lu6kUiXxLCm06\nZ/cqJbCaPK5MS4+YBkYT+Hs4m1SAAa3zQFZR2YTspLvRqhtz+imNLAJmEaXORLHX\nsZsh8Kj31lkznXOZyByAey8rSH/pUiO5/MjrQ83DzOB329ctDWWwZJ+RtITxdY7b\nz88mL1Y156nq1eHdyO9oQ7DZMY1g3HTlC6nPrlt+ySwp0pProVjdvGhlKIuMswLI\nmwyAlEuXY0qVykipKRcTZZ1wLsYyZKj+qLLnSCkeX0TfGfzfkvJSbzhRTrsUox7v\nIVw/5Q9d2X0+SDbJdVoi\n=pcNq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T07:31:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKGRkOWQ0YTViNTVhMTZhMzJmOGQ0N2I2MzBmMjY0YzJiZjgwZTQ3ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4","sha":"4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4"}],"sha":"dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/dd9d4a5b55a16a32f8d47b630f264c2bf80e4784"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:31:16Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:31:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(selection-lists): deflake access.routes membership-token assertion (#1268)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nThe `selection-list-service` unit suite `tests/access.routes.test.ts`\nwas failing intermittently on the `machine identity for grant/revoke\nwrites › PUT: grant uses the machine token; the membership check keeps\nthe end-user token` test (seen red on CI run 37209111757, job \"Selection\nlist service (unit)\", on the merge ref of PR #1249).\n\n**Root cause — a flaky test, not an authorization regression.** The\nassertion compared the token the route *forwarded* to the membership\n`check` against a *freshly minted* `userToken()`:\n\n```ts\nconst userToken = () => makeToken();            // jwt.sign(...) — stamps a per-second `iat`\n...\n.set({ Authorization: `Bearer ${userToken()}` })   // minted at request-build time\n...\nexpect(checkToken).toBe(userToken());              // minted again in the assertion\n```\n\n`makeToken()` is `jwt.sign(...)`, which stamps an `iat` (seconds). The\ntwo calls produce **byte-different** JWTs whenever they straddle a\n1-second boundary — which happens when the handler''s async work is slow\non a loaded CI runner. The failure message masked the tokens as\n`***`/`***`; decoding them shows identical payloads differing only by\n`iat` (off by one).\n\nProduction is correct: `access.ts` forwards the end-user bearer\n(`bearer(req)`) to the membership probe and the service''s machine token\nonly to the grant/revoke writes — exactly as intended by the review-C-1\ndesign. The test was asserting against the clock, not the principal.\n\nIntroduced in #1248 (commit 35032540), which added this `D) Machine\nidentity` block. PR #1249 only edits\n`scripts/expected-portal-apps.json`, so it did not cause the break — it\nmerely surfaced the pre-existing flake on its merge ref.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [x] 🧪 Test addition or improvement\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n\nRan the service''s unit suites locally with the same command CI uses\n(`npm run -w selection-list-service test`), after building the workspace\ndeps the CI job builds (`@fuzefront/auth`, `shared`, `security-client`,\n`service-auth`) on Node 22 (CI uses 24).\n\n**Before (failure reproduced deterministically):** forcing the handler\nto cross a 1-second boundary (a 1.1s busy-wait in the injected `check`\nmock) reproduces the exact CI failure at `access.routes.test.ts:638`:\n\n```\n● machine identity for grant/revoke writes › PUT: grant uses the machine token; the membership check keeps the end-user token\n    expect(received).toBe(expected)\n    Expected: \"...eyJ1c2VySWQiOiJ1c3JfYWRtaW4iLCJvcmdJZCI6Im9yZ19jb3JwIiwiaWF0IjoxNzkxMTM3ODEwfQ...\"   // iat …810 (re-minted)\n    Received: \"...eyJ1c2VySWQiOiJ1c3JfYWRtaW4iLCJvcmdJZCI6Im9yZ19jb3JwIiwiaWF0IjoxNzkxMTM3ODA5fQ...\"   // iat …809 (the user token the route forwarded)\n    > 638 |     expect(checkToken).toBe(userToken());\n```\n\nThe `Received` token decodes to\n`{userId:\"usr_admin\",orgId:\"org_corp\",iat:…809}` — the real end-user\ntoken, not the machine token.\n\n**After:** the fixed test passes normally **and** still passes when the\nhandler is forced across the same 1-second boundary:\n```\n✓ PUT: grant uses the machine token; the membership check keeps the end-user token (1141 ms)\n```\n\nFull unit run after the fix: `21 passed, 2 failed` suites — the only 2\nfailures are `handlers.db.test.ts` and\n`migrations.seed-events.db.test.ts`, which fail with `ECONNREFUSED\n127.0.0.1:5432` because this sandbox has no Postgres (CI provides the\n`postgres` service). `access.routes.test.ts` passes.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **Backend Changes (test only):**\n`services/selection-list-service/tests/access.routes.test.ts`\n- Mint the caller''s token **once** (`const userToken = makeToken();`)\nand reuse the exact string in the request header and both assertions, so\nthe comparison tests the principal, not the `iat` clock.\n- Add an explicit `expect(checkToken).not.toBe(MACHINE_TOKEN)` guard so\nthe test still fails loudly if the membership probe ever starts\nevaluating the service''s machine identity instead of the human''s\nauthority over the target — preserving the real regression this test is\nmeant to catch.\n\nNo production code changed; no behavior change.\n\n### Code Quality\n\n- [x] Self-review of code completed\n- [x] No console.log or debugging statements left in code\n\n## 📋 Checklist\n\n- [x] I have performed a self-review of my code\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings or errors\n- [x] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes (except\nthe 2 Postgres-dependent suites, which need the CI `postgres` service)\n- [x] Code follows conventional commit format\n\n## 🔄 Backwards Compatibility\n\n- [x] Fully backwards compatible\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01JvPbucfxXXBrCheqhxYyzR\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01JvPbucfxXXBrCheqhxYyzR)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"95f8afcd118b64c2c4a20d0b38d58980f1b91180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/95f8afcd118b64c2c4a20d0b38d58980f1b91180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4","verification":{"payload":"tree 95f8afcd118b64c2c4a20d0b38d58980f1b91180\nparent c3593ee2ef7367346254e138dc6bc77d88d27879\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791185476 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791185476 +0300\n\nfix(selection-lists): deflake access.routes membership-token assertion (#1268)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nThe `selection-list-service` unit suite `tests/access.routes.test.ts`\nwas failing intermittently on the `machine identity for grant/revoke\nwrites › PUT: grant uses the machine token; the membership check keeps\nthe end-user token` test (seen red on CI run 37209111757, job \"Selection\nlist service (unit)\", on the merge ref of PR #1249).\n\n**Root cause — a flaky test, not an authorization regression.** The\nassertion compared the token the route *forwarded* to the membership\n`check` against a *freshly minted* `userToken()`:\n\n```ts\nconst userToken = () => makeToken();            // jwt.sign(...) — stamps a per-second `iat`\n...\n.set({ Authorization: `Bearer ${userToken()}` })   // minted at request-build time\n...\nexpect(checkToken).toBe(userToken());              // minted again in the assertion\n```\n\n`makeToken()` is `jwt.sign(...)`, which stamps an `iat` (seconds). The\ntwo calls produce **byte-different** JWTs whenever they straddle a\n1-second boundary — which happens when the handler''s async work is s