t/commit/4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDRhZDhiZGE5MWVmMjdiYTk4NGYyNmQ0YmRjZTNmYWM5MGY3MTBlZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/c3593ee2ef7367346254e138dc6bc77d88d27879","sha":"c3593ee2ef7367346254e138dc6bc77d88d27879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c3593ee2ef7367346254e138dc6bc77d88d27879"}],"sha":"4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/4ad8bda91ef27ba984f26d4bdce3fac90f710ef4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c3593ee2ef7367346254e138dc6bc77d88d27879/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:22:48Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:22:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(app-builder): Permit App#creator role, instance-role revoke on removal, Helm env wiring, Unleash flag creation (#1288)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nFollow-up to #1261 (build-with-agent / creator ownership / marketplace\npublishing, flags OFF). This PR makes the platform side ready to turn\nthose flags on.\n\n- **Permit:** declares an `App#creator` resource-instance role in both\nschema copies. It has `read`, `update`, `install` and `uninstall`. It\nhas no `delete` or `create`, and no derivation, so org admins keep\ncontrol through their tenant roles.\n- **Member removal:** `PermitAuthorizationProvider.removeMember` now\nalso revokes instance-scoped role assignments. Before this change it\nunassigned by (user, role, tenant) only. A Permit assignment is keyed by\n(user, role, tenant, resource_instance), so a departed member''s\n`App#creator` grant would have stayed in place. The code already says\nthis in `role-assignment.ts`.\n- **Helm:** adds `applicationsService.appBuilder.*` values and optional\nenv vars: `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_URL`, `APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`,\nthree rate limits, and `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_TOKEN` as an `optional:\ntrue` secretKeyRef. Every default is declared in `values.yaml`, with no\ncasts on `.Values` lookups. With the new values unset, the chart renders\nbyte-identical to before. The only rendered change is\n`APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` for local and prod.\n- **Runbook:** `docs/runbooks/app-builder-secrets.md` covers sealing the\ntoken.\n- **Unleash:** `prod-unleash-ops.yml` gains an `app-builder` set that\nonly creates the three flags. It never turns the environment on, adds a\nstrategy or calls `off`, so re-running it can''t undo a later enablement.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n- New `backend/security/tests/permit-remove-member.test.ts`: 3 pass. It\ncovers tenant-role and instance-role unassign, a tenant-wide unassign\ncarrying no `resource_instance`, and rows without a role.\n- `backend/tests/permit-schema.test.ts` gets an assertion for the\ncreator role. That suite can''t run here because its shared setup needs a\ndatabase (all 17 tests time out, with or without my change). I checked\nboth schema copies directly instead: the role''s permissions are all\ndeclared `App` actions.\n- Helm: `helm lint` passes and `kubeconform` is valid for values, local\nand prod. A before/after render diff shows only\n`APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` added for local and prod.\n`check-sealed-key-regression.sh` reports no regression.\n- Workflow: `bash -n` passes on both steps, and the dispatch options\nparse.\n- Existing failure: `authz-provider.test.ts › bulkCheck stays\nindex-aligned` fails with or without this change.\n\n## 🚨 Needs a decision (not changed here)\n\nThe app-registry authorizes with Permit actions named `apps:register`,\n`apps:write` and `apps:activate`\n(`backend/applications/src/app-registry/permit.ts`). The `App` resource\nin `permitSchema` declares only `create, read, update, delete, install,\nuninstall`, so those `apps:*` actions are not defined in this repo''s\nschema.\n\n- **Unconfirmed:** whether they exist in the live Permit project, and\nwhether Permit accepts a `:` in an action key. I couldn''t verify either\nfrom here.\n- **If they don''t exist,** the Permit half of those checks always\ndenies. Registry writes then work only for platform admins, and the\ncreator role grants nothing the registry checks.\n- **Why I didn''t change it:** renaming the checks could newly authorize\norg members, and that decision is yours.\n- **Org membership is still the object-level gate:** `canMutate`\nrequires membership in the owning org, so a departed creator can''t\nmutate an app even if a stale grant existed.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n- [x] Requires environment variable changes: `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_URL`\nand the sealed `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_TOKEN` are not set yet. Until they\nare, the build endpoint answers 503 `builder_unavailable`.\n- [x] Requires configuration changes:\n  - Permit schema sync (to create `App#creator`).\n- After merge, dispatch **Prod Unleash ops** with `flags: app-builder`\nto create the three flags (they stay OFF).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01HJeisvuB8eV9CR2m8XK8Be\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01HJeisvuB8eV9CR2m8XK8Be)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"870cd4a0383a1b444d9034d43e1fb630d9298646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/870cd4a0383a1b444d9034d43e1fb630d9298646"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/c3593ee2ef7367346254e138dc6bc77d88d27879","verification":{"payload":"tree 870cd4a0383a1b444d9034d43e1fb630d9298646\nparent d5e421c862bd6f70592593504e70460b3ebc1bc1\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791184968 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791184968 +0300\n\nfeat(app-builder): Permit App#creator role, instance-role revoke on removal, Helm env wiring, Unleash flag creation (#1288)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nFollow-up to #1261 (build-with-agent / creator ownership / marketplace\npublishing, flags OFF). This PR makes the platform side ready to turn\nthose flags on.\n\n- **Permit:** declares an `App#creator` resource-instance role in both\nschema copies. It has `read`, `update`, `install` and `uninstall`. It\nhas no `delete` or `create`, and no derivation, so org admins keep\ncontrol through their tenant roles.\n- **Member removal:** `PermitAuthorizationProvider.removeMember` now\nalso revokes instance-scoped role assignments. Before this change it\nunassigned by (user, role, tenant) only. A Permit assignment is keyed by\n(user, role, tenant, resource_instance), so a departed member''s\n`App#creator` grant would have stayed in place. The code already says\nthis in `role-assignment.ts`.\n- **Helm:** adds `applicationsService.appBuilder.*` values and optional\nenv vars: `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_URL`, `APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`,\nthree rate limits, and `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_TOKEN` as an `optional:\ntrue` secretKeyRef. Every default is declared in `values.yaml`, with no\ncasts on `.Values` lookups. With the new values unset, the chart renders\nbyte-identical to before. The only rendered change is\n`APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` for local and prod.\n- **Runbook:** `docs/runbooks/app-builder-secrets.md` covers sealing the\ntoken.\n- **Unleash:** `prod-unleash-ops.yml` gains an `app-builder` set that\nonly creates the three flags. It never turns the environment on, adds a\nstrategy or calls `off`, so re-running it can''t undo a later enablement.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n- New `backend/security/tests/permit-remove-member.test.ts`: 3 pass. It\ncovers tenant-role and instance-role unassign, a tenant-wide unassign\ncarrying no `resource_instance`, and rows without a role.\n- `backend/tests/permit-schema.test.ts` gets an assertion for the\ncreator role. That suite can''t run here because its shared setup needs a\ndatabase (all 17 tests time out, with or without my change). I checked\nboth schema copies directly instead: the role''s permissions are all\ndeclared `App` actions.\n- Helm: `helm lint` passes and `kubeconform` is valid for values, local\nand prod. A before/after render diff shows only\n`APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` added for local and prod.\n`check-sealed-key-regression.sh` reports no regression.\n- Workflow: `bash -n` passes on both steps, and the dispatch options\nparse.\n- Existing failure: `authz-provider.test.ts › bulkCheck stays\nindex-aligned` fails with or without this change.\n\n## 🚨 Needs a decision (not changed here)\n\nThe app-registry authorizes with Permit actions named `apps:register`,\n`apps:write` and `apps:activate`\n(`backend/applications/src/app-registry/permit.ts`). The `App` resource\nin `permitSchema` declares only `create, read, update, delete, install,\nuninstall`, so those `apps:*` actions are not defined in this repo''s\nschema.\n\n- **Unconfirmed:** whether they exist in the live Permit project, and\nwhether Permit accepts a `:` in an action key. I couldn''t verify either\nfrom here.\n- **If they don''t exist,** the Permit half of those checks always\ndenies. Registry writes then work only for platform admins, and the\ncreator role grants nothing the registry checks.\n- **Why I didn''t change it:** renaming the checks could newly authorize\norg members, and that decision is yours.\n- **Org membership is still the object-level gate:** `canMutate`\nrequires membership in the owning org, so a departed creator can''t\nmutate an app even if a stale grant existed.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n- [x] Requires environment variable changes: `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_URL`\nand the sealed `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_TOKEN` are not set yet. Until they\nare, the build endpoint answers 503 `builder_unavailable`.\n- [x] Requires configuration changes:\n  - Permit schema sync (to create `App#creator`).\n- After merge, dispatch **Prod Unleash ops** with `flags: app-builder`\nto create the three flags (they stay OFF).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01HJeisvuB8eV9CR2m8XK8Be\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01HJeisvuB8eV9CR2m8XK8Be)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw1BICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbUEQAJVkCpJG8kxsU6La7p8pUpbO\nEWlaOVqDtAy2S2yh6f5Per3QLv0DOIM1yg385aY/IU0zl9pAvkGG27NtybhjfxRU\nGl/K5FA0tWWFmGTkCGz9GwqYYJP7EOMb3w2kmLdFQrunK2X1ureBeXY3dx8nLNZ7\nfKqm/uAt27IiyW3GDMo/mKGWX8GoD5MSsi7DRv4Y/HXyHWWqwaC+UXZFnTVc0vin\ntwMV/BA