77d88d27879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c3593ee2ef7367346254e138dc6bc77d88d27879"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/d5e421c862bd6f70592593504e70460b3ebc1bc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:21:20Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:21:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): stop the subscription rung skipping silently and name it as the cause (#1274)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\n`fuze-code-review` keeps reporting a credit/quota outage. **The cause is\nnot a vendor balance — the\nsubscription rung never runs**, so every review is billed per token on\nthe metered rungs and dies at\nwhichever metered provider runs dry first.\n\nFrom the actual run log (job `111509563783`, on #1272):\n\n```\n##[notice]rung=claude vendor=litellm verdict: availability: matched pattern ''prepayment credits''\n\"message\": \"Your prepayment credits are depleted. Please go to AI Studio at https://ai.studio/...\"\n```\n\n**Two things that log does *not* contain are the point:** there is no\n`rung=claude-oauth` notice,\nand there are no warnings at all. `classify-claude-oauth` is gated\n`if: steps.claude-oauth.outcome != ''skipped''`, so the absence of that\nnotice is *proof* rung 1a was\nskipped — which, per its own `if: inputs.claude-code-oauth-token != ''''`,\nmeans the token was empty.\nThe depleted balance is **Google''s**, reached through LiteLLM, on a path\nonly taken because the\nsubscription path was never attempted.\n\nSo the failing credential is `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` being unset, and\nthe *reported* one is\nsomebody else''s prepaid balance. Nothing in the run said so.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- 🧪 Test addition or improvement\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n### What was actually wrong\n\n**Rung 1a''s absence was the only silent one.** The openai and gemini\nrungs each have a dedicated\n\"skipped — key empty\" notice step; rung 1a had none. That asymmetry is\nbackwards: those two are\noptional extras whose absence costs nothing, while rung 1a''s absence\nchanges the **billing model** of\nevery run through this action and converts a third party''s exhausted\ncredits into a review that never\nhappened.\n\nThe Finish step already knew — its own comment reads *\"An empty\nOAUTH_CODE means the rung never\nran\"* — and told nobody.\n\n### The fix — in the composite action, so it covers all **11** callers\nthat pass this token\n\n1. **A skip step** gated `inputs.claude-code-oauth-token == ''''`,\nemitting a `::warning` (not a\n`::notice`, unlike openai/gemini, for the reason above) that names the\nconsequence, the secret,\n   and `claude setup-token`.\n2. **`SUBSCRIPTION_NOTE` appended to the terminal availability\n`::error`**, naming the likely root\ncause. Empty whenever rung 1a actually ran, so a genuine vendor outage\nreads *exactly* as before.\n3. **A new `subscription-rung` output** (`ran` | `skipped-no-token`) so\na caller can distinguish \"a\nvendor ran out of credits\" from \"we never tried the subscription\".\nEmitted on every exit path\nincluding the green ones — a caller reporting \"this review was billed\nper token\" wants it on\n   success too.\n\n### Deliberately *not* changed\n\n- **`fuze-code-review.yml`''s credential check** treats the three\ncredentials as equivalent, which is\nthe same conflation one level up. Left alone: **#1266 is open against\nthat exact region**\n(`@@ -245,6 +266,10 @@`) and editing it would conflict for no gain. The\naction is the better place\n  anyway — one change, all eleven callers.\n- **Provider precedence** needed no change. It is already correct: rung\n1a runs first and only falls\nthrough on a classified availability error. Worth stating since \"make it\nprefer OAuth\" is the\n  natural assumption, and it already does.\n\n## 🚨 What this does NOT do\n\n**It does not make the outage stop.** Without a subscription token there\nis no subscription billing,\nfull stop — the only thing that fixes that is setting the secret:\n\n```sh\nclaude setup-token           # mints the token\ngh secret set CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN   # owner action; I cannot hold or set a secret value\n```\n\nThis change makes that absence **impossible to miss** instead of\ninvisible. It is the difference\nbetween a run that says \"a vendor ran out of credits\" and one that says\n\"you are on metered billing\nbecause this secret is unset, and that is why a vendor''s credits\nmattered.\"\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `classify.sh` self-test | **52 passed, 0 failed** |\n| `test_rung_gating` | **8 → 11 tests**, OK |\n| `test_run_blocks_parse` | OK — the new bash parses |\n| `test_passthrough_defaults` / `test_extra_env` /\n`test_review_caller_readonly` | 3 / 7 / 8, all OK |\n| `gate-workflow-yaml` | 90 files, **0 unparseable** |\n| `gate-vacuous-check` | **OK** |\n| Shell behaviour | executed the new Finish block over\n`OAUTH_CODE={empty,1,2}`: empty → `subscription-rung=skipped-no-token`\n**and** the error names the cause; `1` and `2` → `ran`, message\nbyte-identical to before |\n\n### The new tests are mutation-tested, not just observed passing\n\nThis repo''s own rule is that a gate seen only passing proves nothing, so\nI broke it three ways:\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Delete the skip step (i.e. restore the original bug) | **2 errors** |\n| Downgrade `::warning` to `::notice` | **1 failure** |\n| Make the two gates overlap (`if: always()`) | **1 failure** |\n| Restored | **OK** |\n\nThe gating test asserts the rung and its skip-notice are **exact\ncomplements** — not merely that a\nnotice exists somewhere. An overlap would warn on a run that *was*\nbilled to the subscription; a gap\nis the original silent-skip bug.\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n- [x] Manual testing (new shell logic executed across all branches)\n- [ ] Integration tests — n/a\n- [ ] E2E tests — n/a\n\n**Test Configuration:** Python 3 + PyYAML · bash\n\n## 📋 Checklist\n\n- [x] Self-review completed\n- [x] Code is commented, particularly in hard-to-understand areas —\nincluding *why* this is a warning\n      where the sibling rungs use notices\n- [x] No secret value is read, printed, fabricated or committed\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n- [x] Code follows conventional commit format\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n\n- [ ] Requires database migration — no\n- [x] **Requires configuration changes** — `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`\nmust be set for the underlying\nproblem to go away. This PR is what makes that requirement visible; it\ndoes not satisfy it.\n\n### Future Work\n\n- Once `subscription-rung` has a consumer, `fuze-code-review`''s outage\ncomment can say \"billed per\ntoken because the subscription token is unset\" instead of the generic\nvendor-credit wording. The\noutput is added here precisely so that is a one-line change later; it is\nintentionally unconsumed\n  for now so this PR does not collide with #1266.\n\n## 🔗 Related Issues and PRs\n\n- Diagnosed from `fuze-code-review` run `37227286759` / job\n`111509563783` on #1272\n- No overlap with **#1266** (narrows the outage exception): that PR\ntouches `fuze-code-review.yml`,\n`auto-merge.yml`, `a2a-maintain.yml` and\n`scripts/fuze_code_review_verdict.py`. This one touches\n  only `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/**`, which #1266 does not.\n\n## 🔄 Backwards Compatibility\n\n- [x] Fully backwards compatible. With a token present, behaviour and\nmessages are unchanged\n(verified by execution). With it absent, the run takes the same path and\nreaches the same\n      verdict — it just says why.\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0183JMAkioT5pGt8aVmddPtc\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_0183JMAkioT5pGt8aVmddPtc)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f51c6b50b7a0be2c53a49393f325a030f8210d66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/f51c6b50b7a0be2c53a49393f325a030f8210d66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/d5e421c862bd6f70592593504e70460b3ebc1bc1","verification":{"payload":"tree f51c6b50b7a0be2c53a49393f325a030f8210d66\nparent c77ec8c70153c18ec48e3065d1aa057cbc5ec1dc\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791184880 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791184880 +0000\n\nfix(ci): stop the subscription rung skipping silently and name it as the cause (#1274)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\n`fuze-code-review` keeps reporting a credit/quota outage. **The cause is\nnot a vendor balance — the\nsubscription rung never runs**, so every review is billed per token on\nthe metered rungs and dies at\nwhichever metered provider runs dry first.\n\nFrom the actual