.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fuze-agent","id":321521006,"login":"fuze-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEyoFbg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c77ec8c70153c18ec48e3065d1aa057cbc5ec1dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:20:56Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:20:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(billing): automate the authz cutover and turn it on in production (#1272)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nCompletes billing-service''s migration off the embedded Permit SDK\n(#1053) by **automating the\nproduction cutover and performing it**. #1053 shipped dark — correct\ncode, flag default OFF — and\nleft four manual steps behind. Three of them did not need to be manual.\n\n| Manual step from #1053 | What it is now |\n|---|---|\n| Register the Authentik S2S application | `billing-s2s-register`\nPreSync Job |\n| Retrieve the `client_secret` | never leaves the cluster at all |\n| Seal it into `billing-secrets` | a Job-written Secret instead (see\nbelow) |\n| Flip the flag + drop `optional: true` | `values-prod.yaml`, derived,\nrevertible in one line |\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- 🔧 Refactoring (removes a manual runbook procedure)\n- 🔨 Build system or dependency update (Helm chart)\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n### The credential never leaves the cluster\n\n`register-s2s-cli.js` gains `--write-env-file`: it writes\n`AUTHENTIK_CLIENT_ID` /\n`AUTHENTIK_CLIENT_SECRET` to a path at mode `0600` and **still never\nprints the secret**. The Job\nmints the credential in an initContainer, writes it to a memory-backed\n`emptyDir`, and a second\ncontainer feeds that file to `kubectl create secret generic\n--from-env-file`. The credential never\npasses through a terminal, a `kubectl logs` capture, a GitHub repo\nsecret, a PR diff, or this\nrepo''s history.\n\n**This is deliberately not the `seal-*.yml` route.** Those workflows are\nthe right shape for an\n*external vendor* credential a human already holds — they read a GitHub\nrepo secret the owner sets.\nRouting a cluster-minted secret out to GitHub and back would add two\nplaces it can leak for no gain.\n\n### A separate Secret, not `billing-secrets`\n\n`deploy/contabo/sealed/billing-secrets.yaml` carries no\n`sealedsecrets.bitnami.com/patch`\nannotation, so the controller **replaces** that Secret on every\nreconcile. A key patched into it\nwould survive until the next reconcile and then silently vanish. The Job\nwrites\n`billing-s2s-credentials` instead, and `billing-service.yaml` reads the\ntwo keys from there.\n\n### Ordering is the safety property — and it is fail-safe\n\nThe comment this replaces said *\"remove `optional: true` in the SAME\ndeploy window that seals the\nreal values and flips the flag on — not before\"*: a three-way\nhand-coordination with no mechanism\nbehind it. Now:\n\n- **`optional` is derived** — `optional: {{ not .authz.enabled }}`. Flag\nOFF ⇒ a missing Secret\ncannot break the live pod. Flag ON ⇒ a missing Secret is a hard error.\nThere is no window in\n  which the two can disagree.\n- **The Job is PreSync**, so the Secret exists before the Deployment is\nupdated.\n- **If the Job fails, the sync aborts and the Deployment is never\ntouched** — the live billing pod\n  keeps running its current spec.\n- PostSync would deadlock the other way round: Deployment applied first,\nthen\n`CreateContainerConfigError` waiting on a Secret nothing has created\nyet.\n\nA render-time assertion (`billing.assertAuthzCredentialSource`, the same\nidiom as\n`authentik.yaml`''s `assertOidcSecret`) rejects\nflag-on-without-a-credential-source before anything\nis applied, with `authz.externallyProvisioned` as the escape hatch.\nAsserted in the template rather\nthan as a new CI gate so it cannot drift from the thing it protects —\nand so this PR does not claim\na gate that does not exist.\n\nA **capability probe** in the Job handles the one real coupling: this\nchart pins\n`backend.image.tag`, and `release.yml` rewrites that tag in a *separate*\ncommit, so Argo can briefly\nsync these templates against a backend image built before\n`--write-env-file` existed. The old CLI\nignores an unknown trailing flag and writes nothing, which would surface\nas a confusing\n`ENV_FILE is missing`. The probe names the real cause instead; either\nway the sync aborts untouched\nand the next one succeeds.\n\n## 🚨 Blast radius — this turns a flag ON for a LIVE payments service\n\nWorst case is **not** an outage, by construction:\n\n| Failure | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Provisioning Job fails | Sync aborts, Deployment untouched, live pod\nunaffected |\n| Credentials wrong/absent | `getMachineToken()` throws →\n`syncPlanToPermit()` catches → returns `false`. The Stripe webhook still\nreturns 200, so **Stripe does not retry**. The DB mirror\n(`billingProjection`, off Kafka) is independent of this path and keeps\nupdating. |\n| Need to revert | `billingService.authz.enabled: false` — one line, one\nsync. Also restores `optional: true` automatically. |\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\nMeasured on a **committed** tree with `git status` clean (0 tracked\nmodifications).\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `helm lint` | 3 overlays, **0 failed** |\n| `helm template` | all 3 overlays render. `values-local`''s failure\nreproduces **identically on clean master** — pre-existing, not mine |\n| `kubeconform --strict` (CI''s exact invocation) | values **45 valid**,\nvalues-local **52**, values-prod **86** — **0 Invalid, 0 Errors** on all\nthree |\n| Render-time assertion | fires on flag-on + register-off; escape hatch\nrenders; prod renders |\n| Prod render diff | exactly the intended delta — flag env,\n`billing-s2s-credentials`, `optional: false`, and the Job + its\nSA/Role/RoleBinding. Nothing else moved. |\n| New unit tests | **13 passed** — `parseArgs`,\n`writeCredentialsEnvFile` (0600 mode, empty/newline refusal, no partial\nfile left behind) |\n| Capability probe | probed **both** CLI versions: this branch''s usage\nadvertises the flag, master''s does not |\n| `billing-service` | `tsc --noEmit` **clean**; jest **289 passed** |\n| `billing-service` pre-existing failures | 3 suites\n(`subscription.service`, `invoice-synced`, `org-deleted.handler`) fail\n**byte-identically on clean master** — same counts, same suites.\nPre-existing. |\n| Existing S2S tests | **12 passed**, no regression |\n| Line endings | LF on every touched file |\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n- [x] Integration tests (chart render + schema validation)\n- [ ] E2E tests — not applicable\n- [x] Manual testing (probe executed against both CLI builds)\n\n**Test Configuration:** Node 24.x · Helm v4.2.4 · kubeconform v0.6.7\n(k8s 1.29 schemas) · PostgreSQL 16\n\n### Not run locally, and why\n\n`deploy/scripts/check-job-interpreters.sh` needs a Docker **daemon**\nthis environment lacks (the\nCLI alone is not enough, and the script hard-errors rather than skipping\n— correctly). Verified by\nreading it instead: it **SKIPs** `ghcr.io/izzywdev/*` images (line 150,\nfirst-party), and the only\nother image in the new Job, `alpine/k8s:1.36.2`, is already probed in\nthe same rendered output via\nthe existing `consumer-registration-seed` Job. Both of the new Job''s\ncontainers invoke `/bin/sh -c`\nand both bases provide it (`node:24-alpine`, `alpine/k8s`).\n\n## 📋 Checklist\n\n- [x] Self-review of code completed\n- [x] Code is commented, particularly in hard-to-understand areas — each\nnon-obvious choice carries\n      the reasoning *and* the rejected alternative\n- [x] No secret value is read, printed, fabricated or committed\n- [x] TypeScript strict mode passes\n- [x] Authentication/authorization properly handled — the `authz:admin`\nscope is granted at\nregistration; the Job''s SA holds only `create` on secrets plus\n`get/patch/update` on the one\n      Secret it manages\n- [x] Code follows conventional commit format\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n\n- [x] **Requires configuration changes** — this PR *is* the\nconfiguration change. Merging it is the\n      cutover, because `master` is deploy-on-push.\n- [ ] Requires database migration — no\n- [ ] Requires dependency updates — no\n\n### Future Work\n\n- Retire the flag per `authz.flags.ts`''s own removal criterion: after\nthe Security-API-backed sync\nhas run clean in prod for ≥ 2 sprints, delete the flag and the dead\nOFF-path rather than leaving a\n  permanent toggle.\n- The runbook now documents the Job as the reference implementation for\nthe next **in-namespace**\nS2S consumer; the manual recipe remains for out-of-namespace consumers,\nwhere the credential\n  genuinely has to cross a boundary.\n\n### Questions for Reviewers\n\n- The flag flip (`values-prod.yaml`) is in the **same PR** as the\nplumbing. That is deliberate — the\nPreSync ordering makes it atomic and fail-safe, so splitting it would\nadd a deploy window without\nadding safety. Say the word if you would rather land the plumbing first\nand flip separately; it is\n  a two-line split.\n- `register-s2s-cli.ts` keeps its run-on-import `main()`; the testable\nhelpers moved to\n`s2s-credentials-file.ts` so a unit test cannot trigger a real Authentik\nregistration as an import\n  side effect.\n\n## 🔗 Related Issues and PRs\n\n- Completes #1053 (billing off the embedded Permit SDK), which shipped\nthis dark\n- Builds on #1042 (the Security API''s subject-attribute-write contract)\n- Follows #648''s S2S foundation\n(`docs/runbooks/s2s-client-credentials.md`)\n- No overlap with open PRs: #1269 touches selection-list-service only (0\nbilling files); #1240\n  touches different regions of the same values files\n\n## 🔄 Backwards Compatibility\n\n- [x] Fully backwards compatible. Default values keep `authz.enabled:\nfalse` and\n`register.enabled: false`, so every non-prod overlay renders exactly as\nbefore apart from one\nadded env var set to `\"false\"`. Verified by diffing the rendered output.\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0183JMAkioT5pGt8aVmddPtc\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f51c6b50b7a0be2c53a49393f325a030f8210d66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/f51c6b50b7a0be2c53a49393f325a030f8210d66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/c77ec8c70153c18ec48e3065d1aa057cbc5ec1dc","verification":{"payload":"tree f51c6b50b7a0be2c53a49393f325a030f8210d66\nparent 739e8287a95cfa83ec30db1571ec2e6aaf356441\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791184856 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791184856 +0000\n\nfeat(billing): automate the authz cutover and turn it on in production (#1272)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nCompletes billing-service''s migration off the embedded Permit SDK\n(#1053) by **automating the\nproduction cutover