ve ids schema, owner grants on seeded lists, org.updated consumer, canonical flag context (SL8) (#1289)\n\nD1 bodies reject undeclared properties; D2 resolve enforces ids schema (ids [] is now 400 per minItems 1) and limit validated on paginated GETs; G1 platform-seeded lists grant list-owner to the org owner after the seed commits (idempotent, retried, never re-grants a revoked owner; migration 000010); G2 identity.org.updated consumer; G3 canonical TypeID flag context; G4 service port 3008. All it.failing pins removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwty+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8voQABnxsMj2HbNDyE2wcYjU/n9h\nZswfquXaCLOFigGTXvO/xUwDUfttU+VRYY6445B8LqiPduoy8kuqVfhpWkguGhPq\nfSZo9ZsxvKIolyEZGyQSdD5l/ir3MaPEUYC4Lmsm7MTJnUYEuDyKENQRHrLDWANV\n1YKY6io/xj/I5dxMewNJD+fiH7PD386/OouDuA6+MUA67AIo2gajlIUAOBe817k/\no2ph31Lq1z+rLDmEG8uk0ljPNexIs8OfbUDlkvKtg+L6cnEBPuDlvZm/zJtFtf3N\nIlhLHMlW7BqYF0PkFcaR69iNzA4PTT4fy7ny2Ahnt0A1U+DeB9EtO1ZvYqTguKKQ\n97eq4gQYIZrGyxCiwiGRDQfYFM1Ai2FLIG9OxLGgoTgCmitsbCscu6GegwA8XoXW\n1yUmaxTDfAY8q/+sA24UqSejxfrfaPodV5Ug6Fj42M+QDbRZcqHx5DHJLoCeTvFA\nbXZ+RHyV94dew0R3x2u78ilsgL4KzZ678PF6LOlHMDoIm5tTO3QZm9DJsM672u2p\nrnfNXWquolzqLTYPSmlTcQmFLyrgBEuB/7sbfPFBC6gXivccxmXoI7V0Bn1tDRfp\nf40IM4+o+My4bcvcYf+WrMEvbEOMi44eC3wiPBPgITj2uHtGLxDGDsBww6ru+sBP\necy/P32JVfYN/COt3aBn\n=+3Oc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T23:09:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/37ed4c5e80b52d99e9060fa2031da43013f7df22","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDM3ZWQ0YzVlODBiNTJkOTllOTA2MGZhMjAzMWRhNDMwMTNmN2RmMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/58360b34ba7eaf8389313632a50189331a131ace","sha":"58360b34ba7eaf8389313632a50189331a131ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/58360b34ba7eaf8389313632a50189331a131ace"}],"sha":"37ed4c5e80b52d99e9060fa2031da43013f7df22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/37ed4c5e80b52d99e9060fa2031da43013f7df22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/58360b34ba7eaf8389313632a50189331a131ace/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:03:16Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:03:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(identity): publish org membership add/remove events + downstream ReBAC seeding (#1284)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nPublish a domain event whenever a user is added to / removed from an\norganization (`identity.membership.added` /\n`identity.membership.removed`), so downstream services seed user-org\ndata + initial ReBAC policies off one source of truth. Design of record:\n`docs/planning/org-membership-events.md`.\n\nThe event **contract already existed** in `@fuzefront/shared/kafka`\n(topics + `membershipChangeSchemaV1 = {organizationId, userId, role}` +\nregistry); this PR wires the publishers and the reconcile consumer. No\nshared-schema change → no breaking version bump.\n\n### Publisher (transactional outbox, per the data-consistency standard)\n`enqueueEvent(trx, …)` **inside the write transaction** at the live-prod\nwriter of each op (ingress: `/api/organizations` → security,\n`/api/invitations` → monolith), via a DRY `emitMembershipAdded/Removed`\nhelper. Org-create already emitted `added` (precedent). Added emits at:\npersonal-org provisioning (+ self-heal), `ensureRootMembership`,\n`ensureDeveloperMembership`, invite-accept (monolith); removed at\n`DELETE /:id/members/:memberId`. **Idempotency:** provisioning upserts\nrun every login, so each emit is gated on an actual row insert\n(`.returning(''id'')`) — no spurious `added` on repeat sign-in.\n\n### Consumer — ReBAC reconcile\n`provisioning-service` consumes both topics → new S2S `POST\n/internal/membership-sync|unsync` (same `INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET`\nguard as the sibling `/internal/*`) →\n`assignOrganizationRole`/`unassignOrganizationRole` (maps membership\nrole → Permit tenant role). Non-2xx on Permit failure so the consumer\nretries then DLQs; replay-safe (Permit assign is idempotent). Satisfies\n`gate-microservice-events` anti-vacuity (real outbound write).\n\n### Scope decision — no per-service \"seed on membership\" handlers\nA tenant role applies to every instance in the tenant, so the reconcile\nabove gives a new member correct access to downstream org-scoped\nresources centrally. Audited: `selection-list-service` (tenant-role\ngoverned; its per-list grants are explicit admin actions),\n`config-service` (no per-(user,org) data), ref-index (projects entity\nexistence, not edges). Adding handlers there would be vacuous. Rationale\nin the design doc.\n\n### Deploy-safety\n- Monolith `@fuzefront/core` dependency added **and packaged** in\n`backend/Dockerfile` (copy `backend/core/package.json` pre-install,\nbuild it, copy `dist`) — mirrors the proven security-service pattern;\nprevents the #538 \"Cannot find module\" boot crash.\n`image-reproducibility` builds it on this PR.\n- `/internal/membership-*` added to `governance/openapi-exempt.txt`\n(like the sibling `/internal/*`), so `gate-openapi-conformance` passes.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n- [x] ✨ Feature — event publication + ReBAC reconcile consumer\n- [x] 📝 Docs — design doc + #1095 post-deploy runbook\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- [x] Publisher: 14+ unit tests (emit on real insert; **no** emit on\nrepeat-login/lost-race/existing/absent-root; no emit on 404/owner-403\ndelete).\n- [x] Consumer: security `/internal/membership-*` route tests (34) +\nprovisioning-service handler tests (ADDED→sync, REMOVED→unsync, 5xx\nretried-then-thrown, 4xx thrown, replay).\n- [x] `tsc` clean; `gate-microservice-events`,\n`gate-openapi-conformance`, `In-repo packages resolve from source`, `npm\nci --dry-run` all green locally. `@fuzefront/core` build verified.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_017zdYnxKQVVhFyRubDa1BmK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"98e3db92b489fff51ec83611af9e87605e449328","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/98e3db92b489fff51ec83611af9e87605e449328"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/58360b34ba7eaf8389313632a50189331a131ace","verification":{"payload":"tree 98e3db92b489fff51ec83611af9e87605e449328\nparent 3057920bdb852cae00843fa3fb98a042b051ab51\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791154996 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791154996 +0300\n\nfeat(identity): publish org membership add/remove events + downstream ReBAC seeding (#1284)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nPublish a domain event whenever a user is added to / removed from an\norganization (`identity.membership.added` /\n`identity.membership.removed`), so downstream services seed user-org\ndata + initial ReBAC policies off one source of truth. Design of record:\n`docs/planning/org-membership-events.md`.\n\nThe event **contract already existed** in `@fuzefront/shared/kafka`\n(topics + `membershipChangeSchemaV1 = {organizationId, userId, role}` +\nregistry); this PR wires the publishers and the reconcile consumer. No\nshared-schema change → no breaking version bump.\n\n### Publisher (transactional outbox, per the data-consistency standard)\n`enqueueEvent(trx, …)` **inside the write transaction** at the live-prod\nwriter of each op (ingress: `/api/organizations` → security,\n`/api/invitations` → monolith), via a DRY `emitMembershipAdded/Removed`\nhelper. Org-create already emitted `added` (precedent). Added emits at:\npersonal-org provisioning (+ self-heal), `ensureRootMembership`,\n`ensureDeveloperMembership`, invite-accept (monolith); removed at\n`DELETE /:id/members/:memberId`. **Idempotency:** provisioning upserts\nrun every login, so each emit is gated on an actual row insert\n(`.returning(''id'')`) — no spurious `added` on repeat sign-in.\n\n### Consumer — ReBAC reconcile\n`provisioning-service` consumes both topics → new S2S `POST\n/internal/membership-sync|unsync` (same `INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET`\nguard as the sibling `/internal/*`) →\n`assignOrganizationRole`/`unassignOrganizationRole` (maps membership\nrole → Permit tenant role). Non-2xx on Permit failure so the consumer\nretries then DLQs; replay-safe (Permit assign is idempotent). Satisfies\n`gate-microservice-events` anti-vacuity (real outbound write).\n\n### Scope decision — no per-service \"seed on membership\" handlers\nA tenant role applies to every instance in the tenant, so the reconcile\nabove gives a new member correct access to downstream org-scoped\nresources centrally. Audited: `selection-list-service` (tenant-role\ngoverned; its per-list grants are explicit admin actions),\n`config-service` (no per-(user,org) data), ref-index (projects entity\nexistence, not edges). Adding handlers there would be vacuous. Rationale\nin the design doc.\n\n### Deploy-safety\n- Monolith `@fuzefront/core` dependency added **and packaged** in\n`backend/Dockerfile` (copy `backend/core/package.json` pre-install,\nbuild it, copy `dist`) — mirrors the proven security-service pattern;\nprevents the #538 \"Cannot find module\" boot crash.\n`image-reproducibility` builds it on this PR.\n- `/internal/membership-*` added to `governance/openapi-exempt.txt`\n(like the sibling `/internal/*`), so `gate-openapi-conformance` passes.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n- [x] ✨ Feature — event publication + ReBAC reconcile consumer\n- [x] 📝 Docs — design doc + #1095 post-deploy runbook\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- [x] Publisher: 14+ unit tests (emit on real insert; **no** emit on\nrepeat-login/lost-race/existing/absent-root; no emit on 404/owner-403\ndelete).\n- [x] Consumer: security `/internal/membership-*` route tests (34) +\nprovisioning-service handler tests (ADDED→sync, REMOVED→unsync, 5xx\nretried-then-thrown, 4xx thrown, replay).\n- [x] `tsc` clean; `gate-microservice-events`,\n`gate-openapi-conformance`, `In-repo packages resolve from source`, `npm\nci --dry-run` all green locally. `@fuzefront/core` build verified.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_017zdYnxKQVVhFyRubDa1BmK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwts0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbDwQAD+DNGhD79OY21LJNosd6ds6\nug7AqDTtaAmvg6F141rUuciKvqlheixx3+OSoV/wJ/ceg/VvM2YQUPM5jfuuIuoK\nuOwcJveJNCTRQfzvZsgBsdjzxGKJ6t38D2iv9VarfDsSpeD067y9YtoE4uuGHKzn\nnMW+DGVN7uTwE9XFw9Cm46RDo1/BwWRJSKMw08t9E689IzwT8CIrd9rmkt/cqU1y\nfzNTWI90qaTsbNR3i1J/+aJtfxyV0DqeDKMmRL8WdPVeHykBaD1tCmv5AItwvYwi\nawmLuugW86CILPGSMoDwIj8bpUIrtttdlKlH2QcJ7CSKCGn06I7Xm9X5gBtFxCGW\nTlg1sa9nOvIrD3T/+cdm/3ecAMcQwySc4fFfS8XI/1VIh/gtrzz2sUdG5PAJztQs\njhjpF3mG7G0fz1WHMqXgrAa28BxLSxVcHD2eQKwSTXaS7XP8WUI3ENxNAUJmu0Yo\nAnrDjYa2OIw/2FwILRi7pdIO1qTi/3JNweBM1IVg2fj/W4VpYLo+JMMFeuixsWK3\nh/uBgPSnG+rVun8zOSDSco5jcZKAABO0COhsxiOKlYdiqTgDiyDHQn+8NXaemrF8\nGY6pzjnZ5gnk34DiA4MCAWjHrzRbptzMvO6yLG2JLRtULFzaPTNo/2J/SpowqKbA\nWZdgy2e5k84rKWR/ZK2S\n=xEPx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T23:03:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/org