repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/56009bc3c8ee0034741173908abd6e4dcd4e790b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/00c493b684713cf5edea3ef14fa9652d290fd9ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/00c493b684713cf5edea3ef14fa9652d290fd9ad","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDAwYzQ5M2I2ODQ3MTNjZjVlZGVhM2VmMTRmYTk2NTJkMjkwZmQ5YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98","sha":"60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98"}],"sha":"00c493b684713cf5edea3ef14fa9652d290fd9ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/00c493b684713cf5edea3ef14fa9652d290fd9ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fuze-agent","id":321521006,"login":"fuze-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEyoFbg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:36:48Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:36:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(app-registry): build-with-agent sessions, creator ownership, marketplace publishing (flagged OFF) (#1261)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nThis PR adds the backend, contract and flag wiring for three\ncapabilities:\n\n- **\"Build your application\":** starts a FuzeAgent session that builds\nan app and deploys it into the user''s personal workspace or the current\norg.\n- **Ownership:** the org owns the app and the user who created it is\nrecorded as its creator. The creator''s authority is a Permit role scoped\nto the org, so it ends when they leave. The app stays with the org.\n- **Marketplace publishing:** a submit/approve flow for listing an app\nin the marketplace.\n\nPlan of record: `docs/planning/app-builder-and-ownership.md`.\n\nEach capability has its own release flag. All three default OFF:\n`fuzefront.apps.build-with-agent`, `fuzefront.apps.creator-ownership`,\n`fuzefront.apps.marketplace-publishing`.\n\n**There is no UI in this PR.** `frontend/src/pages/ApplicationsPage.tsx`\nis covered by the unapproved `app-management` frames, so\n`gate-frames-first` blocks the card until a frames-only PR\n(`design/frames/app-builder/`) is approved.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n- [x] Integration tests (real Postgres: the migration chain including\n018, plus the build-session store)\n\n- `backend/applications` jest: 24 suites, 302 tests pass. Both flag\nstates are covered for every gated endpoint.\n- Gates that pass: `gate_identifier.py` (including `--registry-parity`),\n`gate_openapi_conformance.py`, `check-route-ownership.mjs`,\n`gate-toolchain.mjs`, spectral, `packages/identity` jest (74),\nidentity-py pytest (66).\n- Failures that predate this PR:\n- `packages/feature-flags`: 1 test fails because of the existing\n`org-context-disabled` default of true, and 2 suites fail on type errors\nin their own test files.\n- `gate_platform_auth.py`: flags every `authenticateConsumerOrSession`\nroute, existing ones included.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n- **Backend Changes:**\n- **Migration 018:** adds `apps.created_by_user_id` (FK users, ON DELETE\nSET NULL) and the `app_build_sessions` table. Each session is pinned to\na single org.\n- **`/api/v1/app-registry/build-sessions`:** create, list (paginated),\nget and cancel.\n- The FuzeAgent status callback is for the service identity only. States\nonly move forward.\n- A `deployed` report for an app in a different org is rejected with\n409.\n    - A caller who isn''t entitled to a session gets 404.\n- If the launcher isn''t configured, the endpoint returns 503\n`builder_unavailable` and saves nothing.\n- **`FuzeAgentHttpLauncher`:** has a DI seam and boundary logging, and\nnever logs its token.\n  - **Creator ownership:**\n- The creator is set by the server only. It is never accepted from the\nrequest body, never changed by PUT, and `canMutate` never reads it.\n- The App DTO gains `createdBy` and `creator{isCurrentMember}`. A former\nmember gets no contact details.\n- The Permit `App#creator` role is granted best-effort; a failed grant\nis logged and registration continues.\n- **Publication:** submit, approve, reject and get. Approve and reject\nare platform-admin only. These wire up the existing marketplace columns.\n- **Contracts:**\n- app-registry OpenAPI goes from 1.1.0 to 1.2.0 with 9 new operations.\nThe Helm copy stays byte-identical.\n- New identity prefix `appBuildSession = front_abs`, added in both TS\nand Python.\n- `@izzywdev/fuzefront-identity` bumped to 1.1.0 and\n`@fuzefront/feature-flags` to 1.2.0.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n- [x] Requires database migration (018, idempotent)\n- [x] Requires environment variable changes, only when the build flag is\nturned on: `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_URL`, `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_TOKEN`\n(SealedSecret), `APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`\n- [x] Requires configuration changes:\n  - Create the three flags in Unleash.\n  - Define `App#creator` in Permit.\n- Before enabling `creator-ownership` in prod, verify that Permit drops\ninstance roles when a member is removed from the tenant.\n\n### Future Work\n1. Frames PR for `design/frames/app-builder/` (product-designer).\n2. UI: the card, the build flow, the creator block and the publish\naction (frontend-engineer), after the frames are approved.\n3. The FuzeAgent build endpoint and status callback (cross-repo).\n4. Quotas and billing for agent compute.\n5. Cancelling a session should also notify FuzeAgent.\n\n## 🔄 Backwards Compatibility\n\n- [x] Fully backwards compatible. With every flag OFF, DTOs and existing\nroutes behave exactly as before.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01HJeisvuB8eV9CR2m8XK8Be\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fef3fcb831629452af0c17e8491e0fc0ac2b1b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/fef3fcb831629452af0c17e8491e0fc0ac2b1b0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98","verification":{"payload":"tree fef3fcb831629452af0c17e8491e0fc0ac2b1b0c\nparent 58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791142608 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791142608 +0300\n\nfeat(app-registry): build-with-agent sessions, creator ownership, marketplace publishing (flagged OFF) (#1261)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nThis PR adds the backend, contract and flag wiring for three\ncapabilities:\n\n- **\"Build your application\":** starts a FuzeAgent session that builds\nan app and deploys it into the user''s personal workspace or the current\norg.\n- **Ownership:** the org owns the app and the user who created it is\nrecorded as its creator. The creator''s authority is a Permit role scoped\nto the org, so it ends when they leave. The app stays with the org.\n- **Marketplace publishing:** a submit/approve flow for listing an app\nin the marketplace.\n\nPlan of record: `docs/planning/app-builder-and-ownership.md`.\n\nEach capability has its own release flag. All three default OFF:\n`fuzefront.apps.build-with-agent`, `fuzefront.apps.creator-ownership`,\n`fuzefront.apps.marketplace-publishing`.\n\n**There is no UI in this PR.** `frontend/src/pages/ApplicationsPage.tsx`\nis covered by the unapproved `app-management` frames, so\n`gate-frames-first` blocks the card until a frames-only PR\n(`design/frames/app-builder/`) is approved.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n- [x] Integration tests (real Postgres: the migration chain including\n018, plus the build-session store)\n\n- `backend/applications` jest: 24 suites, 302 tests pass. Both flag\nstates are covered for every gated endpoint.\n- Gates that pass: `gate_identifier.py` (including `--registry-parity`),\n`gate_openapi_conformance.py`, `check-route-ownership.mjs`,\n`gate-toolchain.mjs`, spectral, `packages/identity` jest (74),\nidentity-py pytest (66).\n- Failures that predate this PR:\n- `packages/feature-flags`: 1 test fails because of the existing\n`org-context-disabled` default of true, and 2 suites fail on type errors\nin their own test files.\n- `gate_platform_auth.py`: flags every `authenticateConsumerOrSession`\nroute, existing ones included.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n- **Backend Changes:**\n- **Migration 018:** adds `apps.created_by_user_id` (FK users, ON DELETE\nSET NULL) and the `app_build_sessions` table. Each session is pinned to\na single org.\n- **`/api/v1/app-registry/build-sessions`:** create, list (paginated),\nget and cancel.\n- The FuzeAgent status callback is for the service identity only. States\nonly move forward.\n- A `deployed` report for an app in a different org is rejected with\n409.\n    - A caller who isn''t entitled to a session gets 404.\n- If the launcher isn''t configured, the endpoint returns 503\n`builder_unavailable` and saves nothing.\n- **`FuzeAgentHttpLauncher`:** has a DI seam and boundary logging, and\nnever logs its token.\n  - **Creator ownership:**\n- The creator is set by the server only. It is never accepted from the\nrequest body, never changed by PUT, and `canMutate` never reads it.\n- The App DTO gains `createdBy` and `creator{isCurrentMember}`. A former\nmember gets no contact details.\n- The Permit `App#creator` role is granted best-effort; a failed grant\nis logged and registration continues.\n- **Publication:** submit, approve, reject and get. Approve and reject\nare platform-admin only. These wire up the existing marketplace columns.\n- **Contracts:**\n- app-registry OpenAPI goes from 1.1.0 to 1.2.0 with 9 new operations.\nThe Helm copy stays byte-identical.\n- New identity prefix `appBuildSession = front_abs`, added in both TS\nand Python.\n- `@izzywdev/fuzefront-identity` bumped to 1.1.0 and\n`@fuzefront/feature-flags` to 1.2.0.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n- [x] Requires database migration (018, idempotent)\n- [x] Requires environment variable changes, only when the build flag is\nturned on: `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_URL`, `FUZEAGENT_BUILD_API_TOKEN`\n(SealedSecret), `APP_REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`\n- [x] Requires configuration changes:\n  - Create the three flags in Unleash.\n  - Define `App#creator` in Permit.\n- Before enabling `creator-ownership` in prod, verify that Permit drops\ninstance roles when a member is removed from the tenant.\n\n### Future Work\n1. Frames PR for `design/frames/app-builder/` (product-designer).\n2. UI: the card, the build flow, the creator block and the publish\naction (frontend-engineer), after the frames are approved.\n3. The FuzeAgent build endpoint and status callback (cross-repo).\n4. Quotas and billing for agent compute.\n5. Cancelling a session should also notify FuzeAgent.\n\n## 🔄 Backwards Compatibility\n\n- [x] Fully backwards compatible. With every flag OFF, DTOs and existing\nroutes behave exactly as before.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01HJeisvuB8eV9CR2m8XK8Be\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwqrQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkmEQAFbuPYvvaO8EWT5MBFMMmGam\nV0wtg7w92PIOPT6F85owvQGFCTPQWC3KMPZ15tXp2ABcBLtOZ3ZFV7OrDP5bfFqu\nhfa3qD96MaPvlOrmnOsu3FPWfcxll6xCgQ6GZo61rzz90ZRyYF4UklWgNIYdYspV\nT3nolLIoF/vBjrIzzY9tjEGPu04ypm3Rgu+Y8+10v7niPFaKUKaEDwS40PSe70QL\nuWuZd2mTuZvvoRTcN/cABRZqnCULnjJMdQ6imtV4uBJvJu2gjQPsoM8+gLX6Iv00\nJczPi1St7gc2xZxl1+gGKu3uriH5HiJMrdH8OoM0PRKPqhPGWvhn8ejSTi1Rs3Cj\ns6xg3zlyCoR6uJrWA6jwdpLCgQUy+iZxuo7abWkUdMh4tOVAYSvP93wBlHPj8YMD\nRiw61ukf6mmx1wq/ZmIKcCK1I4ULrgAxFolWqzSCdlV3ZrDnIIBlzy0fF44GjMAr\nIIgu0M99P5cNIvUkO7uOqqaEHGYBxFQNalUasnagVTUJL3TzUrmWBz8mzC+EIrKI\nGP/HivwEeDTHPcoHGN6oY7/kpmF1zTix4fv/mr7nJT60tk8Y6FX7LfX18FxjSdiJ\nU7tjaGXDn4iTgnpfI47AM81qO2bKqht5nVWTKr7QVH1YD3GR4pE6cmTZBYqvM4An\nMU9am6tr1jASI/QxLzcw\n=6zCN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T19:36:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDYwYzdmM2M3YTMwMDViOGViZjAzNmFiNTVjMjU1NmRlNTgyZTFhOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df","sha":"58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df"}],"sha":"60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/60c7f3c7a3005b8ebf036ab55c2556de582e1a98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98424459?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shlomiNugarker","id":98424459,"login":"shlomiNugarker","node_id":"U_kgDOBd3Wiw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shlomiNugarker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:30:25Z","email":"98424459+shlomiNugarker@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Shlomi Nugarker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:30:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: Fix the local quickstart and Windows e2e startup (#1018) (#1205)\n\n## Description\n\nOn a fresh Windows clone the documented quickstart cannot run: its\ncommands don''t exist, and the e2e stack dies before postgres starts.\nThis PR fixes the Windows blocker and rewrites the quickstart around the\nstack CI already runs.\n\nCloses #1018\n\n### What was broken\n\n- **Quickstart / README \"Quick Demo\":** `npm run install:all`,\n`db:init`, `db:seed` and `demo` don''t exist in `package.json`.\n- **e2e stack on Windows:** `.gitattributes` has no rule for `*.sh`, so\nwith Git for Windows'' default `core.autocrlf=true` every script checks\nout as CRLF. Postgres runs `deploy/e2e/init-postgres.sh` from\n`/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d` and exits 127 with `env: can''t execute\n''bash\\r''`. Nothing else starts.\n- **No doc** says which URL to open, how to sign in, or how to get\n`clock-app` into the shell.\n\n### What this PR does\n\n- **`fix(build)`** — add `*.sh text eol=lf` to `.gitattributes` and\nrenormalize the 4 scripts already stored as CRLF. Line endings only;\n`git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` shows no content change.\n- **`docs(build)`** — quickstart path 1 now uses\n`docker-compose.e2e.yml`: start, what \"healthy\" looks like, sign-up\n(with the password policy), and building/serving/registering `clock-app`\nthe way `.github/workflows/e2e.yml` does, in bash and PowerShell. Adds\nWindows troubleshooting. README \"Quick Demo\" links there instead of\nduplicating it.\n\n## Testing\n\nManual, on Windows 11 · PowerShell 5.1 · Git 2.48.1 (default\n`core.autocrlf=true`) · Node 24.21.0 · Docker Desktop 28.0.1.\n\n1. **Before:** fresh clone → `docker compose -f docker-compose.e2e.yml\nup -d --build` → postgres `exited (127)`.\n2. **After**, same Git defaults: `deploy/e2e/*.sh` check out as `w/lf`,\npostgres `(healthy)`.\n3. Followed the new quickstart end to end from `down -v`: sign-up worked\nfirst try, Clock mounted inside the shell (\"Mounted inside FuzeFront:\nyes\").\n\n## Questions for reviewers\n\nLeft out of this PR on purpose — they need your call:\n\n1. **Is `docker-compose.yml` (`npm run docker:up`) still a supported dev\npath?** `npm run dev` points to it. It needs an undocumented `.env`,\nthen the build fails: `build.context` is `./backend` /\n`./services/payment-service` while both Dockerfiles expect the repo root\n(every other build of them uses `.`). I can fix it or drop the hint —\nwhichever you prefer.\n2. **Quickstart path 2 (Kubernetes)** uses `docker build … ./backend` —\nlooks like the same context problem. Not verified, so not touched.\n3. **`CONTRIBUTING.md` \"Local Development Setup\"** has the same gaps\n(`npm run dev` only prints a hint; clock-app step misses `npm install`,\nwrong URL, dev server never registers). Should it link to the quickstart\nlike the README now does?\n\n## Found along the way (not Windows-specific — separate issues?)\n\n- Sign-up shows \"Incorrect email or password\" when Authentik rejects the\npassword policy; the rule isn''t shown on the form.\n- Dashboard hides platform-owned apps while the sidebar shows them:\n`isAppVisibleForOrg` treats only `null` as global, but migration 026\ndefaults `organization_id` to the root org. Still the case after #1188.\n- `window.__FUZEFRONT__` gives remotes an empty apps list (\"Apps known\nto host: 0\").\n- Every dashboard load toasts `Unexpected token ''<'', \"<!doctype \"... is\nnot valid JSON`.\n- Dashboard greets \"User\" instead of the first name entered at sign-up.\n- `clock-app/dist/` isn''t gitignored; `clock-app/.npmrc` uses\n`always-auth` (npm 11 warns); `docs/setup/README-SETUP.md` still lists\n`admin@fuzefront.dev / admin123`, which doesn''t exist in the Authentik\nstack.","tree":{"sha":"f665aaade30396ba4d5413e898c7ffe724a73ac4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/f665aaade30396ba4d5413e898c7ffe724a73ac4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df","verification":{"payload":"tree f665aaade30396ba4d5413e898c7ffe724a73ac4\nparent b6dcd40f8575d80fa6f7ec3eb97cbabcbd8f495f\nauthor Shlomi Nugarker <98424459+shlomiNugarker@users.noreply.github.com> 1791142225 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791142225 +0300\n\ndocs: Fix the local quickstart and Windows e2e startup (#1018) (#1205)\n\n## Description\n\nOn a fresh Windows clone the documented quickstart cannot run: its\ncommands don''t exist, and the e2e stack dies before postgres starts.\nThis PR fixes the Windows blocker and rewrites the quickstart around the\nstack CI already runs.\n\nCloses #1018\n\n### What was broken\n\n- **Quickstart / README \"Quick Demo\":** `npm run install:all`,\n`db:init`, `db:seed` and `demo` don''t exist in `package.json`.\n- **e2e stack on Windows:** `.gitattributes` has no rule for `*.sh`, so\nwith Git for Windows'' default `core.autocrlf=true` every script checks\nout as CRLF. Postgres runs `deploy/e2e/init-postgres.sh` from\n`/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d` and exits 127 with `env: can''t execute\n''bash\\r''`. Nothing else starts.\n- **No doc** says which URL to open, how to sign in, or how to get\n`clock-app` into the shell.\n\n### What this PR does\n\n- **`fix(build)`** — add `*.sh text eol=lf` to `.gitattributes` and\nrenormalize the 4 scripts already stored as CRLF. Line endings only;\n`git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` shows no content change.\n- **`docs(build)`** — quickstart path 1 now uses\n`docker-compose.e2e.yml`: start, what \"healthy\" looks like, sign-up\n(with the password policy), and building/serving/registering `clock-app`\nthe way `.github/workflows/e2e.yml` does, in bash and PowerShell. Adds\nWindows troubleshooting. README \"Quick Demo\" links there instead of\nduplicating it.\n\n## Testing\n\nManual, on Windows 11 · PowerShell 5.1 · Git 2.48.1 (default\n`core.autocrlf=true`) · Node 24.21.0 · Docker Desktop 28.0.1.\n\n1. **Before:** fresh clone → `docker compose -f docker-compose.e2e.yml\nup -d --build` → postgres `exited (127)`.\n2. **After**, same Git defaults: `deploy/e2e/*.sh` check out as `w/lf`,\npostgres `(healthy)`.\n3. Followed the new quickstart end to end from `down -v`: sign-up worked\nfirst try, Clock mounted inside the shell (\"Mounted inside FuzeFront:\nyes\").\n\n## Questions for reviewers\n\nLeft out of this PR on purpose — they need your call:\n\n1. **Is `docker-compose.yml` (`npm run docker:up`) still a supported dev\npath?** `npm run dev` points to it. It needs an undocumented `.env`,\nthen the build fails: `build.context` is `./backend` /\n`./services/payment-service` while both Dockerfiles expect the repo root\n(every other build of them uses `.`). I can fix it or drop the hint —\nwhichever you prefer.\n2. **Quickstart path 2 (Kubernetes)** uses `docker build … ./backend` —\nlooks like the same context problem. Not verified, so not touched.\n3. **`CONTRIBUTING.md` \"Local Development Setup\"** has the same gaps\n(`npm run dev` only prints a hint; clock-app step misses `npm install`,\nwrong URL, dev server never registers). Should it link to the quickstart\nlike the README now does?\n\n## Found along the way (not Windows-specific — separate issues?)\n\n- Sign-up shows \"Incorrect email or password\" when Authentik rejects the\npassword policy; the rule isn''t shown on the form.\n- Dashboard hides platform-owned apps while the sidebar shows them:\n`isAppVisibleForOrg` treats only `null` as global, but migration 026\ndefaults `organization_id` to the root org. Still the case after #1188.\n- `window.__FUZEFRONT__` gives remotes an empty apps list (\"Apps known\nto host: 0\").\n- Every dashboard load toasts `Unexpected token ''<'', \"<!doctype \"... is\nnot valid JSON`.\n- Dashboard greets \"User\" instead of the first name entered at sign-up.\n- `clock-app/dist/` isn''t gitignored; `clock-app/.npmrc` uses\n`always-auth` (npm 11 warns); `docs/setup/README-SETUP.md` still lists\n`admin@fuzefront.dev / admin123`, which doesn''t exist in the Authentik\nstack.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwqlRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdJIQAHKT+nvcN3MMSFE3wcJM2gvj\nMP1FdupWn9z82dWcfL1GqR7NRbvw2G0RLI6iqe1mz0TDct/e0v0sSlHBs2xmZuVy\nYNiq4pDNPA9W0MS/JXicmLzNQoXx7LCCgOVgsceIb2CRhVXDXUrYQ7QYP84IJcfT\nk03ajeMMTx1MJTwmAwHg5J6Z3wUXjT4mB17lpNWDHuZpJ84reTBkjOS1ht0RKSGK\n73E/kdye1fM9GFfUGBO6yb4iRpSND9e4t5/yPQJKvjIYI3aAXxzGa8Ek0tsL5Sqx\nGNMRrDon4VzrQ6croxAuWw4pBBXOhNBBfkYrO+BcKhGg4XcnO8gLZWuWoa4Z8row\nQvCVF1rGGPDIjWE3YRiOku/VcalaId4j3w80BYSh5vGXHsstbRXBr8jZsmCgZy2N\nvY+BA0xRKtvDhXlGJiNQFEqFbCOGfO16yTGOrgOAerhdAZYD/zoUEPVjSP5k+Jgl\n8BaZNmVm6+kkE4DXZ/FY56MWoIrOSe7pyxvbAjZIDZ6XiytWBXAfiMwoYOhZe08x\ngcTHp+gYhOkNgdm2RMinNZv4/3dEiUm57aFImr2McHLM2EmQvjD9bRhjw8dit2qW\nb/XB4in7Qap7aJJJSS0NLn8Zb+GtIfUA+HQXffhm+tB2o8n35IVz4PfjejQpNLQ5\nxAidmb7HWYnDegwL540x\n=DV5b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T19:30:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDU4MDcwYjBmYWNmODdjYTE3Yjc0ZjRlNzkyM2FmN2IxOGQ5ODQ5ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/b6dcd40f8575d80fa6f7ec3eb97cbabcbd8f495f","sha":"b6dcd40f8575d80fa6f7ec3eb97cbabcbd8f495f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/b6dcd40f8575d80fa6f7ec3eb97cbabcbd8f495f"}],"sha":"58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/58070b0facf87ca17b74f4e7923af7b18d9849df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","id":198982749,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/b6dcd40f8575d80fa6f7ec3eb97cbabcbd8f495f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:29:57Z","email":"198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:29:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: developers.fuzefront.com Fuze family developer portal — design proposal (#920)\n\nNo unified developer portal exists to discover, read, and try out\nOpenAPI specs published across the Fuze family of repos and their\nmicroservices. This PR adds a design proposal for\n`developers.fuzefront.com`: a home page, shared FuzeFront sign-in,\nroot-org membership with a `Developer` group, an aggregated OpenAPI\ncatalog, and a sandboxed playground. **Plan only — no implementation**,\npending approval.\n\n### Added\n- `docs/planning/developers-portal.md` — full design proposal covering:\n- **Build vs. adopt review**: compares Backstage, Redoc, Docusaurus, and\na FuzeFront-native app; recommends building a lightweight native portal\n+ spec registry using an embedded OSS renderer (Stoplight Elements /\nSwagger UI) over adopting Backstage.\n- **Architecture**: new `devportal-service` (spec registry, harvest job,\nsandbox proxy) + `devportal-frontend` (home, catalog, spec viewer,\nplayground), harvesting `openapi.yaml` contracts from every `providesTo`\nfamily repo.\n- **Identity**: reuse of the existing Authentik OIDC provider; a new,\nadditive root-org `developer` membership role with no cross-tenant ReBAC\nauthority.\n- **Authorization**: a narrowly-scoped Permit.io\n`DevPortalCatalog`/`DevPortalPlayground` resource pair and `developer`\nrole — deliberately narrower than `viewer`, catalog + sandbox access\nonly.\n- **Sandboxed playground**: try-it calls are proxied through a\nmock-server-by-default layer (Prism, generated from each spec) with an\nopt-in real sandbox URL per service — never a direct call to a family\nrepo''s production `servers` entry.\n- **Deploy/rollout**: Helm/Argo wiring, feature-flag gating\n(`fuzefront.devportal.enabled`, default OFF), and phased rollout.\n\n### Open questions flagged for approval\n1. Permit policy placement — base platform schema vs. devportal''s own\n`ProductPolicy`.\n2. Spec harvest mechanism — push (family repos add a CI step) vs. pull\n(devportal polls).\n3. Argo topology — own Argo Application vs. folded into the `fuzefront`\numbrella chart.\n4. Spec renderer — Stoplight Elements vs. Swagger UI (needs a theming\nspike).\n5. Sandbox depth — mock-only by default vs. real sandbox environments\nfrom day one for some services.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: izzywdev <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"af6bffc6d5e6fbbebffdff99776bc0d6f4f9dfbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/af6bffc6d5e6fbbebffdff99776bc0d6f4f9dfbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/b6dcd40f8575d80fa6f7ec3eb97cbabcbd8f495f","verification":{"payload":"tree af6bffc6d5e6fbbebffdff99776bc0d6f4f9dfbb\nparent 1a3b80860708a34dc97721b65adf93ac999c1a70\nauthor Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com> 1791142197 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791142197 +0300\n\ndocs: developers.fuzefront.com Fuze family developer portal — design proposal (#920)\n\nNo unified developer portal exists to discover, read, and try out\nOpenAPI specs published across the Fuze family of repos and their\nmicroservices. This PR adds a design proposal for\n`developers.fuzefront.com`: a home page, shared FuzeFront sign-in,\nroot-org membership with a `Developer` group, an aggregated OpenAPI\ncatalog, and a sandboxed playground. **Plan only — no implementation**,\npending approval.\n\n### Added\n- `docs/planning/developers-portal.md` — full design proposal covering:\n- **Build vs. adopt review**: compares Backstage, Redoc, Docusaurus, and\na FuzeFront-native app; recommends building a lightweight native portal\n+ spec registry using an embedded OSS renderer (Stoplight Elements /\nSwagger UI) over adopting Backstage.\n- **Architecture**: new `devportal-service` (spec registry, harvest job,\nsandbox proxy) + `devportal-frontend` (home, catalog, spec viewer,\nplayground), harvesting `openapi.yaml` contracts from every `providesTo`\nfamily repo.\n- **Identity**: reuse of the existing Authentik OIDC provider; a new,\nadditive root-org `developer` membership role with no cross-tenant ReBAC\nauthority.\n- **Authorization**: a narrowly-scoped Permit.io\n`DevPortalCatalog`/`DevPortalPlayground` resource pair and `developer`\nrole — deliberately narrower than `viewer`, catalog + sandbox access\nonly.\n- **Sandboxed playground**: try-it calls are proxied through a\nmock-server-by-default layer (Prism, generated from each spec) with an\nopt-in real sandbox URL per service — never a direct call to a family\nrepo''s production `servers` entry.\n- **Deploy/rollout**: Helm/Argo wiring, feature-flag gating\n(`fuzefront.devportal.enabled`, default OFF), and phased rollout.\n\n### Open questions flagged for approval\n1. Permit policy placement — base platform schema vs. devportal''s own\n`ProductPolicy`.\n2. Spec harvest mechanism — push (family repos add a CI step) vs. pull\n(devportal polls).\n3. Argo topology — own Argo Application vs. folded into the `fuzefront`\numbrella chart.\n4. Spec renderer — Stoplight Elements vs. Swagger UI (needs a theming\nspike).\n5. Sandbox depth — mock-only by default vs. real sandbox environments\nfrom day one for some services.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: izzywdev <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid",