p-python/issues/811\">#811</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-python/compare/v5.6.0...v7\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwqktCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOV4QAGqxa2vOXDCEnoiUemHwd6hG\n4BbAvwXMBdW+n1x4TxSeyTi402wKv45Idojp1s+b+/p7xI2oHcs/4m8A3iYz1vhS\nKwKbpwVW0iD1RZTW00XaJdesN7rAklxyAF7fdcKiZZW2cR0jCHXnelqpIO9FnX+T\ngQ4JjphAChayDLQZMKypKAIRDvzgUVeeL2EY3vBOg4tJI3TdNwsXEgVwa2dx21tx\nCeWhJ0WwcKyo/sOq+DYbChmtqr9uKEQC+7ga9o6z5P6SmTjcjEmF8ZJDtd2w89BM\n+XZXNLa+tJIkE1WZ1Ri+gnqjXbEftrSYTZsBASg8bhCD/A0okN3NDcNn3BCFCFis\nFscrnlro24UwUKjWoycZBoE5BLiHRqCsQIShou2w2wUi+MCcacrlbJkrvi1WnDkX\n9DZ26rfra1bWX3qq2zEKNLiD9u3NOKK/AW67J9oc1JWLOGl8JLdLJIfDlKP/AIZi\nGN1EC3oX68hVG1wqypqnJZQlqmwCj+/nc70j7OU3k4pm0GWYGOrGvDjcDVr8XnQr\nk7+AZlTFTDniI7kMTlZ+FrW3AEeHHlOskGaockUuIS+xL+FI56IzofG3QtpadutZ\nvRpkKDEeIy2qhGSXNqpsWvet/hK4PkFzGocqTkgt+QmkDLLhHNhNA1ocsJSihqui\nAQBGlv0QHjSmhsK5xBtV\n=C14n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T19:29:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/e7da492624431f314927422d4e199ff8093aff40","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKGU3ZGE0OTI2MjQ0MzFmMzE0OTI3NDIyZDRlMTk5ZmY4MDkzYWZmNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/0896a7940300c62735dfd554d104e1b94701e235","sha":"0896a7940300c62735dfd554d104e1b94701e235","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/0896a7940300c62735dfd554d104e1b94701e235"}],"sha":"e7da492624431f314927422d4e199ff8093aff40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/e7da492624431f314927422d4e199ff8093aff40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/0896a7940300c62735dfd554d104e1b94701e235/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:29:46Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:29:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(planning): EPIC-21 tag management — capability tagging, matching, earned-tag tracks (#1197)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nAdds `docs/planning/epics/EPIC-21-tag-management.md` — the design of\nrecord for a tag-management microservice + frontend.\n\n**This is a plan only. Nothing is implemented.** The \"Work, in order\"\nsection describes PRs that later sessions will open; merging this\ndocument authorizes that work, it does not perform it.\n\n### What the design covers\n\n- **Tag sets as vocabularies**, scoped `private` (a user''s own) or `org`\n(ReBAC-governed), with a `free`/`controlled` mode. Mirrors the\n`selection_lists → selection_list_items` shape already proven in this\nrepo.\n- **Generic taggings by TypeID** — `{objectType, objectId}` validated\nagainst the identity registry prefix, so any Fuze entity is taggable\nwith no change in its owning service.\n- **A multi-parent tag DAG with two distinct edge kinds.** `specializes`\n(\"Spanish — Mexico\" → \"Spanish\") is followed by matching;\n`requires_first` (\"Senior Agent\" → \"Agent L2\") is a progression\nconstraint and is deliberately **not** followed by matching. Conflating\nthe two silently widens who qualifies for a line — a bug that produces\nplausible results and is only caught by asserting the *absence* of a\nmatch.\n- **Cross-scope hierarchy with a per-caller closure filter**, plus a\nscope-direction rule (private child → org parent allowed; org child →\nprivate parent rejected 422) so a private tag cannot leak through a\nshared parent. A parent the caller cannot read is omitted with **no\ncount** — a redacted count is an existence oracle.\n- **`has` / `requires` / `desires` tagging intents and a first-class\nmatch endpoint** — the call-centre agent↔line projection, ranked by\n`desires` coverage with matched/missing tags named per candidate so a\nrouting decision is explainable.\n- **Earned tags**: a closed criteria grammar (`all`/`any`/`not` over\nmetric comparisons and tag prerequisites), metric values pushed by the\nowning product, append-only awards carrying the justifying snapshot,\nrevoke on lapse, and explicit authorization on progress disclosure\n(progress responses *are* the metric values).\n- **Career tracks** as ordered ladders through tags — `requires_first`\nalone gives only a partial order, which cannot answer \"what''s my next\nrung?\".\n\n### Notable constraints the plan already accounts for\n\n- `gate-microservice-events` requires a **new** service to subscribe to\nall four identity lifecycle events *and* write — `knownUnhandled` is a\nshrink-only ratchet a new service cannot join.\n- The design system has no `Chip`, `TagInput`, `TagGraph` or\n`CriteriaProgress` primitive; these go into the DS **base**, gated by\nframes-first approval.\n- Helm `networkPolicy.port` must be a literal, never `| int` / `|\ndefault` — per the FuzeInfra#501 note in `CLAUDE.md`.\n- The `db-bootstrap` hook runs before the SealedSecret''s sync wave, so\nthe DB password must land in an earlier sync than the one enabling the\nservice.\n- Port 3014 proposed; verified free (3007 is payment-service, 3012/3013\ndevportal).\n- A capability tag is **not** an authorization grant — matching is\nrouting; permission stays with Permit.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 📝 Documentation update\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Manual testing — docs-only change; no code paths touched.\n\nVerified: the committed document contains no session-specific content,\nits section structure renders correctly, and the commit adds exactly one\nfile.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **Frontend Changes:** none\n- **Backend Changes:** none\n- **SDK Changes:** none\n\nOne added file: `docs/planning/epics/EPIC-21-tag-management.md`.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] Documentation has been updated\n\n## 🚨 Breaking Changes\n\nNone.\n\n## 🔗 Related Issues and PRs\n\nFollows the design-first / contract-first flow in `CLAUDE.md`. The\nimplementation PRs this document authorizes are sequenced in its \"Work,\nin order\" section.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Questions for Reviewers\n\nThe ten items under **Career path — open decisions** need an owner call\nbefore the earned-tag work starts — particularly **manual override /\ngrandfathering** (a new hire with ten years'' prior experience starts at\nzero metrics, and the \"earned tags can never be applied by hand\" rule\nblocks attesting it) and **criteria versioning** (whether raising a bar\ndemotes existing holders). Each carries a recommendation; none is\nsettled.\n\n### Future Work\n\nExplicitly out of scope for v1 and named in the document: leaderboards\nand points, the resolver registry, a materialised closure table, and the\ncall-centre product itself — telephony, call records, star ratings and\nACD routing stay in the owning repo. tag-service receives metric values\nand never learns what a call is.\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01V49Rf8VrH3CeLhZVGQ1tg4\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7aacd312beb1aac0ed697e69d93c4e24df5d3742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/7aacd312beb1aac0ed697e69d93c4e24df5d3742"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/0896a7940300c62735dfd554d104e1b94701e235","verification":{"payload":"tree 7aacd312beb1aac0ed697e69d93c4e24df5d3742\nparent 9b9d801742bbd5bccb7dfa505d454deaa1abb46a\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791142186 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791142186 +0300\n\ndocs(planning): EPIC-21 tag management — capability tagging, matchin