tifying snapshot,\nrevoke on lapse, and explicit authorization on progress disclosure\n(progress responses *are* the metric values).\n- **Career tracks** as ordered ladders through tags — `requires_first`\nalone gives only a partial order, which cannot answer \"what''s my next\nrung?\".\n\n### Notable constraints the plan already accounts for\n\n- `gate-microservice-events` requires a **new** service to subscribe to\nall four identity lifecycle events *and* write — `knownUnhandled` is a\nshrink-only ratchet a new service cannot join.\n- The design system has no `Chip`, `TagInput`, `TagGraph` or\n`CriteriaProgress` primitive; these go into the DS **base**, gated by\nframes-first approval.\n- Helm `networkPolicy.port` must be a literal, never `| int` / `|\ndefault` — per the FuzeInfra#501 note in `CLAUDE.md`.\n- The `db-bootstrap` hook runs before the SealedSecret''s sync wave, so\nthe DB password must land in an earlier sync than the one enabling the\nservice.\n- Port 3014 proposed; verified free (3007 is payment-service, 3012/3013\ndevportal).\n- A capability tag is **not** an authorization grant — matching is\nrouting; permission stays with Permit.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 📝 Documentation update\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Manual testing — docs-only change; no code paths touched.\n\nVerified: the committed document contains no session-specific content,\nits section structure renders correctly, and the commit adds exactly one\nfile.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **Frontend Changes:** none\n- **Backend Changes:** none\n- **SDK Changes:** none\n\nOne added file: `docs/planning/epics/EPIC-21-tag-management.md`.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] Documentation has been updated\n\n## 🚨 Breaking Changes\n\nNone.\n\n## 🔗 Related Issues and PRs\n\nFollows the design-first / contract-first flow in `CLAUDE.md`. The\nimplementation PRs this document authorizes are sequenced in its \"Work,\nin order\" section.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Questions for Reviewers\n\nThe ten items under **Career path — open decisions** need an owner call\nbefore the earned-tag work starts — particularly **manual override /\ngrandfathering** (a new hire with ten years'' prior experience starts at\nzero metrics, and the \"earned tags can never be applied by hand\" rule\nblocks attesting it) and **criteria versioning** (whether raising a bar\ndemotes existing holders). Each carries a recommendation; none is\nsettled.\n\n### Future Work\n\nExplicitly out of scope for v1 and named in the document: leaderboards\nand points, the resolver registry, a materialised closure table, and the\ncall-centre product itself — telephony, call records, star ratings and\nACD routing stay in the owning repo. tag-service receives metric values\nand never learns what a call is.\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01V49Rf8VrH3CeLhZVGQ1tg4\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwqkqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy8oQAI1Ue0wqyuj6yOb0Rvp+XxSQ\ni1Sr5PcUwm3dDS8STd3s7FIr4EfPAxDthT8QgrGkfCbfiWiQBmFeRfsKD6JGspdA\nlk2wBqWnHrP/shQAOwmo/XuZmoBJmPr5BYKuR8QcaAcMbtfmVbmGz6HlRPrJ6EZG\nbO36zuDLLBpJOSdRcpd0E3H4hRNNj44DnA1H1tmkEXno9814WWTcWAFHkx74KT1i\nfrhEoHEFdQQEMYzymdVa8HvXdPlw0EPIVSpkhGEvqPOS+bpygzam2tSBSu7/xTA1\n2ysf87oRf9/XbpMnH+QlZAvpm4jvdPOryX4q4HWvgF08EsITb6dLRDnT8WGtRtRP\n+zB544g9+Kec7C50Qhfs7AeW2OMChFKxXvmq9CPCtu84bP7JPOB2m4EKeaOW3Z61\nb1ibEV8ZzKq+I937/ux8EvlUBahFv0tPFMo4lzXww8vJaRhPrjm1zyumV+YLNwqC\nqNa1B5ka3zKqabRoUCqVOkHDw+tla8zLQm39VmgXwaLdUcnVXfwL0SzwDYZSeECz\njuuU19Lv01BLZWJkTkJjowrK/HHUikAfJrtHEp5mIl1EHFcBkBXhf5c8POExNWco\nfo0wycJ0YNmmD6u2AmhQYShgc7vwhpWJgjUC05g9DsOF6GfSpc5gNcHWczL1EOfi\n7Yk06/iO+mcf8qx2x6gW\n=2tLg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T19:29:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https: