hub.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/ab2d153a73853f083f778f29e8d6ed29b90ecd4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:18:25Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:18:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(governance): adopt the data ownership & read-model standard (baseline §4.4) (#1255)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nThis is phase 0 on the FuzeFront side. It adopts the new FuzeSDLC\ndata-consistency standard (`governance/data-consistency-standard.md`,\nbaseline §4.4): one writer per entity, events published through an\noutbox, cross-service references declared with an on-delete policy, and\nlists that span services served from projections owned by each UI''s BFF.\n\n- **`docs/planning/data-consistency-and-read-models.md`** is the design\nof record. It covers:\n- the problem: browser-side joins in `ApplicationsPage` and\n`EmployeeOrgDrilldownPage` cannot paginate, filter or sort across\nservices;\n- the rejected alternatives, including \"centralized write + cached read\nservices\";\n- the BFF topology: the host `backend/` is the shell BFF, each product\nhas its own BFF, and a shared view-service is built only once two BFFs\nneed the same projection;\n  - the current state as measured today;\n  - the six-phase roadmap and open items.\n- **`CLAUDE.md`** gets a short pointer section, in the same style as the\nidentifier section.\n- **`governance/identifier-standard.md` §5** now says that each\nreference''s validation layer and on-delete policy are declared in\n`data-contract.json`. It also records a known gap: a soft delete\ncurrently tombstones the org in `ref_index`.\n- **`microservice-readiness`** gets a new dimension, 9a \"Data ownership\n& consistency\".\n\nThe new `data-consistency` skill and the agent updates are not copied in\nby hand, because those files are `managed`. They will arrive through\ngovernance-sync once FuzeSDLC 1.22.0 is cut.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 📝 Documentation update\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\nDocs only; no code paths change. The schema and its example are\nvalidated in the FuzeSDLC PR.\n\n## 🔗 Related Issues and PRs\n\n- Depends on https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/pull/462 (the\nstandard, the schema, baseline §4.4 and the skill).\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Future Work\n\nADR §5 lays out phases 1–6:\n1. events foundation;\n2. query contract;\n3. references;\n4. projection and BFF pilot;\n5. frontend data layer;\n6. fleet rollout.\n\nBefore phase 1, confirm whether prod runs Kafka.\n`deploy/fuzeinfra-lean-values.yaml` disables it, but the lifecycle doc\nrecords a live broker.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01QahAZ4pQji1uuk42GXyDBs\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4bef7e627a426372d0b7f090a307c13e481e0202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/4bef7e627a426372d0b7f090a307c13e481e0202"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/ab2d153a73853f083f778f29e8d6ed29b90ecd4c","verification":{"payload":"tree 4bef7e627a426372d0b7f090a307c13e481e0202\nparent e1e133140c18b9fc4aaf9fde87b7eb31c0757dd5\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791141505 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791141505 +0300\n\ndocs(governance): adopt the data ownership & read-model standard (baseline §4.4) (#1255)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nThis is phase 0 on the FuzeFront side. It adopts the new FuzeSDLC\ndata-consistency standard (`governance/data-consistency-standard.md`,\nbaseline §4.4): one writer per entity, events published through an\noutbox, cross-service references declared with an on-delete policy, and\nlists that span services served from projections owned by each UI''s BFF.\n\n- **`docs/planning/data-consistency-and-read-models.md`** is the design\nof record. It covers:\n- the problem: browser-side joins in `ApplicationsPage` and\n`EmployeeOrgDrilldownPage` cannot paginate, filter or sort across\nservices;\n- the rejected alternatives, including \"centralized write + cached read\nservices\";\n- the BFF topology: the host `backend/` is the shell BFF, each product\nhas its own BFF, and a shared view-service is built only once two BFFs\nneed the same projection;\n  - the current state as measured today;\n  - the six-phase roadmap and open items.\n- **`CLAUDE.md`** gets a short pointer section, in the same style as the\nidentifier section.\n- **`governance/identifier-standard.md` §5** now says that each\nreference''s validation layer and on-delete policy are declared in\n`data-contract.json`. It also records a known gap: a soft delete\ncurrently tombstones the org in `ref_index`.\n- **`microservice-readiness`** gets a new dimension, 9a \"Data ownership\n& consistency\".\n\nThe new `data-consistency` skill and the agent updates are not copied in\nby hand, because those files are `managed`. They will arrive through\ngovernance-sync once FuzeSDLC 1.22.0 is cut.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 📝 Documentation update\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\nDocs only; no code paths change. The schema and its example are\nvalidated in the FuzeSDLC PR.\n\n## 🔗 Related Issues and PRs\n\n- Depends on https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/pull/462 (the\nstandard, the schema, baseline §4.4 and the skill).\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Future Work\n\nADR §5 lays out phases 1–6:\n1. events foundation;\n2. query contract;\n3. references;\n4. projection and BFF pilot;\n5. frontend data layer;\n6. fleet rollout.\n\nBefore phase 1, confirm whether prod runs Kafka.\n`deploy/fuzeinfra-lean-values.yaml` disables it, but the lifecycle doc\nrecords a live broker.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01QahAZ4pQji1uuk42GXyDBs\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwqaBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUHkQAFKXM4u0ukqnyPDzB3c8N7ms\n4ltdQASNqkODJ8lEt6QRP6I7VtfySysOGmERhf/8p9YbXqp33xMA71bwGzQ4fjqm\nDMHjmfBdSQKKUQ36boDXxc6a6nDYQVBdzyFjAng1j15i0Pb29kDNvRlAIWB9YJfa\naBTJkcuRh+MOBLxE0QKjFGn2CD2EMaVWDdn1478sGR0zH6xKdvEfVkmes6O8llom\nTadw26YNXPAsZedMWV9H6qcFjhYu37Rx3CvC9vaWnS6a2tZDlwiw4T3EAgpj0Z93\nm4aZdfLOq2UlJecVpzqp8GQ83Hvl+yMHTWLfYfxpslxTYiiVNoeS8XxVSp/6cdHB\nO/XaPOL+1kuXRfhGBEgvVfsPDXZlvN9QTwuqgGdn6UgX+1RRGUxN2rmlF+ElYe6K\nAZpovW7z/t0x0pIvn5JbPZVy4F6rQgs4lDRS71neCkbJyMQ4Z77bifyUzpgyJrNs\nFgXfn9+bnFeLS0F6SShp9PXt62PA+u2EaODqTtxLHMqmsXuMLkG+ecRz702KX21x\nqyDP5t4DrV2jsJuj1FeV+h1FEXdwkpIzWCYkrGerT/sE/GdLi6Wj9MbadrFELAGu\nkaHGMGmLjVTbNqF+gf73ltIWoad8uMLyITLgYBc1IOTFa5o7B2pe8UEv4DQN+Djo\n4RopFlNABw2ykD4kDJC4\n=QxM+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T19:18:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0ND