e20cd1366e6bde"}],"sha":"8ccd4ca37648adccc4b2c20de71ed2e0ca29769e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/8ccd4ca37648adccc4b2c20de71ed2e0ca29769e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/7872993d77bb5ee9ca3650af70e20cd1366e6bde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:45:02Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:45:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(identity): set root owner + backfill root memberships (#750 follow-up) (#1095)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nCloses the two halves of **#750** that migration\n`028_seed_root_platform_organization_additively` deliberately left open.\n`028` (owner ruling 2026-09-14, reparent-over-repoint) additively seeds\n`ROOT_ORG_ID` (`…010`), but:\n- it owns the root with the **platform registrar** (`…0001`, a bootstrap\nidentity, not a person); and\n- it does **not** backfill a membership for every user — migration\n`022`''s step (a) was meant to, but it ran while `…010` was still absent\nand **skipped**, and knex won''t re-run it.\n\nNet effect on the live portal: every human — **including the platform\nowner** — is still a **GUEST** of the root org, and the root has no\nhuman owner. (This is exactly what surfaced in the owner''s \"Your\norganizations\" screen: root shows `GUEST`, no owner.)\n\nThis adds `029` (monolith) + `019` (security mirror) to finish it:\n- set `organizations.owner_id` for `ROOT_ORG_ID` to the **platform\nowner** and give them an explicit `owner` membership (upgrading a stale\n`member`/other row if present);\n- backfill a `member` row for **every other user** (`022` step (a),\ndeferred until `…010` existed).\n\nOwner resolution: `ROOT_OWNER_EMAIL` env → else the documented default\nowner email (the repo CODEOWNER) → else the oldest non-registrar user.\nThis makes **you** the explicit owner of root, per your decision.\n\nRelated: #750.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking; data repair migration)\n- [x] 🧪 Test addition\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Real-DB integration tests (monolith\n`tests/setRootOwnerAndBackfillMigration.test.ts`; security\n`tests/migrations.setRootOwnerAndBackfill.test.ts`) — cover: owner_id +\nowner-membership set, member backfill for other users,\nstale-non-owner-row upgrade, idempotency (double `up()`), and the\n**absent-root safe-skip** (no throw, no create). Every scenario runs in\nan always-rolled-back transaction so the shared/scratch DB is never\npolluted.\n- [x] `tsc --noEmit` clean on both backends (0 errors beyond the repo''s\npre-existing `baseUrl` config deprecation).\n- [ ] Local full jest run — the DB integration tests **skip without a\nreachable Postgres**; they will run in CI.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n-\n**`backend/src/migrations/029_set_root_owner_and_backfill_memberships.ts`**\n+ security mirror **`backend/security/src/migrations/019_...`** —\nidempotent; **never throws** (an absent root is a logged skip, so it can\nnever re-introduce the #750 crashloop). Operates on the canonical\nliteral `ROOT_ORG_ID` only; does **not** touch the adopted legacy\n`fuzefront` org (converging the two is the repoint decision `028`''s\nheader explains was declined).\n- No app/UI/contract changes.\n\n## ⚠️ deploy-window — DO NOT auto-merge\n\n`master` is deploy-on-push and this migration mutates prod\n`organizations`/`organization_memberships` rows on deploy. **No\n`auto-merge` label** — please merge this in a deliberate deploy window.\nIt runs after `028` in the chain, so `…010` exists when it runs.\n\n**One thing to confirm before/at merge:** on prod, `ROOT_OWNER_EMAIL` is\nunset, so owner resolution falls to the default email\n(`izzy.weinberg@gmail.com`) — assuming that''s the email on your platform\naccount. If your account uses a different email, set `ROOT_OWNER_EMAIL`\nin the backend deployment env (or tell me and I''ll adjust the default)\nso the right account becomes owner.\n\n## OUT OF SCOPE — NOT DONE\n\n- The remaining `…010` ↔ adopted-`fuzefront` divergence (a repoint +\nPermit-side migration) — deliberately declined in `028`; not revisited\nhere.\n- The live **HTTP 500** seen in the screenshot — likely the same\nroot-absence surfacing; should resolve once `028`+`029` land and `…010`\nexists. Worth confirming from logs post-deploy.\n- Personal-org retirement for new signups — gated by\n`fuzefront.identity.root-membership` (still OFF; the Unleash flip is the\nseparately-blocked operator step).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_017zdYnxKQVVhFyRubDa1BmK\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_017zdYnxKQVVhFyRubDa1BmK)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9c16e40e90e17ba39fe17fc33fe0d5532d7cece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/tre