m/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c10002a7f8f9608e687af872533bb51f4e8ae8c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:53:55Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:53:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(permit): declare SelectionList + SelectionListCatalog resources (H-2/H-3 groundwork) (#1251)\n\n## What\n\nDeclares the Permit resource types for selection lists (H-2) plus\ntenant-level catalog groundwork (H-3). Schema only: no service, flag or\nroute change.\n\n- `SelectionList` (per-list, ReBAC instance roles). Actions: `read,\nadd_value, update_value, remove_value, translate, update, delete,\nmanage_access`. Five direct roles (no `granted_to`) per\n`services/selection-list-service/openapi.yaml`: `list-owner` (all 8),\n`list-editor` (read, add/update/remove_value, translate, update),\n`list-contributor` (read, add/update_value, translate),\n`list-translator` (read, translate), `list-viewer` (read).\n- `SelectionListCatalog` (tenant-level). Actions: `list, create,\nread_quota, resolve`. Tenant grants: `admin` = all four; `editor` =\nlist, create, resolve; `viewer` = list, resolve; `developer` = none.\n- Tenant roles hold zero `SelectionList:*` actions (asserted).\n- Declared in both `backend/src/permit/schema.ts` (authoritative, synced\nto Permit) and the diverged copy `backend/security/src/permit/schema.ts`\n(role/resource catalog, `mapScopesToPermitRole`, grant tests).\n- `authz-gate.ts` unchanged: `TENANT_LEVEL_ROLES` has no `list-*` names.\n- `authz.human-grant-authz.test.ts`: hand-written\n`INSTANCE_ROLE_ACTIONS` double replaced by one built from the real\n`resources[SelectionList].roles`; new route tests (owner-1 grants\nlist-owner on L1 -> 201 (the route returns 201, not 200); denied on\nanother list / tenant; denied for tenant-level role names; non-owner\nlist roles cannot grant).\n\n## Prod apply path\nMerging deploys the backend image. The Helm post-install/upgrade hook\n(`permit-schema-job.yaml`, runs `node\ndist/permit/sync-permit-schema.js`, 120s deadline) and the non-fatal\nstartup `syncPermitSchemaFromRegistry` push the schema automatically,\nonly when `permit.enabled`. Nothing else to run by hand.\n\n## Open design question (deliberately NOT implemented): derived\nlist-owner from org admin\nNo derived role (org admin -> list-owner) is declared. It would be\ninert: nothing creates a `SelectionList --organization--> Organization`\nrelation tuple, and customer-org admins hold tenant `admin`, not ReBAC\n`org-admin` (only FuzeOne staff do). A tenant admin already holds\n`Organization:manage`, so the grant gate lets them grant themselves\n`list-owner` via `/authz/grants`. Revisit only if/when the service\nwrites the relation tuple.\n\n(`docs/planning/selection-lists-permit-actions.md` was absent on origin\nat finish time and is owned by `claude/sl5-h3-contract`; these notes\nlive here instead.)\n\n## Verification\n- `cd backend && PERMIT_API_KEY=x npx jest -c <config without\ntests/setup.ts> tests/permit-schema.test.ts tests/product-policy.test.ts\ntests/permit-sync-registry.test.ts` -> 3 suites, 70 tests passed (the\ndefault config needs Postgres via tests/setup.ts).\n- `cd backend/security && npx jest\ntests/authz.human-grant-authz.test.ts` -> 53 passed.\n- Full security jest: 773 passed / 9 failed; the same 13 suites (9\ntests) fail identically against the origin/master schema (pre-existing),\nnone touch this change.\n- `node scripts/check-version-bump.mjs` -> OK (no published package\ntouched). `tsc --noEmit` shows only pre-existing missing-export errors\nfrom unbuilt workspace packages, none in `permit/` or tests.\n\nIntentionally opened WITHOUT the `auto-merge` label (task: do not\nmerge).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43914194058e8c2889d351e109bdd899dd23e6df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/43914194058e8c2889d351e109bdd899dd23e6df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/c10002a7f8f9608e687af872533bb51f4e8ae8c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 43914194058e8c2889d351e109bdd899dd23e6df\nparent 4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791125635 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791125635 +0300\n\nfeat(permit): declare SelectionList + SelectionListCatalog resources (H-2/H-3 groundwork) (#1251)\n\n## What\n\nDeclares the Permit resource types for selection lists (H-2) plus\ntenant-level catalog groundwork (H-3). Schema only: no service, flag or\nroute change.\n\n- `SelectionList` (per-list, ReBAC instance roles). Actions: `read,\nadd_value, update_value, remove_value, translate, update, delete,\nmanage_access`. Five direct roles (no `granted_to`) per\n`services/selection-list-service/openapi.yaml`: `list-owner` (all 8),\n`list-editor` (read, add/update/remove_value, translate, update),\n`list-contributor` (read, add/update_value, translate),\n`list-translator` (read, translate), `list-viewer` (read).\n- `SelectionListCatalog` (tenant-level). Actions: `list, create,\nread_quota, resolve`. Tenant grants: `admin` = all four; `editor` =\nlist, create, resolve; `viewer` = list, resolve; `developer` = none.\n- Tenant roles hold zero `SelectionList:*` actions (asserted).\n- Declared in both `backend/src/permit/schema.ts` (authoritative, synced\nto Permit) and the diverged copy `backend/security/src/permit/schema.ts`\n(role/resource catalog, `mapScopesToPermitRole`, grant tests).\n- `authz-gate.ts` unchanged: `TENANT_LEVEL_ROLES` has no `list-*` names.\n- `authz.human-grant-authz.test.ts`: hand-written\n`INSTANCE_ROLE_ACTIONS` double replaced by one built from the real\n`resources[SelectionList].roles`; new route tests (owner-1 grants\nlist-owner on L1 -> 201 (the route returns 201, not 200); denied on\nanother list / tenant; denied for tenant-level role names; non-owner\nlist roles cannot grant).\n\n## Prod apply path\nMerging deploys the backend image. The Helm post-install/upgrade hook\n(`permit-schema-job.yaml`, runs `node\ndist/permit/sync-permit-schema.js`, 120s deadline) and the non-fatal\nstartup `syncPermitSchemaFromRegistry` push the schema automatically,\nonly when `permit.enabled`. Nothing else to run by hand.\n\n## Open design question (deliberately NOT implemented): derived\nlist-owner from org admin\nNo derived role (org admin -> list-owner) is declared. It would be\ninert: nothing creates a `SelectionList --organization--> Organization`\nrelation tuple, and customer-org admins hold tenant `admin`, not ReBAC\n`org-admin` (only FuzeOne staff do). A tenant admin already holds\n`Organization:manage`, so the grant gate lets them grant themselves\n`list-owner` via `/authz/grants`. Revisit only if/when the service\nwrites the relation tuple.\n\n(`docs/planning/selection-lists-permit-actions.md` was absent on origin\nat finish time and is owned by `claude/sl5-h3-contract`; these notes\nlive here instead.)\n\n## Verification\n- `cd backend && PERMIT_API_KEY=x npx jest -c <config without\ntests/setup.ts> tests/permit-schema.test.ts tests/product-policy.test.ts\ntests/permit-sync-registry.test.ts` -> 3 suites, 70 tests passed (the\ndefault config needs Postgres via tests/setup.ts).\n- `cd backend/security && npx jest\ntests/authz.human-grant-authz.test.ts` -> 53 passed.\n- Full security jest: 773 passed / 9 failed; the same 13 suites (9\ntests) fail identically against the origin/master schema (pre-existing),\nnone touch this change.\n- `node scripts/check-version-bump.mjs` -> OK (no published package\ntouched). `tsc --noEmit` shows only pre-existing missing-export errors\nfrom unbuilt workspace packages, none in `permit/` or tests.\n\nIntentionally opened WITHOUT the `auto-merge` label (task: do not\nmerge).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwmiDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYoQQABRv1B4vFeRfxEjJOVTfetHL\nfag0oHwx2vvt2N4iNIraC/gcYn2Sbn9I6GT+gDofo2ey/OIUhCLjxnJE6ZrY1zN0\nX9CUXASDQls/ETMFvnDywTvNKVSX4wFCK3ok+mDtOsAMOuNxHqj1JJtJt8tmgf9S\nsL9P5FGT8UTXMaC3NBpe1o3RYD8M8/us2BnsgJlTYOc/BMaXAr/JH8vZCW5xEC/e\nIycVIvy1weZZtn4bHXEIFYDCk4ugt7HwisHVNmQs4A3fsre6ppjfTMjbxTchZz/d\npuqUNdWomC+jQSHtal2cNhb0Ogl6kJXRZGXcw6GwfGQJO9cxvAa3HRP4ahLccI1c\n/gpmoGDHbDv0E4bhpH7rHBJHtWlft5T42tR5HP+/XhYWmnhv6FyrONEkCYyRRs2p\n+hIhklRQb7ADF4yQMLN8AiiYCaAcP/JgwgwtAXEu5PP6nE6W4BfqlzTAjEAPu4OE\nnTRs41ByNLiOXaw8QOB9ruDZCxXz8l7MfCtTfZUBFZl341Y5HBQ288JUiO+qSLPj\npOm0v/D33DUxb0zHhcDtCF8ihAUCpXsgPSgtNjMRfFXctLYA6RR2C2OeSHXKGMDY\nHJQMxKVHFXHAcEdQYas5CTxsaROhPAFW0VKFafkNQe6hRflKO7VpKuLZYsz52vxY\nANH6HUbuiTOe1zzo+F0A\n=E0pT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T14:53:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/c10002a7f8f9608e687af872533bb51f4e8ae8c4","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKGMxMDAwMmE3ZjhmOTYwOGU2ODdhZjg3MjUzM2JiNTFmNGU4YWU4YzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1","sha":"4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1"}],"sha":"c10002a7f8f9608e687af872533bb51f4e8ae8c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c10002a7f8f9608e687af872533bb51f4e8ae8c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fuze-agent","id":321521006,"login":"fuze-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEyoFbg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:41:13Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:41:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(selection-lists)!: contract 3.0.0, split authz into SelectionListCatalog + SelectionList (H-3) (#1250)\n\nEvery operation now declares x-permit-resource alongside\nx-permit-action.\nCollection-level operations (list, create, quota, resolve) are checked\nagainst the tenant-level SelectionListCatalog resource (list, create,\nread_quota, resolve); per-list actions on SelectionList are\ninstance-only\nand tenant roles confer none of them. Tenant grants on the catalog:\nadmin = list/create/read_quota/resolve, editor = list/create/resolve,\nviewer = list/resolve, developer = none.\n\nItem purge (DELETE .../items/{itemId}?purge=true) additionally requires\ndelete on the parent list (x-permit-additional-actions), making it\nowner-only as the prose always stated (review M-1). Resolve deliberately\nskips the per-list read check; documented as an accepted trade-off\n(L-4).\nNo automatic admin -> list-owner derivation; the documented support path\nis\na tenant admin self-granting list-owner via /authz/grants.\n\n403 is declared on listSelectionLists and getSelectionListQuota. Wire\nshapes are unchanged (oasdiff: 0 breaking, 2 info), but MAJOR because\nexisting grants stop satisfying operations they used to. Helm vendored\ncopy synced byte-identical. Design record + migration notes in\ndocs/planning/selection-lists-permit-actions.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a4e917676a5555c7227671e1700d4934e4ee1ebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/a4e917676a5555c7227671e1700d4934e4ee1ebe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1","verification":{"payload":"tree a4e917676a5555c7227671e1700d4934e4ee1ebe\nparent adb88ab112cacbf0640a9d1fd47f3da99054cedc\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791124873 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791124873 +0300\n\nfeat(selection-lists)!: contract 3.0.0, split authz into SelectionListCatalog + SelectionList (H-3) (#1250)\n\nEvery operation now declares x-permit-resource alongside\nx-permit-action.\nCollection-level operations (list, create, quota, resolve) are checked\nagainst the tenant-level SelectionListCatalog resource (list, create,\nread_quota, resolve); per-list actions on SelectionList are\ninstance-only\nand tenant roles confer none of them. Tenant grants on the catalog:\nadmin = list/create/read_quota/resolve, editor = list/create/resolve,\nviewer = list/resolve, developer = none.\n\nItem purge (DELETE .../items/{itemId}?purge=true) additionally requires\ndelete on the parent list (x-permit-additional-actions), making it\nowner-only as the prose always stated (review M-1). Resolve deliberately\nskips the per-list read check; documented as an accepted trade-off\n(L-4).\nNo automatic admin -> list-owner derivation; the documented support path\nis\na tenant admin self-granting list-owner via /authz/grants.\n\n403 is declared on listSelectionLists and getSelectionListQuota. Wire\nshapes are unchanged (oasdiff: 0 breaking, 2 info), but MAJOR because\nexisting grants stop satisfying operations they used to. Helm vendored\ncopy synced byte-identical. Design record + migration notes in\ndocs/planning/selection-lists-permit-actions.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwmWJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgOsQAE/hpQDIxwQmRdTtGQ2ELT5f\n2c9JZpgXfM6DoziZAeTCFn+f5Eps5yT7cZfOaxUckX8NizzFuLIeRn5GUVQ7P8kj\nNiec6f2ghnzDl6jVKqLH9sSIAKa3mpa97kJ/kFRCTAZ14Ri2jwyXBqlY8vsMk8A9\nz0MZpsglQtj0S1QKkXyEuaS6TNYcH92gPPpAj10aiW3xW+HOG24njQBO67L5Lys8\nVvICB7nimPSXzfUl4tjGKebIjaNTZZXG0iH0tM8Vqt3apAXyOFp0ypzl41+HpMam\nO02xDrkP/evzwATZSLGZxuuSwCJRNbh9sFXPghGvTgJz/9CN+BzCU4QqVGykkZaM\nrRVqGJVEeRRHjd9efhCZnH0jr7gZcCdguoqkAQ8xmpaoDJV+pk9AC7qzBO3t7JQe\nhV1KLGT5P+LQQkRkiARsTa/J2osgpXhCPrlxYscW7WGtNmbAusA43D7wNkYezABE\nWTuLk+JkOlPVdZJs4dyyPUsNVCskdnRtw7eq8mW2UZ6YViGiRAyuczM8Cd55meKT\nlOOCUi28fHqqaiTh+PwaEJK0mcbb9vI323rloDFwYugxFSdiEAHvBoBHz7LGHqVI\n0fMngJP106Ux9j7Bf5fx0vIOiCSxLni4GX5Q6JxZqYPGaa58e+CC38dVU23vOFRO\nX4Z7WAVN9iQMSGKLUcyS\n=w6NS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T14:41:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDRiNDljYzQ3NjM2MDg1NjczYzg2MjhiOTkyNGE2NmYzZmMyZDk2ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/adb88ab112cacbf0640a9d1fd47f3da99054cedc","sha":"adb88ab112cacbf0640a9d1fd47f3da99054cedc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/adb88ab112cacbf0640a9d1fd47f3da99054cedc"}],"sha":"4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/4b49cc47636085673c8628b9924a66f3fc2d96d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/adb88ab112cacbf0640a9d1fd47f3da99054cedc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:40:18Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:40:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dashboard): show public/marketplace apps regardless of active org (post-prod smoke) (#1252)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nFixes the standing **prod post-deploy smoke** failure\n(`prod-post-deploy.yml` → \"Live smoke / Playwright live smoke\",\n`frontend/e2e/post-prod/live-smoke.spec.ts` test 7, line 338:\n`expect(cards.first()).toBeVisible()` on `.app-card` times out). It has\nfailed on **every** run since ≥2026-09-27.\n\nThe dashboard renders cards from `useRegisteredApps()` filtered through\n`isAppVisibleForOrg()`. That filter only treated `organizationId ===\nnull` as platform-global and **never looked at `manifest.visibility`**.\nAfter the 2026-08-25 owner ruling backfilled every first-party app''s org\nfrom `null` to `ROOT_ORG_ID` (applications migration `011` / backend\nmigration `026`), a `public` app such as **Clock** now carries\n`organizationId: ROOT_ORG_ID`, so the `null` branch no longer recognizes\nit. Any user whose active org isn''t ROOT — a brand-new account with no\norg included — got an empty dashboard, while the server\n(`canRead`/`list`/`scopeAppsQuery`) and the sidebar (which applies no\norg filter) correctly listed it.\n\nThe post-prod smoke''s org-less synthetic is exactly that case: its\n`/api/apps` check (same visibility rule) returned `apps.length > 0`\n(passed), yet zero `.app-card` rendered because the dashboard dropped\nthe app here.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [x] 🧪 Test addition or improvement\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests — `isAppVisibleForOrg` now returns `true` for a\n`public`/`marketplace` app regardless of active org\n- [x] DOM tests — `DashboardPage` renders a `public` app owned by\n`ROOT_ORG_ID` for an org-less user\n\n```bash\ncd frontend && npx vitest run src/__tests__/DashboardPage.org-app-visibility.test.tsx\n# 12 passed\nnpx eslint src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx src/__tests__/DashboardPage.org-app-visibility.test.tsx  # clean\n```\n\nNew tests use the prod-realistic shape (public app owned by\n`ROOT_ORG_ID`, org-less user) and fail without the fix.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n- **Frontend:** `isAppVisibleForOrg()` now mirrors the server''s BOLA\nrule — `visibility` `public`|`marketplace` is visible to everyone,\nchecked before the org-ownership branch. No backend/SDK changes.\n\n### Code Quality\n\n- [x] Self-review completed\n- [x] ESLint passes without errors\n- [x] Commented (why the check is required post-backfill)\n\n## 🚨 Breaking Changes\n\nNone. Public/marketplace apps become visible to more users (the server\nalready authorized them); org/private scoping is unchanged.\n\n## ⚠️ Scope note for reviewers / verification\n\nThis fix resolves the **observed** failure (zero `.app-card` at line\n338). Test 7 then navigates to `/app/:id` and asserts the\nModule-Federation remote mounts. If a prod remote is not actually\nserving (`backend/src/routes/apps.ts` historically noted \"0 of 16\nremotes serving\"), that step could surface a **separate** failure — a\nFuzeInfra/prod-runtime concern, not this repo. I could not verify prod\nremote health from the session (prod probes are blocked here). Full\nsmoke green should be confirmed by a fresh `prod-post-deploy` dispatch\nafter merge.\n\nNot the cause here: the\n`POST_PROD_ADMIN_EMAIL`/`POST_PROD_ADMIN_PASSWORD` secrets (PR #1235)\ngate the **skipped** Portals-directory test, not test 7. Run logs\nconfirm `POST_PROD_PASSWORD` is set and the synthetic login succeeds.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Wrb3ZmwUESEDDaomKNpXbj\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wrb3ZmwUESEDDaomKNpXbj)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79826f581b5e462def229224fbc77c323f19d7f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/79826f581b5e462def229224fbc77c323f19d7f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/adb88ab112cacbf0640a9d1fd47f3da99054cedc","verification":{"payload":"tree 79826f581b5e462def229224fbc77c323f19d7f6\nparent dd0a2516f9cea8c4008ca5ff5329b430fd6264bc\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791124818 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791124818 +0000\n\nfix(dashboard): show public/marketplace apps regardless of active org (post-prod smoke) (#1252)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nFixes the standing **prod post-deploy smoke** failure\n(`prod-post-deploy.yml` → \"Live smoke / Playwright live smoke\",\n`frontend/e2e/post-prod/live-smoke.spec.ts` test 7, line 338:\n`expect(cards.first()).toBeVisible()` on `.app-card` times out). It has\nfailed on **every** run since ≥2026-09-27.\n\nThe dashboard renders cards from `useRegisteredApps()` filtered through\n`isAppVisibleForOrg()`. That filter only treated `organizationId ===\nnull` as platform-global and **never looked at `manifest.visibility`**.\nAfter the 2026-08-25 owner ruling backfilled every first-party app''s org\nfrom `null` to `ROOT_ORG_ID` (applications migration `011` / backend\nmigration `026`), a `public` app such as **Clock** now carries\n`organizationId: ROOT_ORG_ID`, so the `null` branch no longer recognizes\nit. Any user whose active org isn''t ROOT — a brand-new account with no\norg included — got an empty dashboard, while the server\n(`canRead`/`list`/`scopeAppsQuery`) and the sidebar (which applies no\norg filter) correctly listed it.\n\nThe post-prod smoke''s org-less synthetic is exactly that case: its\n`/api/apps` check (same visibility rule) returned `apps.length > 0`\n(passed), yet zero `.app-card` rendered because the dashboard dropped\nthe app here.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [x] 🧪 Test addition or improvement\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests — `isAppVisibleForOrg` now returns `true` for a\n`public`/`marketplace` app regardless of active org\n- [x] DOM tests — `DashboardPage` renders a `public` app owned by\n`ROOT_ORG_ID` for an org-less user\n\n```bash\ncd frontend && npx vitest run src/__tests__/DashboardPage.org-app-visibility.test.tsx\n# 12 passed\nnpx eslint src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx src/__tests__/DashboardPage.org-app-visibility.test.tsx  # clean\n```\n\nNew tests use the prod-realistic shape (public app owned by\n`ROOT_ORG_ID`, org-less user) and fail without the fix.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n- **Frontend:** `isAppVisibleForOrg()` now mirrors the server''s BOLA\nrule — `visibility` `public`|`marketplace` is visible to everyone,\nchecked before the org-ownership branch. No backend/SDK changes.\n\n### Code Quality\n\n- [x] Self-review completed\n- [x] ESLint passes without errors\n- [x] Commented (why the check is required post-backfill)\n\n## 🚨 Breaking Changes\n\nNone. Public/marketplace apps become visible to more users (the server\nalready authorized them); org/private scoping is unchanged.\n\n## ⚠️ Scope note for reviewers / verification\n\nThis fix resolves the **observed** failure (zero `.app-card` at line\n338). Test 7 then navigates to `/app/:id` and asserts the\nModule-Federation remote mounts. If a prod remote is not actually\nserving (`backend/src/routes/apps.ts` historically noted \"0 of 16\nremotes serving\"), that step could surface a **separate** failure — a\nFuzeInfra/prod-runtime concern, not this repo. I could not verify prod\nremote health from the session (prod probes are blocked here). Full\nsmoke green should be confirmed by a fresh `prod-post-deploy` dispatch\nafter merge.\n\nNot the cause here: the\n`POST_PROD_ADMIN_EMAIL`/`POST_PROD_ADMIN_PASSWORD` secrets (PR #1235)\ngate the **skipped** Portals-directory test, not test 7. Run logs\nconfirm `POST_PROD_PASSWORD` is set and the synthetic login succeeds.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Wrb3ZmwUESEDDaomKNpXbj\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wrb3ZmwUESEDDaomKNpXbj)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","rea