l":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fuze-agent","id":321521006,"login":"fuze-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEyoFbg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/0e300a6d656426f28365a2d5abde8ecf159fc83d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:17:28Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:17:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"diag(prod-synthetic-admin): print k8s secret GET status to pinpoint the provision failure (#1247)\n\nThe provision step swallowed the HTTP status (curl -sf ... || true), so\n''Could not read INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET'' could mean a 403 (runner Role\nnot yet granting fuzefront-secrets), a 200 with the key missing, or a\nreachability problem — indistinguishable from the log.\n\nCapture the status of the fuzefront-secrets GET (target) alongside a\ncontrol GET of unleash-secrets (which the runner Role has always\nallowed),\nand branch the error message on the pair: target=403 + control=200 means\nthe unleash-runner-secret-reader Role hasn''t picked up the resourceNames\naddition from #1237 yet (an un-applied Argo sync, not a code gap);\ntarget=200 means the key is missing from the live Secret; anything else\nis\nRBAC/reachability. Makes the next run self-diagnosing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0127R9Zcw92tmBkxUUuLEB79\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3802430375df6b571c27230acfe6d86396c5ac82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/3802430375df6b571c27230acfe6d86396c5ac82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/0e300a6d656426f28365a2d5abde8ecf159fc83d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3802430375df6b571c27230acfe6d86396c5ac82\nparent 35032540118ebd0e36aa47c98c958edf45e51521\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791123448 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791123448 +0300\n\ndiag(prod-synthetic-admin): print k8s secret GET status to pinpoint the provision failure (#1247)\n\nThe provision step swallowed the HTTP status (curl -sf ... || true), so\n''Could not read INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET'' could mean a 403 (runner Role\nnot yet granting fuzefront-secrets), a 200 with the key missing, or a\nreachability problem — indistinguishable from the log.\n\nCapture the status of the fuzefront-secrets GET (target) alongside a\ncontrol GET of unleash-secrets (which the runner Role has always\nallowed),\nand branch the error message on the pair: target=403 + control=200 means\nthe unleash-runner-secret-reader Role hasn''t picked up the resourceNames\naddition from #1237 yet (an un-applied Argo sync, not a code gap);\ntarget=200 means the key is missing from the live Secret; anything else\nis\nRBAC/reachability. Makes the next run self-diagnosing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0127R9Zcw92tmBkxUUuLEB79\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwl/4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATXAQAHRQiUWp7ikAlFVSydu1mRtN\nSrMJvbffxFKFIQTS7sEmn444j2b+b/dV7mel7I+lBdTCcNeHK/7L14OH1/PsyJTr\nAtegI4Wee1k/a3hUY962vxZ87MqLAWIUo6n+7RBl8bifvV3XRFRykq2ImcKmDtF0\npRv0ASZ3+V7BHf62ABwkfdwCmx13zJfc0PbCek4Jn7+5Mlx0bitfp6jN+rCwMmaX\nC4KnK4LhJebF0/4Vk0lVZPNyncthnKbvLrkrsTfbDTx/OV5KblWrMqOuqiJX400Z\n1LE53H00OnE1F44dPgGV/1WWMYRJLPAe98flqNfWse62UxYRNQsEnV9A00NggAGr\nAoMXowftXA+Wn+L3Zggmik6wkcRROCQdigYRsfkI7lboVqRjH7zvvmcyij+K9+b1\nx4WjEp3+x3Ms+wlFeQglwWpWItTt5304CbtKZLsw7Gr26RA1PRAjJAkYhvXYdj0r\nZWWZQ9PPr3ASogQU8JhAEDNwzQap07ZXgJIK/BoJYIzrOtx0G9KBsv9bGdn1j/II\nHZTQS81kDLVTRCSA2ypr+tjVm3OnFDoQJitJu/fNxOqqnu6Rxfacev+UisqaSmEU\nBITHfT1Xx/Zof/nyusXWFct67QLUyQ7VtmvK4b0a5ITv8PNSNIKSsBZaJvm2iMjE\nKJS02oPKsitu/APXs5Vz\n=Q/pO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T14:17:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/0e300a6d656426f28365a2d5abde8ecf159fc83d","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDBlMzAwYTZkNjU2NDI2ZjI4MzY1YTJkNWFiZGU4ZWNmMTU5ZmM4M2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/35032540118ebd0e36aa47c98c958edf45e51521","sha":"35032540118ebd0e36aa47c98c958edf45e51521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/35032540118ebd0e36aa47c98c958edf45e51521"}],"sha":"0e300a6d656426f28365a2d5abde8ecf159fc83d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/0e300a6d656426f28365a2d5abde8ecf159fc83d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/35032540118ebd0e36aa47c98c958edf45e51521/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:08:09Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:08:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(selection-lists): service hardening: authz always on in prod, crash-proof requests, org-deleted handler, flag init, /ready + /metrics, machine identity for grants (#1248)\n\nFixes the selection-list-service findings from the independent authz review and the rollout readiness check. The service stays disabled; rendered Helm output is unchanged while disabled.\n\n- H-1: authz is always enforced when NODE_ENV=production; the env var only matters outside production. Deployment sets it explicitly (authzEnabled: true).\n- H-4: every route handler is wrapped so rejections reach a final error handler; NUL bytes are rejected at the edge (400) and path ids are validated against the contract pattern (prefix compared with startsWith, no dynamic RegExp); process-level handlers keep the process up on an unhandled rejection and shut down gracefully on an uncaught exception.\n- M-3 / B7: org-deleted and user-deleted handlers use the real columns (organization_id, status), hard mode is one FK-safe transaction, and both match bare UUID and TypeID forms.\n- B4: @fuzefront/feature-flags is a dependency, built into the image, and init() runs at startup (bounded, never fatal; unreachable Unleash stays OFF).\n- /ready does a bounded select 1; /metrics exposes process metrics and a request-duration histogram with no id labels; the readiness probe uses /ready.\n- Grant/revoke writes use a client_credentials machine token (scope authz:admin, via @fuzefront/service-auth), never the end user''s token, and fail closed if the identity is not configured. New optional SealedSecret keys: SERVICE_CLIENT_ID, SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET.\n\nWith authz always on in prod, requests fail closed (403) until the Permit SelectionList schema (H-2) and tenant-level actions (H-3) land, so the service must not be enabled before them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","tree":{"sha":"36ac160b9a2a7a9f3655e9e12fed6d63047c23a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/36ac160b9a2a7a9f3655e9e12fed6d63047c23a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/35032540118ebd0e36aa47c98c958edf45e51521","verification":{"payload":"tree 36ac160b9a2a7a9f3655e9e12fed6d63047c23a6\nparent 297043928ec381576be83c79ed6136ad73c1d8f0\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791122889 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791122889 +0300\n\nfix(selection-lists): service hardening: authz always on in prod, crash-proof requests, org-deleted handler, flag init, /ready + /metrics, machine identity for grants (#1248)\n\nFixes the selection-list-service findings from the independent authz review and the rollout readiness check. The service stays disabled; rendered Helm output is unchanged while disabled.\n\n- H-1: authz is always enforced when NODE_ENV=production; the env var only matters outside production. Deployment sets it explicitly (authzEnabled: true).\n- H-4: every route handler is wrapped so rejections reach a final error handler; NUL bytes are rejected at the edge (400) and path ids are validated against the contract pattern (prefix compared with startsWith, no dynamic RegExp); process-level handlers keep the process up on an unhandled rejection and shut down gracefully on an uncaught exception.\n- M-3 / B7: org-deleted and user-deleted handlers use the real columns (organization_id, status), hard mode is one FK-safe transaction, and both match bare UUID and TypeID forms.\n- B4: @fuzefront/feature-flags is a dependency, built into the image, and init() runs at startup (bounded, never fatal; unreachable Unleash stays OFF).\n- /ready does a bounded select 1; /metrics exposes process metrics and a request-duration histogram with no id labels; the readiness probe uses /ready.\n- Grant/revoke writes use a client_credentials machine token (scope authz:admin, via @fuzefront/service-auth), never the end user''s token, and fail closed if the identity is not configured. New optional SealedSecret keys: SERVICE_CLIENT_ID, SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET.\n\nWith authz always on in prod, requests fail closed (403) until the Permit SelectionList schema (H-2) and tenant-level actions (H-3) land, so the service must not be enabled before them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwl3JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT18QAEc9Ai6+VKA23V51Tw3kUHn3\nuxlZebEcuTlbUpqXnZyjbb0OklwGFTQK+GjkDuhSk5oKNCet7BtAeg3dlJvhUjpF\nlwXgXT2f51sPO576VpZl38jpQ7OfNXhZU2UmM00Yxt1fD6e62ZVQ3mWhfuA2W66K\nHILImSsKwXoXp575KsqB9cmI+z/6c1nh5UmmULRGsaf6uzIP4pR07w5HuKf2BE+M\npRijhYpO5Sdpldmokj4hVGE0oDDb9kf30J9DSzZLxk8i5PF85S0C/nxmHHKWP8qJ\nQLXNXK2So0AUNESnB3rZ1w9WOW19t8aybxTNDK5l5kCvHT0ahxm2s/pGlYcuIfTR\nzSpUP6bq3Qx0Xn67cjag/Y4NMOsyfEG7r5mdd9DWILdHMlNRq5Rk/uwHaeLBZaNf\nhPbAX9d/4jewxVyeOElWHBZ3oYegpJrfD/Z+5Ep+rmavX3U2OBBGM/Ops93WMivV\niXAIdpLyfcwV7GEAAA39deVqxz3gKG1FoQFtEfv0r2jNNIux0PbzSbyrncfrEXME\nkNNEnzNME41gscFBf/ZZxBd0xADga5SAHlEYM715RovkZk98P2dn8JuR+soS7mSZ\n4D20NfkX26eMMwA4m+FRy6tmEOzmVvTog5KZ3SkOaU9sjCH2A8GnB+2/M9pk3AJt\n3hg/iXusMUzx07DuY1zh\n=gMzj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T14:08:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","ur