lags catches and fails closed) is still asserted by the same tests. 0 unhandled in 30 consecutive runs after the change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","tree":{"sha":"2bba213fcfe0c1ed0c56fff6724b987abf7d6a57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/2bba213fcfe0c1ed0c56fff6724b987abf7d6a57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/aec50a3049d1a01558d56a0040fd9b4460e0b81b","verification":{"payload":"tree 2bba213fcfe0c1ed0c56fff6724b987abf7d6a57\nparent bcf2e1e5cd1822390d42e778bf5dadf53ebdf0d8\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791121221 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791121221 +0300\n\ntest(frontend): guard the flag-ready test''s deferred fetch against an unhandled rejection (#1245)\n\nApp.selection-lists-flag-ready.test.tsx rejects a test-owned deferred promise to simulate a network failure. When the rejection raced the component''s own handler Node reported it as unhandled and Vitest failed the whole run with every test passing (about 1 run in 8 locally; hit several PRs'' Lint & Test). Attach a no-op catch to the deferred; production behavior (fetchFlags catches and fails closed) is still asserted by the same tests. 0 unhandled in 30 consecutive runs after the change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwldFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARNMQAFeHpdlt2BcOJhdRKjql9dLG\nf5xXo46uuj3Y5mA1zKUUnBkMtYmMrON7TxWck1Wgyhjhrievj8os4Ef9J6cN6cup\nTdZiVL91Bxy55orD6WXSf5iv5DSBSQLNDD7mdRRLh7yi+N6fCY2DHpyRPMVou54Q\nPHaQ9FFyomI1fZuGDV1INr5cak3uKUIkx9dLzeOrqZ54phoDqgOaS0vGQnEdgTrM\ndL/QRaE2uzuEtjz2/+Hh3rRTWBdiMCJ81WrQbhQDdekXFyv4byTkgUVoC52ddjEL\npYCpdOmRzaFbRBJRW+pmg0OzxCybtaBZwjXm0nhovlI6ACwzppdxvW09dEd8pmK8\n526VO