"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fuze-agent","id":321521006,"login":"fuze-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEyoFbg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/bcf2e1e5cd1822390d42e778bf5dadf53ebdf0d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:36:28Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:36:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): require tenant admin for grant/revoke and tenant management by human callers (#1246)\n\nPOST/DELETE /authz/grants only gated machine callers, so any authenticated human could grant or revoke any role in any tenant through the Security API.\n\n- New authz-gate: human grant/revoke requires Organization:manage on the TARGET tenant (admin / derived org-admin). An instance-scoped grant additionally passes for a holder of manage_access on that exact instance, only for non-tenant-level roles. Default-deny: only a literal true allows, a throwing provider is a 502, a deny is a 403. A keyless resource is gated as tenant-wide; a grantId is resolved to its tenant:subject:role tuple so the authorized tuple is the executed one.\n- GET /authz/grants and /authz/permissions: listing your own is open, another subject needs tenant admin (machine callers need authz:admin).\n- /tenants/:id/* mutations need tenant admin; reads need view_members/read on that tenant; checks run before the tenant lookup.\n- PATCH /authz/subjects/.../attributes is machine-only (authz:admin).\n- Machine grant/revoke path unchanged (AUTHZ_ADMIN_SCOPE).\n- 47 new tests (fail on the old route, pass on the new one); contract documents 403/502; security-client 0.9.1 and the four UI packages that pin it patch-bumped.\n\nKnown callers that relied on the hole: selection-list-service grantListOwner and its access routes (human token). The service is disabled; it must move to a machine identity before it is enabled. Not addressed: POST/GET /tenants remain open to any authenticated caller (needs a design decision).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","tree":{"sha":"d312e686da99a1fa90da81849598ade87473c209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/d312e686da99a1fa90da81849598ade87473c209"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/bcf2e1e5cd1822390d42e778bf5dadf53ebdf0d8","verification":{"payload":"tree d312e686da99a1fa90da81849598ade87473c209\nparent ff7555d8fe4ce457e26534cb7f570ddd41343d12\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791120988 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791120988 +0300\n\nfix(security): require tenant admin for grant/revoke and tenant management by human callers (#1246)\n\nPOST/DELETE /authz/grants only gated machine callers, so any authenticated human could grant or revoke any role in any tenant through the Security API.\n\n- New authz-gate: human grant/revoke requires Organization:manage on the TARGET tenant (admin / derived org-admin). An instance-scoped grant additionally passes for a holder of manage_access on that exact instance, only for non-tenant-level roles. Default-deny: only a literal true allows, a throwing provider is a 502, a deny is a 403. A keyless resource is gated as tenant-wide; a grantId is resolved to its tenant:subject:role tuple so the authorized tuple is the executed one.\n- GET /authz/grants and /authz/permissions: listing your own is open, another subject needs tenant admin (machine callers need authz:admin).\n- /tenants/:id/* mutations need tenant admin; reads need view_members/read on that tenant; checks run before the tenant lookup.\n- PATCH /authz/subjects/.../attributes is machine-only (authz:admin).\n- Machine grant/revoke path unchanged (AUTHZ_ADMIN_SCOPE).\n- 47 new tests (fail on the old route, pass on the new one); contract documents 403/502; security-client 0.9.1 and the four UI packages that pin it patch-bumped.\n\nKnown callers that relied on the hole: selection-list-service grantListOwner and its access routes (human token). The service is disabled; it must move to a machine identity before it is enabled. Not addressed: POST/GET /tenants remain open to any authenticated caller (needs a design decision).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwlZcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAmMQACZRMLAm33redwfOPsIEadTW\nu8xyFPrlZ+gn/ltI3fUUdVWafft7JNEMt6ShftRN+mayy74XpEtYbAjLqyN4xaf2\nqaqNKyvjuZcbPKsk6q4LbHlOZe7A3wYCRFT/EAOl/fODveKR2vDy6dgdvGWgI7lK\nQ1wl6EuFozLPhmtWCFgz3pRLL9+GHsQ43dle3sj4d0U+rE8ItMNibM6QGKV2OY7V\nx5KU7FjG57r5R0BfP32FzXv+6Lyi4H9hFNF4MMDcCdm9+L0ktvZr8SIlBOLgAoUE\nn++8BnOvpU5qQex5Le3SlLWo8fxfkeMfrqvD78QG7o2xBT8ZNlF9Syb4M8kffXRF\nK+eu1fY14MSnpdpZeLQghcAEA2615RjFUixoOcpy03R8woaCDENDxzx9NBL96KON\nwQRp02mup+leWOOJYnm0Q