https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/ff7555d8fe4ce457e26534cb7f570ddd41343d12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:33:33Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:33:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): fuze-code-review fails closed: no codex/gemini keys forwarded, no persisted token (#1243)\n\nThe review workflow claimed the reviewer has no Bash/Write/Edit, but that held only for the Anthropic rungs. On fallover the OpenAI rung ran danger-full-access (a full shell on the runner) and the Gemini rung runs --yolo, while actions/checkout left the job GITHUB_TOKEN (pull-requests: write) in .git/config. A prompt-injected PR diff could run commands and use the token.\n\n- fuze-code-review.yml: OPENAI_API_KEY and GEMINI_API_KEY are no longer forwarded; fuze-code-action only runs those rungs when their key is non-empty, so both are skipped by name. The checkout uses persist-credentials: false (base-ref fetch authenticated explicitly, submit step names GH_REPO). Header and comments state what is true per rung.\n- test_review_caller_readonly.py, wired into gate-fuze-code-action: read-only-intent callers must not forward those keys, must not persist credentials and must not put an env block on the LLM step, and the action must still gate both rungs on their key.\n- An exhausted chain still classifies as an availability outage (non-blocking). Classification code is untouched.\n\nA dedicated review-only switch has to be proposed upstream: fuze-code-action is FuzeSDLC-managed and governance-sync resets local edits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","tree":{"sha":"81fa56dcc10a94b4ec8790298cb6774b5035153e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/81fa56dcc10a94b4ec8790298cb6774b5035153e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/ff7555d8fe4ce457e26534cb7f570ddd41343d12","verification":{"payload":"tree 81fa56dcc10a94b4ec8790298cb6774b5035153e\nparent 5fc4e274f60d39d8eebc6dd32d6988fce43ece6c\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791120813 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791120813 +0300\n\nfix(ci): fuze-code-review fails closed: no codex/gemini keys forwarded, no persisted token (#1243)\n\nThe review workflow claimed the reviewer has no Bash/Write/Edit, but that held only for the Anthropic rungs. On fallover the OpenAI rung ran danger-full-access (a full shell on the runner) and the Gemini rung runs --yolo, while actions/checkout left the job GITHUB_TOKEN (pull-requests: write) in .git/config. A prompt-injected PR diff could run commands and use the token.\n\n- fuze-code-review.yml: OPENAI_API_KEY and GEMINI_API_KEY are no longer forwarded; fuze-code-action only runs those rungs when their key is non-empty, so both are skipped by name. The checkout uses persist-credentials: false (base-ref fetch authenticated explicitly, submit step names GH_REPO). Header and comments state what is true per rung.\n- test_review_caller_readonly.py, wired into gate-fuze-code-action: read-only-intent callers must not forward those keys, must not persist credentials and must not put an env block on the LLM step, and the action must still gate both rungs on their key.\n- An exhausted chain still classifies as an availability outage (non-blocking). Classification code is untouched.\n\nA dedicated review-only switch has to be proposed upstream: fuze-code-action is FuzeSDLC-managed and governance-sync resets local edits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018PKRvNfpskTKPUfDc8X1G1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwlWtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnpgQABYL+h4PKZPpKHVoV3/Ah2xY\n0yBsysPA8zZpdGNKxRUq6T9kzfc2WlDVtGwfeuBeVoZ9WVew35lnDsAIsGYPeIFr\n0EAsaBudjn2I7WO/oa5xqvT1XdxFZKseqVfgXyQTQWHc3OdtlArIk8/10J8V3ANN\n2tIMfTg/ffIezeqadPTKeY/vgv/hKhgbSkb9Hhv3oCwYMmqzxpTd8Nzi7xQHrOse\n9j3IF3U1O21HXNXGrfd90Da9AuSIL0/LCTeQpOJUQfGsZv6TrMfbcgp4dh5tusBn\nPQGF94rgCo7xaaKBgZxRpE0QVlYhQsAY0EmcxyzmN/53+u/eEJwG5cRmLnShGXg5\nnD9QWHQRVGQ7FYGljt4gOFOlE4wF2uCW34SldR9Xw+DFAQjxtW0KpZd6Gf495Hp1\nJ4jxSby5tYzDrhR7ToS/UL1cZNoVEFCTogj/TW6/fC5bmTRh4P7ix+uC14siqfH3\nTnG7saQiKNOCBsc7TVDoxTdlV7BIen+bQwm1k5VL13E6T/bmPdttK/yvke4m1nX8\nI44s48cEy+uwsAGi9wGXgnbcEINX1HVZofbw6t74fSH9lf0vTK/gMKJIUxz43kwk\nC9b93EbAGofonrf8bnhnhGdnyzMZFv13U3pYOBTMzCWMbcPNZuQBTOaRaVvrUNO6\nklQ9CAXt6jMbOSi2xUJt\n=be5Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T13:33:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://githu