atar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/37cb78f151a098e154e9b691ca778972faafcd91","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDM3Y2I3OGYxNTFhMDk4ZTE1NGU5YjY5MWNhNzc4OTcyZmFhZmNkOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/c446e4e3c3daa80979f06e4125c7f48ad66a6751","sha":"c446e4e3c3daa80979f06e4125c7f48ad66a6751","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c446e4e3c3daa80979f06e4125c7f48ad66a6751"}],"sha":"37cb78f151a098e154e9b691ca778972faafcd91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/37cb78f151a098e154e9b691ca778972faafcd91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fuze-agent","id":321521006,"login":"fuze-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEyoFbg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/c446e4e3c3daa80979f06e4125c7f48ad66a6751/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T12:24:32Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T12:24:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(rbac): grant the ARC runner read on fuzefront-secrets for prod-synthetic-admin (#1237)\n\n## Problem\n\n`prod-synthetic-admin.yml` (the dispatchable ops workflow that\nprovisions the post-prod master-admin synthetic for the Portals\ndirectory smoke) reads `INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET` from the\n`fuzefront-secrets` Secret via the k8s API, using the runner pod''s\nmounted ServiceAccount token — the same mechanism `prod-unleash-ops.yml`\nuses for `unleash-secrets`.\n\nBut the runner''s Role (`unleash-runner-secret-reader`) was\n`resourceNames`-scoped to **`unleash-secrets` alone**. So the GET on\n`fuzefront-secrets` 403''d and the workflow failed:\n\n```\n##[error]Could not read INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET from the fuzefront-secrets Secret.\nCheck the runner SA can get secret/fuzefront-secrets in the fuzefront namespace (same RBAC as unleash-secrets).\n```\n\n(Observed on run `37201208289`, step \"Provision the synthetic\nmaster-admin\".)\n\n## Fix\n\nGeneralise the Role: it now grants `get` on `unleash.secretName`\n**plus** every name in a new `unleash.ciRunner.extraSecretNames` list.\n\n- Base `values.yaml`: `extraSecretNames: []` — dev/local stays\nleast-privilege (`unleash-secrets` only).\n- `values-prod.yaml`: adds `fuzefront-secrets`.\n\nStill an explicit `resourceNames` allowlist — **never** a blanket\n`secrets: get`.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n# prod render\nresourceNames:\n  - \"unleash-secrets\"\n  - \"fuzefront-secrets\"\n\n# base render\nresourceNames:\n  - \"unleash-secrets\"\n```\n\n`helm lint … -f values-prod.yaml` → `1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s)\nfailed`.\n\nOnce merged (master deploys on push; Argo syncs the Role),\nre-dispatching `prod-synthetic-admin.yml` will read the secret, grant\n`admin`, and the post-prod Portals smoke''s list-contents test can run.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0127R9Zcw92tmBkxUUuLEB79\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9a083eb2411785c1881ffe2eff0657b86ba7a32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/f9a083eb2411785c1881ffe2eff0657b86ba7a32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/c446e4e3c3daa80979f06e4125c7f48ad66a6751","verification":{"payload":"tree f9a083eb2411785c1881ffe2eff0657b86ba7a32\nparent 433b20fd5a5bce595ad9559ab424fbf0d0b1bf9e\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791116672 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791116672 +0300\n\nfix(rbac): grant the ARC runner read on fuzefront-secrets for prod-synthetic-admin (#1237)\n\n## Problem\n\n`prod-synthetic-admin.yml` (the dispatchable ops workflow that\nprovisions the post-prod master-admin synthetic for the Portals\ndirectory smoke) reads `INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET` from the\n`fuzefront-secrets` Secret via the k8s API, using the runner pod''s\nmounted ServiceAccount token — the same mechanism `prod-unleash-ops.yml`\nuses for `unleash-secrets`.\n\nBut the runner''s Role (`unleash-runner-secret-reader`) was\n`resourceNames`-scoped to **`unleash-secrets` alone**. So the GET on\n`fuzefront-secrets` 403''d and the workflow failed:\n\n```\n##[error]Could not read INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET from the fuzefront-secrets Secret.\nCheck the runner SA can get secret/fuzefront-secrets in the fuzefront namespace (same RBAC as unleash-secrets).\n```\n\n(Observed on run `37201208289`, step \"Provision the synthetic\nmaster-admin\".)\n\n## Fix\n\nGeneralise the Role: it now grants `get` on `unleash.secretName`\n**plus** every name in a new `unleash.ciRunner.extraSecretNames` list.\n\n- Base `values.yaml`: `extraSecretNames: []` — dev/local stays\nleast-privilege (`unleash-secrets` only).\n- `values-prod.yaml`: adds `fuzefront-secrets`.\n\nStill an explicit `resourceNames` allowlist — **never** a blanket\n`secrets: get`.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n# prod render\nresourceNames:\n  - \"unleash-secrets\"\n  - \"fuzefront-secrets\"\n\n# base render\nresourceNames:\n  - \"unleash-secrets\"\n```\n\n`helm lint … -f values-prod.yaml` → `1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s)\nfailed`.\n\nOnce merged (master deploys on push; Argo syncs the Role),\nre-dispatching `prod-synthetic-admin.yml` will read the secret, grant\n`admin`, and the post-prod Portals smoke''s list-contents test can run.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0127R9Zcw92tmBkxUUuLEB79\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwkWACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJo0QAKUOs9j4kmpo4htfUxS4IHSN\nKyNZ40Y7+FRyweKHYFQWgcEEe4+OpHK/6N17rs6htqLtcef5RB45o0Yv35h9+7E8\n38HIuiSfpIEGdENFyex6PJkRViS/yi/PRZFNk+4NyHKuNivXd17uFEhBNTJWHJc4\nNVlDXdeDn5mBA8sOylcjdSGYCe/YazvwcvY7b70SFvdCiEqu+t3Ul0MX2WoDCYZx\nr7jAf84v57/p99hRvueLENR4PMQlXN/nUyjay5A/wnjozGrTy01bomjWKn9oJRHc\nPUixuaELJzLYchyslimG2AW9dHehXPK66A/CMZXmKA/hc38zhAQF3yzn3VCQpojQ\nKhy+59JbJED4O2qb0AuHRlx+6qa1CGGzZLbGdDr6XSYfoPwhlSGNifq36CNyp6T