commits/55a87246e559fc59886bd03249aab4f9d682152a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:48:47Z","email":"release-bump@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuzefront-release"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:48:47Z","email":"release-bump@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuzefront-release"},"message":"release: fuzefront images 848485db4f8c [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"911defff289721c10aed72e518537ef7ea7c5fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/911defff289721c10aed72e518537ef7ea7c5fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/55a87246e559fc59886bd03249aab4f9d682152a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/55a87246e559fc59886bd03249aab4f9d682152a","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDU1YTg3MjQ2ZTU1OWZjNTk4ODZiZDAzMjQ5YWFiNGY5ZDY4MjE1MmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081","sha":"848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081"}],"sha":"55a87246e559fc59886bd03249aab4f9d682152a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/55a87246e559fc59886bd03249aab4f9d682152a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fuze-agent","id":321521006,"login":"fuze-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEyoFbg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuze-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:16:21Z","email":"321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuze-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:16:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(internal): admin-grant endpoint + prod-synthetic-admin ops workflow (#1235)\n\n## 📋 Description\nAutomates provisioning the post-prod **master-admin synthetic** (used by\nthe Portals directory smoke''s list-contents test, #1223), removing the\none manual step that otherwise needs a human: granting the account the\n`admin` role — a prod DB write, because the platform has **no self-serve\nadmin grant** (public signup only mints `[\"user\"]`, and the directory\ngates on `requireRole([''admin''])`).\n\n## 🔧 Changes\n**Backend — `POST /internal/set-roles`**\n(`backend/src/routes/internal.ts`)\n- Sets `users.roles` by email, gated by the same `x-internal-secret`\n(`INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET`) + constant-time compare as `/provision`,\n**cluster-internal only** (never ingress-exposed).\n- `roles` validated against a tight allowlist\n`{user,admin,developer,employee}`; normalises to always include `user`,\ndedupes (idempotent); 404 on unknown email; case-insensitive match.\n- Factored the shared-secret check into `internalSecretOk()`; added\n`internal-set-roles.test.ts` (401 / 400 / 404 / 200 + dedupe +\nidempotency).\n\n**Ops — `.github/workflows/prod-synthetic-admin.yml`** (dispatchable,\nin-cluster `fuzefront` runner, mirrors `prod-unleash-ops.yml`)\n- Reads `INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET` from the `fuzefront-secrets` Secret\nvia the k8s API, self-provisions the account via public signup when\nabsent, grants `admin` via `/internal/set-roles`, and verifies the\naccount can read `GET /api/v1/admin/portals`.\n\n## 🔑 Owner-only prerequisite (unchanged)\nSet the `POST_PROD_ADMIN_EMAIL` / `POST_PROD_ADMIN_PASSWORD` repo\nsecrets first — writing GitHub secrets isn''t something a workflow can do\nwithout an admin PAT. Once set, **dispatch `prod-synthetic-admin.yml`\nonce** and the Portals smoke''s list-contents assertion goes live on\nevery deploy.\n\n## ✅ Verification\n- `internal.ts`: 3 routes, balanced; new endpoint + `db` import present.\n- `internal-set-roles.test.ts` mirrors the existing\n`internal-provision.test.ts` integration pattern (real test DB).\n- `prod-synthetic-admin.yml` parses; reuses the proven\ncluster-secret-read + verify shape from `prod-unleash-ops.yml`.\n\nA role is a rollout/break-glass marker — real authorization stays in\nPermit; the endpoint never bypasses it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0127R9Zcw92tmBkxUUuLEB79\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9c89b27f8ad619b0353c9a7c44e07b8e43e9d95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/a9c89b27f8ad619b0353c9a7c44e07b8e43e9d95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081","verification":{"payload":"tree a9c89b27f8ad619b0353c9a7c44e07b8e43e9d95\nparent 5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85\nauthor fuze-agent[bot] <321521006+fuze-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791112581 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791112581 +0300\n\nfeat(internal): admin-grant endpoint + prod-synthetic-admin ops workflow (#1235)\n\n## 📋 Description\nAutomates provisioning the post-prod **master-admin synthetic** (used by\nthe Portals directory smoke''s list-contents test, #1223), removing the\none manual step that otherwise needs a human: granting the account the\n`admin` role — a prod DB write, because the platform has **no self-serve\nadmin grant** (public signup only mints `[\"user\"]`, and the directory\ngates on `requireRole([''admin''])`).\n\n## 🔧 Changes\n**Backend — `POST /internal/set-roles`**\n(`backend/src/routes/internal.ts`)\n- Sets `users.roles` by email, gated by the same `x-internal-secret`\n(`INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET`) + constant-time compare as `/provision`,\n**cluster-internal only** (never ingress-exposed).\n- `roles` validated against a tight allowlist\n`{user,admin,developer,employee}`; normalises to always include `user`,\ndedupes (idempotent); 404 on unknown email; case-insensitive match.\n- Factored the shared-secret check into `internalSecretOk()`; added\n`internal-set-roles.test.ts` (401 / 400 / 404 / 200 + dedupe +\nidempotency).\n\n**Ops — `.github/workflows/prod-synthetic-admin.yml`** (dispatchable,\nin-cluster `fuzefront` runner, mirrors `prod-unleash-ops.yml`)\n- Reads `INTERNAL_PROVISION_SECRET` from the `fuzefront-secrets` Secret\nvia the k8s API, self-provisions the account via public signup when\nabsent, grants `admin` via `/internal/set-roles`, and verifies the\naccount can read `GET /api/v1/admin/portals`.\n\n## 🔑 Owner-only prerequisite (unchanged)\nSet the `POST_PROD_ADMIN_EMAIL` / `POST_PROD_ADMIN_PASSWORD` repo\nsecrets first — writing GitHub secrets isn''t something a workflow can do\nwithout an admin PAT. Once set, **dispatch `prod-synthetic-admin.yml`\nonce** and the Portals smoke''s list-contents assertion goes live on\nevery deploy.\n\n## ✅ Verification\n- `internal.ts`: 3 routes, balanced; new endpoint + `db` import present.\n- `internal-set-roles.test.ts` mirrors the existing\n`internal-provision.test.ts` integration pattern (real test DB).\n- `prod-synthetic-admin.yml` parses; reuses the proven\ncluster-secret-read + verify shape from `prod-unleash-ops.yml`.\n\nA role is a rollout/break-glass marker — real authorization stays in\nPermit; the endpoint never bypasses it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0127R9Zcw92tmBkxUUuLEB79\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwjWFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOogQAAjPh+52JL8sCS0AHEajJfDp\ny/4tzQxuXkXC56tdbI+/AYtqrWyyRdliaRnR8L9vAlqdgry5rlIMuhodprORbOYV\nECX+ln/E1qEYQjPdQk3924GysRm4PQ2x7E2ibrkTdDEdw4EjtfQpJxYDiB1Cn1MC\nc9FRMfR+seOlW0qI+6bQtt/WV1OTo0lPpnXp4Z9MFqKnMUafL9qoD7JS04CZneJn\nTuCBgY17JdQwAaoRveqiyIVS5JWE9R4gStDl/UTZl98YzrpJfPhrgt6VUMx4tNTQ\nmwh0RHFDk8UqVcZMWegNrAeUNL7ki9qvdypHyZC7HqlSF1LJ4WImPwwPVper9xTm\nAu6KHVoCeuGJx/yIuuY1MZzYtBus5c3sk7N4NL0gWtJw66DXZjxx/Y24HUyabjNy\nGcU5t0p6nU7q/nCCACNIksLiJzBr/C5vKzqa9uG+sAv/8mwhhgGOx0mG/2kImsMG\nq02xb4SlAGj07qtWVJmcRTpXGOKf0B2GWNfn7ZTg1yjk8RKQVJHimXNIeizfp+OK\n3/Gi1bO/klLLxbj+16sxeXKaOA/5BL9OWq1hTdcR2g5R94h1Ih85SYzIz5OzcxeU\nLVSEpKieKXPErDGEggD9FQjPRiRi5FyLnrOfqlaYqTBKf1vOyemzEzrTDK+Qz+KZ\nSyX7jNlBgO3KcvtCSw2M\n=cljd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T11:16:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDg0ODQ4NWRiNGY4Y2UyN2QxMDEyNjdjZjA2MjZkZTQ3ODU3NDAwODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85","sha":"5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85"}],"sha":"848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/848485db4f8ce27d101267cf0626de4785740081"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:30:25Z","email":"release-bump@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuzefront-release"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:30:25Z","email":"release-bump@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fuzefront-release"},"message":"release: fuzefront images 02753b6ffd64 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"01ae0c706400929b56173aa80e72d39cc4f6e931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/01ae0c706400929b56173aa80e72d39cc4f6e931"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDU3MjhjNzU1ZWJjMWRhMDlmZjYwNmNkYWFlYTdiZWFlYTg1YTJiODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8","sha":"49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8"}],"sha":"5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/5728c755ebc1da09ff606cdaaea7beaea85a2b85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:21:27Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:21:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(config-service): right-to-erasure for history actors + per-topic gate exemption (#1216)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nImplements the two owner decisions that PR #1156 deliberately deferred\nfor the config-service identity-lifecycle consumer. Both were decided\nvia a Fable 5.1 consult on 2026-10-04; this PR implements the verdicts.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- ✨ New feature (non-breaking, additive) — a new `actorRedacted` field\nand a per-topic gate exemption mechanism.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n### Decision 1 — right-to-erasure for `config_history` actors (migration\n005)\n\nOn `identity.user.deleted(cascade=''hard'')`, the deleted user''s id is now\nredacted from the append-only audit trail: on their `''user''` rows,\n`actor_id → NULL` and a new `actor_redacted → TRUE`, while `actor_type`\nstays `''user''`.\n\n- **A silent `actor_id = NULL` was rejected** — it is indistinguishable\nfrom a system action (migration 004''s invariant: `actor_id` NULL iff\n`actor_type=''system''`). The explicit flag keeps human-vs-system legible\nwhile meeting the erasure obligation.\n- **A UUID sentinel was rejected** — `actor_id` is a native UUID\nsurfaced as a TypeID id; a fabricated sentinel would violate\n`governance/identifier-standard.md` and read as a real user. (The\nsibling `selection-list-service` uses a `''[deleted-user]''` string\nbecause its authorship columns are TEXT — a UUID column takes a flag, a\nTEXT column takes a sentinel.)\n- This is **the one sanctioned in-place mutation** of an otherwise\nappend-only table, and it changes only WHO (`actor_id`,\n`actor_redacted`) — never WHAT\n(`action`/`old_value`/`new_value`/`occurred_at`).\n- Migration 005 also promotes 004''s comment-only invariant to a **CHECK\nconstraint**, extended three-ways for the redacted state.\n- Soft delete is unchanged: a deactivated user is restorable, so their\nauthorship is retained.\n\nFiles: `migrations/005_*.sql` (+ 004 comment),\n`events/user-deleted.handler.ts`, `repositories/history.repository.ts`,\n`types.ts`, `routes/{config,secrets}.write.ts` (write-path actors set\n`false`), `openapi.yaml` (`info.version` 1.1.0 → 1.2.0, additive\n`Actor.actorRedacted`).\n\n### Decision 2 — per-topic `notApplicable` gate exemption for sparse\nstores\n\nconfig-service''s `created`-handlers have nothing to seed\n(`config_values` is a sparse override store; a new org/user inherits via\n`platform→portal→org→user`). An empty handler is the exact *\"subscribes\nand seeds nothing\"* vacuity `gate-microservice-events` rejects, and\nleaving a correct service on the `knownUnhandled` ratchet forever erodes\nthe ratchet''s meaning.\n\nAdded a **per-topic `notApplicable`** declaration, enforced\nnon-abusable:\n- reason mandatory, ≥ 40 chars;\n- **never all four** topics for one service (that is `exempt`, a\nseparately-reviewed decision);\n- **mutually exclusive** with `knownUnhandled`/`exempt`;\n- declaring a topic N/A **and** binding a handler for it fails\n(contradiction);\n- a declaration for an **undiscovered** service fails (no stale\ndeclarations);\n- the seeds/effect check still runs over the topics a service *does*\nsubscribe to.\n\nconfig-service moves off the ratchet into `notApplicable` for the two\n`created` events. `devportal`/`notification` remain real seed debt;\n`email`/`sms`/`payment` are future N/A candidates once they handle the\n`deleted` pair.\n\nFiles: `scripts/gate_microservice_events.py` (validator + loop +\n`--report`), `governance/microservice-events-policy.json`.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n\n```bash\n# config-service\ncd services/config-service && npx tsc --noEmit && npx jest        # 313/313 pass\n# gate\npython3 -m unittest scripts.__tests__.test_gate_microservice_events   # 19/19 pass\npython3 scripts/gate_microservice_events.py --repo . --policy governance/microservice-events-policy.json   # OK\nnode scripts/check-version-bump.mjs --base origin/master           # OK (openapi bumped)\npython3 scripts/gate_openapi_conformance.py .                      # OK\n```\n\nNew tests: history redaction targets only `''user''` rows, runs inside the\ndelete transaction, rolls back on failure (no half-erasure); soft delete\nleaves history untouched; gate — N/A covers the gap and passes, all-four\nfails, short reason fails, contradiction fails, dual-listing fails,\nundiscovered-service fails, and a no-op `deleted` handler still fails.\n\n## 🚨 Breaking Changes\n\nNone. `Actor.actorRedacted` is an additive, always-present response\nfield (minor version bump). No migration required by consumers;\nmigration 005 is idempotent and backfills `FALSE`.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n\n- [x] Requires database migration —\n`005_config_history_actor_redacted.sql`, idempotent, runs on startup. It\nadds a CHECK constraint enforcing the (system / live-user /\nredacted-user) invariant; existing rows satisfy it because the append\npath has always set `actor_id` per that invariant.\n\n### Open items deliberately not in scope\n\n- `email`/`sms`/`payment`/`selection-list` stay on `knownUnhandled` —\neach needs its own `deleted`-handler (or N/A-on-`created`) in a later\nPR; noted in the policy `$comment`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CD1KiuhuHZAooZJMFRbkpo\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01CD1KiuhuHZAooZJMFRbkpo)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"465a7ad8d7e637d9bc6526e56f7946f6148fabc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/465a7ad8d7e637d9bc6526e56f7946f6148fabc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 465a7ad8d7e637d9bc6526e56f7946f6148fabc0\nparent ed4f3062b1ed2483cb7620afa1132a59895923c1\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791109287 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791109287 +0000\n\nfeat(config-service): right-to-erasure for history actors + per-topic gate exemption (#1216)\n\n## 📋 Description\n\nImplements the two owner decisions that PR #1156 deliberately deferred\nfor the config-service identity-lifecycle consumer. Both were decided\nvia a Fable 5.1 consult on 2026-10-04; this PR implements the verdicts.\n\n## 🔄 Type of Change\n\n- ✨ New feature (non-breaking, additive) — a new `actorRedacted` field\nand a per-topic gate exemption mechanism.\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Details\n\n### Decision 1 — right-to-erasure for `config_history` actors (migration\n005)\n\nOn `identity.user.deleted(cascade=''hard'')`, the deleted user''s id is now\nredacted from the append-only audit trail: on their `''user''` rows,\n`actor_id → NULL` and a new `actor_redacted → TRUE`, while `actor_type`\nstays `''user''`.\n\n- **A silent `actor_id = NULL` was rejected** — it is indistinguishable\nfrom a system action (migration 004''s invariant: `actor_id` NULL iff\n`actor_type=''system''`). The explicit flag keeps human-vs-system legible\nwhile meeting the erasure obligation.\n- **A UUID sentinel was rejected** — `actor_id` is a native UUID\nsurfaced as a TypeID id; a fabricated sentinel would violate\n`governance/identifier-standard.md` and read as a real user. (The\nsibling `selection-list-service` uses a `''[deleted-user]''` string\nbecause its authorship columns are TEXT — a UUID column takes a flag, a\nTEXT column takes a sentinel.)\n- This is **the one sanctioned in-place mutation** of an otherwise\nappend-only table, and it changes only WHO (`actor_id`,\n`actor_redacted`) — never WHAT\n(`action`/`old_value`/`new_value`/`occurred_at`).\n- Migration 005 also promotes 004''s comment-only invariant to a **CHECK\nconstraint**, extended three-ways for the redacted state.\n- Soft delete is unchanged: a deactivated user is restorable, so their\nauthorship is retained.\n\nFiles: `migrations/005_*.sql` (+ 004 comment),\n`events/user-deleted.handler.ts`, `repositories/history.repository.ts`,\n`types.ts`, `routes/{config,secrets}.write.ts` (write-path actors set\n`false`), `openapi.yaml` (`info.version` 1.1.0 → 1.2.0, additive\n`Actor.actorRedacted`).\n\n### Decision 2 — per-topic `notApplicable` gate exemption for sparse\nstores\n\nconfig-service''s `created`-handlers have nothing to seed\n(`config_values` is a sparse override store; a new org/user inherits via\n`platform→portal→org→user`). An empty handler is the exact *\"subscribes\nand seeds nothing\"* vacuity `gate-microservice-events` rejects, and\nleaving a correct service on the `knownUnhandled` ratchet forever erodes\nthe ratchet''s meaning.\n\nAdded a **per-topic `notApplicable`** declaration, enforced\nnon-abusable:\n- reason mandatory, ≥ 40 chars;\n- **never all four** topics for one service (that is `exempt`, a\nseparately-reviewed decision);\n- **mutually exclusive** with `knownUnhandled`/`exempt`;\n- declaring a topic N/A **and** binding a handler for it fails\n(contradiction);\n- a declaration for an **undiscovered** service fails (no stale\ndeclarations);\n- the seeds/effect check still runs over the topics a service *does*\nsubscribe to.\n\nconfig-service moves off the ratchet into `notApplicable` for the two\n`created` events. `devportal`/`notification` remain real seed debt;\n`email`/`sms`/`payment` are future N/A candidates once they handle the\n`deleted` pair.\n\nFiles: `scripts/gate_microservice_events.py` (validator + loop +\n`--report`), `governance/microservice-events-policy.json`.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n\n- [x] Unit tests\n\n```bash\n# config-service\ncd services/config-service && npx tsc --noEmit && npx jest        # 313/313 pass\n# gate\npython3 -m unittest scripts.__tests__.test_gate_microservice_events   # 19/19 pass\npython3 scripts/gate_microservice_events.py --repo . --policy governance/microservice-events-policy.json   # OK\nnode scripts/check-version-bump.mjs --base origin/master           # OK (openapi bumped)\npython3 scripts/gate_openapi_conformance.py .                      # OK\n```\n\nNew tests: history redaction targets only `''user''` rows, runs inside the\ndelete transaction, rolls back on failure (no half-erasure); soft delete\nleaves history untouched; gate — N/A covers the gap and passes, all-four\nfails, short reason fails, contradiction fails, dual-listing fails,\nundiscovered-service fails, and a no-op `deleted` handler still fails.\n\n## 🚨 Breaking Changes\n\nNone. `Actor.actorRedacted` is an additive, always-present response\nfield (minor version bump). No migration required by consumers;\nmigration 005 is idempotent and backfills `FALSE`.\n\n## 📝 Additional Notes\n\n### Deployment Notes\n\n- [x] Requires database migration —\n`005_config_history_actor_redacted.sql`, idempotent, runs on startup. It\nadds a CHECK constraint enforcing the (system / live-user /\nredacted-user) invariant; existing rows satisfy it because the append\npath has always set `actor_id` per that invariant.\n\n### Open items deliberately not in scope\n\n- `email`/`sms`/`payment`/`selection-list` stay on `knownUnhandled` —\neach needs its own `deleted`-handler (or N/A-on-`created`) in a later\nPR; noted in the policy `$comment`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CD1KiuhuHZAooZJMFRbkpo\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01CD1KiuhuHZAooZJMFRbkpo)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwiinCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx3wQAEQrpj/TRxHPxI8H1LUo6P1F\nL0qQWs19tA1X0pN34Fjn1bhAm0F5goohkhPZrWuz98p9+hYSuEd/UDESME+LJ1Lx\ntDoctl5nJxYZvzaWmP66+XlqOixD5HezNlpqqprFcWg6NSyhis+jtNwWchedb+Cg\n3OdNKEo3LCxquD7fxijg+yrPYmlZu3kmuuqFIrX2JSD3vA2IoHov5Mz5q2cvrmkT\nuwNdEpeb9ACNuPbUbMWRbnVL/rq4G3yr5Pi89kR8WKcIM16lM/G+q5Fn/V8izScC\n3VFf7q2B23M8cIpEyFuqfmXnm8+ib6yqzd6aa/pOXm6cmVbbN0v5a+628eQMx/up\nDDJa4laxAy36v4583VRclpgs5biyun984jlQvwtdVJfgEbZgF2FUz/39txWeHvmF\nZdVTtIFdd0coGOcUeFeG7CCqjbn+J+zQ6dA9ULhR5qf8lbUNHbb4PfNej6wtkjpL\nNe9i0CIAG2YcyHLTAeUocj8IiPzprr/BViaG0rrEktnHP5BJHHZfRk8A3NTJTRh3\nEhNZUs1N37iBCRr0nOCytanMY3k5mTSzoe7mCBZqH9nv4g18oO0Q4pJZwxLddjJp\nDzYybG/mGlotbEuRgEUVg+j2P0CDIXHlj98TLEEN3jpl8/korzbOEUyE3gkuj2q2\ngVKkr3lV0WhJE5QTlhva\n=gpUA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T10:21:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8","node_id":"C_kwDOOzNzMNoAKDQ5MjM4MzY1YWU1MjdkYzFhYzU4NTI1YWM5YzYxYzAxYjBhMzE2Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commit/ed4f3062b1ed2483cb7620afa1132a59895923c1","sha":"ed4f3062b1ed2483cb7620afa1132a59895923c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/ed4f3062b1ed2483cb7620afa1132a59895923c1"}],"sha":"49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/49238365ae527dc1ac58525ac9c61c01b0a316b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/commits/ed4f3062b1ed2483cb7620afa1132a59895923c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:59:48Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:59:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gitops): scope workload-identity RBAC to what needs cluster scope, and gate cluster-scoped kinds against the AppProject (#1226)\n\n## What froze, and why two objects stopped every deploy\n\n`deploy/helm/fuzefront/templates/workload-identity.yaml` (#1190) renders\na `ClusterRole`/`ClusterRoleBinding` that the `fuzefront` AppProject''s\n`clusterResourceWhitelist` did not permit. **Argo does not skip an\nunpermitted resource — it invalidates the sync task and aborts the\nENTIRE sync operation.** So nothing in the whole `fuzefront` Application\nupdated: three successive GitOps image bumps moved zero resources and\nnothing deployed for hours on 2026-09-28. Nothing was *broken*;\neverything was *stale*, which is why it took so long to spot.\n\n`helm lint` and `kubeconform` were green throughout and always would be\n— they validate manifest **shape**, and an Argo AppProject admission\nboundary is in no manifest''s schema. Same class of gap as the Traefik\n`PathPrefix` guard and the NetworkPolicy port guard (FuzeInfra#501)\nalready in `helm-validate.yml`.\n\n## 1. The guardrail (the main deliverable)\n\n`deploy/scripts/check-cluster-scoped-whitelist.sh`, wired into\n`helm-validate.yml` per values overlay. Renders the chart, extracts\nevery cluster-scoped kind, asserts agreement with\n`clusterResourceWhitelist` **read out of `deploy/argocd/project.yaml`**\n— never hardcoded, so it cannot drift from the project it asserts about.\n\nTwo layers:\n\n1. **rendered ⊆ whitelist** — the freeze itself.\n2. **whitelist ⊆ rendered** (closed set) — a cluster-scoped grant must\nnot outlive the template that justified it. This is what makes retiring\nthe workload-authenticator grant an **enforced paired change** rather\nthan a line in a doc: flipping the values gate without also deleting the\ntwo RBAC entries fails CI, and vice versa.\n\n**Fails closed** on a kind absent from its kind→scope table (Kubernetes\ndoes not encode scope in a manifest and a PR runner has no cluster to\nask). Not theoretical — the table was incomplete on first run\n(`NetworkPolicy`) and the gate refused to pass rather than assume.\n\n**Self-test first, 8 cases, proven against the real regression**\n(`governance/vacuous-check-policy.json` — a check only ever observed\npassing is evidence of nothing): the exact 2026-09-28 shape must go RED;\nthe same render against a permitting whitelist GREEN; a group mismatch\nRED (Argo matches group *and* kind); a namespaced-only render GREEN\n(proving namespaced `Role` is not confused with `ClusterRole`); an\nunused grant RED; an unclassified kind RED; an empty/unparseable\nwhitelist RED rather than \"nothing to check\"; `*/*` GREEN so the\nwildcard is honoured.\n\n**Strongest evidence it catches the real thing** — current chart vs\nFuzeInfra''s *actual, unmodified, still-live*\n`argocd/projects/fuzefront.yaml`:\n\n```\nAppProject clusterResourceWhitelist (fuzeinfra-project.yaml):\n  /Namespace\nCluster-scoped resources rendered by the chart:\n  rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRole\n  rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRoleBinding\n::error::the chart renders cluster-scoped ''rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRole'',\n         which the fuzefront AppProject does NOT permit. [...] ABORTS THE WHOLE SYNC\nEXIT=1\n```\n\nAnd the retirement pairing, verified rather than asserted:\n\n```\n$ helm template ... --set securityService.workloadIdentity.clusterRbac.enabled=false\n$ ./deploy/scripts/check-cluster-scoped-whitelist.sh rendered/fuzefront/templates\n::error::... grants cluster-scoped ''rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRole'', but the chart renders no such resource ...\nEXIT=1\n```\n\n## 2. The chart change — the two rules are not the same kind of thing\n\n- **`tokenreviews: create` is irreducible.** TokenReview is a\nnon-namespaced virtual resource; RBAC for it can only be a ClusterRole.\nThe only way to remove it from FuzeFront is to stop doing TokenReviews\nhere.\n- **`configmaps: get,list` never needed cluster scope.**\n`workload-identity.ts:69` reads one namespace, taken from the\nTokenReview result at line 65. As a ClusterRole that was \"read\nConfigMaps in every namespace in the cluster\" — every other product''s\nincluded — to serve an always-single-namespace lookup. **Now a\nnamespaced `Role`+`RoleBinding`.**\n\nCluster RBAC is gated on\n`securityService.workloadIdentity.clusterRbac.enabled` (explicit default\nin `values.yaml`, *not* a render-site `| default` — CLAUDE.md \"Helm\nvalues hygiene\") **and** on `securityService.enabled`: it previously\nrendered unconditionally, granting cluster-wide TokenReview even with\nthe security service switched off, which is the base `values.yaml`\ndefault.\n\n**Default stays ON, deliberately.** `POST\n/api/v1/security/tokens/workload` is a live route\n(`backend/security/src/routes/security.ts:619`) and FuzeInfra''s broker\ndoes not exist yet, so flipping it off today would break workload\nidentity and the FuzeKeys registration #1198 was merged to unblock. The\nflag exists so the eventual flip is one values line rather than a\ntemplate rewrite under pressure.\n\n## 3. Verification\n\n- **Rendered-output diff per overlay** (`values.yaml`,\n`values-local.yaml`, `values-prod.yaml`), as CLAUDE.md requires instead\nof an eyeballed YAML diff: in all three the **only** file that differs\nis `workload-identity.yaml`, delta exactly = `configmaps` rule removed\nfrom the ClusterRole, `Role`+`RoleBinding` added. No other template\nchanged by a byte.\n- `helm lint` clean on all overlays; all YAML re-parsed; AppProject\nwhitelist/destinations semantics unchanged.\n- `gate_workflow_yaml` 0 unparseable · `gate_vacuous_check` OK ·\n`gate_workflow_policy` **120 → 118** findings — the two fixed are this\nworkflow''s own pre-existing `missing-timeout` and\n`missing-concurrency-cancel`. **Zero new findings.**\n\n## 4. This corrects the premise it was investigated under\n\n- **FuzeInfra never widened its whitelist.**\n`argocd/projects/fuzefront.yaml` is still `Namespace`-only, last commit\n`5af55a5d` (2026-08-23, #629).\n- **FuzeFront never stopped rendering the RBAC.**\n`workload-identity.yaml` was untouched since `f7173453` until this PR.\n- **What actually happened:** #1198 widened **FuzeFront''s own** copy\n(merged 07:54:58Z) and FuzeInfra''s `argocd-register` ran **18 seconds\nlater** (07:55:16Z) and applied it. The cluster holds the consumer''s\ncopy, per owner ruling FuzeInfra#639.\n- **`www.fuzefront.com` returning 301 was never evidence about this\nfreeze.** That is FuzeInfra#1278 (DNS/CloudFront brand split), still\nopen. The two were conflated.\n\n### The freeze is not fixed — it is armed\n\nFuzeInfra''s `Namespace`-only copy still exists; its `deploy-prod.yml`\nre-applies `argocd/projects/*.yaml` on any push touching that directory.\n**Nothing reconciles the AppProject continuously** — this repo''s\napp-of-apps watches `deploy/argocd/applications`, not `deploy/argocd` —\nso only the most recent imperative `kubectl apply` is in effect. **The\nnext FuzeInfra push touching `argocd/projects/**` re-freezes\neverything**, with no FuzeFront change involved and nothing in FuzeFront\nCI able to see it.\n\nAlso corrected here: `deploy/argocd/app-of-apps.yaml` claimed the\nin-repo copy \"is strictly narrower than FuzeInfra''s … so applying it\ncannot re-widen anything\" — #1198 made that false, and the direction of\nthe race now matters.\n\n## 5. Delegated — izzywdev/FuzeInfra#1307\n\nFuzeInfra is never edited from a consumer. Requested there: the\n**platform workload-identity broker** (`/v1/verify` over\n`workload-identity.fuzeinfra.svc.cluster.local`, so consumers hold zero\ncluster RBAC and every consumer AppProject stays `Namespace`-only\nforever); **deleting the duplicate AppProject** and managing AppProjects\nvia a self-healing Argo Application so drift is structurally impossible;\nand **alerting** on Argo `Degraded`/`OutOfSync` and on \"desired image ≠\nrunning image\" age — the highest-value item, since it catches this class\nregardless of cause.\n\n**One correction carried into that issue:** the brief proposed asking\nFuzeInfra to make `argocd-register` refuse `kind: AppProject` from a\nconsumer path. That skip *did* land (#629) and was **deliberately\nremoved by owner ruling #639**. Re-adding it would make this repo''s\n`project.yaml` inert, fall back to the `Namespace`-only copy, and\n**immediately re-freeze every FuzeFront deploy.** The issue asks for the\nopposite.\n\n## NOT DONE\n\n- **The broker does not exist; FuzeFront still holds cluster-wide\n`tokenreviews: create`.** This PR *reduces* the grant, it does not\nremove it. Moving ClusterRole authorship to FuzeInfra would fix\ngovernance but not privilege — only the broker removes the capability.\n- The **armed re-freeze** is not fixed here; the fix is FuzeInfra\ndeleting its duplicate (#1307).\n- No production alerting on sync health or image staleness. Delegated.\n- **FuzeKeys end-to-end token exchange not verified against the live\ncluster** — needs a cluster credential this session does not hold, and\nprod is GitOps. The route, RBAC and registration ConfigMaps are all in\nplace; the live exchange is unproven.\n- The gate covers the `fuzefront` chart via the existing\n`values-local`/`values-prod` matrix. `deploy/helm/unleash` and\n`FuzeQuality/deploy/helm/fuzequality` — under the same AppProject — are\n**not** checked; neither renders a cluster-scoped kind today, so there\nis nothing for layer 1 to catch there yet. Extending it is the next\nincrement.\n- The gate is **pre-merge only**. It cannot see a cluster whose\nAppProject was replaced out from under it (§4).\n- Nothing enforces the kind→scope table''s *correctness*, only its\ncompleteness; a kind misclassified as namespaced would wrongly pass\nlayer 1. Known residual.\n\nFull analysis, evidence and limits:\n`docs/planning/workload-identity-layering.md`. Sibling, unrelated: #1202\n(untouched).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_014CG1GaTmY2tbc5DcHLVUSX)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45ba764e302e319c9aa757ec909ba0ae74f86420","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/trees/45ba764e302e319c9aa757ec909ba0ae74f86420"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeFront/git/commits/ed4f3062b1ed2483cb7620afa1132a59895923c1","verification":{"payload":"tree 45ba764e302e319c9aa757ec909ba0ae74f86420\nparent 6614c6497732967d5f23c5a926a1af7288a986a9\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791107988 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791107988 +0000\n\nfix(gitops): scope workload-identity RBAC to what needs cluster scope, and gate cluster-scoped kinds against the AppProject (#1226)\n\n## What froze, and why two objects stopped every deploy\n\n`deploy/helm/fuzefront/templates/workload-identity.yaml` (#1190) renders\na `ClusterRole`/`ClusterRoleBinding` that the `fuzefront` AppProject''s\n`clusterResourceWhitelist` did not permit. **Argo does not skip an\nunpermitted resource — it invalidates the sync task and aborts the\nENTIRE sync operation.** So nothing in the whole `fuzefront` Application\nupdated: three successive GitOps image bumps moved zero resources and\nnothing deployed for hours on 2026-09-28. Nothing was *broken*;\neverything was *stale*, which is why it took so long to spot.\n\n`helm lint` and `kubeconform` were green throughout and always would be\n— they validate manifest **shape**, and an Argo AppProject admission\nboundary is in no manifest''s schema. Same class of gap as the Traefik\n`PathPrefix` guard and the NetworkPolicy port guard (FuzeInfra#501)\nalready in `helm-validate.yml`.\n\n## 1. The guardrail (the main deliverable)\n\n`deploy/scripts/check-cluster-scoped-whitelist.sh`, wired into\n`helm-validate.yml` per values overlay. Renders the chart, extracts\nevery cluster-scoped kind, asserts agreement with\n`clusterResourceWhitelist` **read out of `deploy/argocd/project.yaml`**\n— never hardcoded, so it cannot drift from the project it asserts about.\n\nTwo layers:\n\n1. **rendered ⊆ whitelist** — the freeze itself.\n2. **whitelist ⊆ rendered** (closed set) — a cluster-scoped grant must\nnot outlive the template that justified it. This is what makes retiring\nthe workload-authenticator grant an **enforced paired change** rather\nthan a line in a doc: flipping the values gate without also deleting the\ntwo RBAC entries fails CI, and vice versa.\n\n**Fails closed** on a kind absent from its kind→scope table (Kubernetes\ndoes not encode scope in a manifest and a PR runner has no cluster to\nask). Not theoretical — the table was incomplete on first run\n(`NetworkPolicy`) and the gate refused to pass rather than assume.\n\n**Self-test first, 8 cases, proven against the real regression**\n(`governance/vacuous-check-policy.json` — a check only ever observed\npassing is evidence of nothing): the exact 2026-09-28 shape must go RED;\nthe same render against a permitting whitelist GREEN; a group mismatch\nRED (Argo matches group *and* kind); a namespaced-only render GREEN\n(proving namespaced `Role` is not confused with `ClusterRole`); an\nunused grant RED; an unclassified kind RED; an empty/unparseable\nwhitelist RED rather than \"nothing to check\"; `*/*` GREEN so the\nwildcard is honoured.\n\n**Strongest evidence it catches the real thing** — current chart vs\nFuzeInfra''s *actual, unmodified, still-live*\n`argocd/projects/fuzefront.yaml`:\n\n```\nAppProject clusterResourceWhitelist (fuzeinfra-project.yaml):\n  /Namespace\nCluster-scoped resources rendered by the chart:\n  rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRole\n  rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRoleBinding\n::error::the chart renders cluster-scoped ''rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRole'',\n         which the fuzefront AppProject does NOT permit. [...] ABORTS THE WHOLE SYNC\nEXIT=1\n```\n\nAnd the retirement pairing, verified rather than asserted:\n\n```\n$ helm template ... --set securityService.workloadIdentity.clusterRbac.enabled=false\n$ ./deploy/scripts/check-cluster-scoped-whitelist.sh rendered/fuzefront/templates\n::error::... grants cluster-scoped ''rbac.authorization.k8s.io/ClusterRole'', but the chart renders no such resource ...\nEXIT=1\n```\n\n## 2. The chart change — the two rules are not the same kind of thing\n\n- **`tokenreviews: create` is irreducible.** TokenReview is a\nnon-namespaced virtual resource; RBAC for it can only be a ClusterRole.\nThe only way to remove it from FuzeFront is to stop doing TokenReviews\nhere.\n- **`configmaps: get,list` never needed cluster scope.**\n`workload-identity.ts:69` reads one namespace, taken from the\nTokenReview result at line 65. As a ClusterRole that was \"read\nConfigMaps in every namespace in the cluster\" — every other product''s\nincluded — to serve an always-single-namespace lookup. **Now a\nnamespaced `Role`+`RoleBinding`.**\n\nCluster RBAC is gated on\n`securityService.workloadIdentity.clusterRbac.enabled` (explicit default\nin `values.yaml`, *not* a render-site `| default` — CLAUDE.md \"Helm\nvalues hygiene\") **and** on `securityService.enabled`: it previously\nrendered unconditionally, granting cluster-wide TokenReview even with\nthe security service switched off, which is the base `values.yaml`\ndefault.\n\n**Default stays ON, deliberately.** `POST\n/api/v1/security/tokens/workload` is a live route\n(`backend/security/src/routes/security.ts:619`) and FuzeInfra''s broker\ndoes not exist yet, so flipping it off today would break workload\nidentity and the FuzeKeys registration #1198 was merged to unblock. The\nflag exists so the eventual flip is one values line rather than a\ntemplate rewrite under pressure.\n\n## 3. Verification\n\n- **Rendered-output diff per overlay** (`values.yaml`,\n`values-local.yaml`, `values-prod.yaml`), as CLAUDE.md requires instead\nof an eyeballed YAML diff: in all three the **only** file that differs\nis `workload-identity.yaml`, delta exactly = `configmaps` rule removed\nfrom the ClusterRole, `Role`+`RoleBinding` added. No other template\nchanged by a byte.\n- `helm lint` clean on all overlays; all YAML re-parsed; AppProject\nwhitelist/destinations semantics unchanged.\n- `gate_workflow_yaml` 0 unparseable · `gate_vacuous_check` OK ·\n`gate_workflow_policy` **120 → 118** findings — the two fixed are this\nworkflow''s own pre-existing `missing-timeout` and\n`missing-concurrency-cancel`. **Zero new findings.**\n\n## 4. This corrects the premise it was investigated under\n\n- **FuzeInfra never widened its whitelist.**\n`argocd/projects/fuzefront.yaml` is still `Namespace`-only, last commit\n`5af55a5d` (2026-08-23, #629).\n- **FuzeFront never stopped rendering the RBAC.**\n`workload-identity.yaml` was untouched since `f7173453` until this PR.\n- **What actually happened:** #1198 widened **FuzeFront''s own** copy\n(merged 07:54:58Z) and FuzeInfra''s `argocd-register` ran **18 seconds\nlater** (07:55:16Z) and applied it. The cluster holds the consumer''s\ncopy, per owner ruling FuzeInfra#639.\n- **`www.fuzefront.com` returning 301 was never evidence about this\nfreeze.** That is FuzeInfra#1278 (DNS/CloudFront brand split), still\nopen. The two were conflated.\n\n### The freeze is not fixed — it is armed\n\nFuzeInfra''s `Namespace`-only copy still exists; its `deploy-prod.yml`\nre-applies `argocd/projects/*.yaml` on any push touching that directory.\n**Nothing reconciles the AppProject continuously** — this repo''s\napp-of-apps watches `deploy/argocd/applications`, not `deploy/argocd` —\nso only the most recent imperative `kubectl apply` is in effect. **The\nnext FuzeInfra push touching `argocd/projects/**` re-freezes\neverything**, with no FuzeFront change involved and nothing in FuzeFront\nCI able to see it.\n\nAlso corrected here: `deploy/argocd/app-of-apps.yaml` claimed the\nin-repo copy \"is strictly narrower than FuzeInfra''s … so applying it\ncannot re-widen anything\" — #1198 made that false, and the direction of\nthe race now matters.\n\n## 5. Delegated — izzywdev/FuzeInfra#1307\n\nFuzeInfra is never edited from a consumer. Requested there: the\n**platform workload-identity broker** (`/v1/verify` over\n`workload-identity.fuzeinfra.svc.cluster.local`, so consumers hold zero\ncluster RBAC and every consumer AppProject stays `Namespace`-only\nforever); **deleting the duplicate AppProject** and managing AppProjects\nvia a self-healing Argo Application so drift is structurally impossible;\nand **alerting** on Argo `Degraded`/`OutOfSync` and on \"desired image ≠\nrunning image\" age — the highest-value item, since it catches this class\nregardless of cause.\n\n**One correction carried into that issue:** the brief proposed asking\nFuzeInfra to make `argocd-register` refuse `kind: AppProject` from a\nconsumer path. That skip *did* land (#629) and was **deliberately\nremoved by owner ruling #639**. Re-adding it would make this repo''s\n`project.yaml` inert, fall back to the `Namespace`-only copy, and\n**immediately re-freeze every FuzeFront deploy.** The issue asks for the\nopposite.\n\n## NOT DONE\n\n- **The broker does not exist; FuzeFront still holds cluster-wide\n`tokenreviews: create`.** This PR *reduces* the grant, it does not\nremove it. Moving ClusterRole authorship to FuzeInfra would fix\ngovernance but not privilege — only the broker removes the capability.\n- The **armed re-freeze** is not fixed here; the fix is FuzeInfra\ndeleting its duplicate (#1307).\n- No production alerting on sync health or image staleness. Delegated.\n- **FuzeKeys end-to-end token exchange not verified against the live\ncluster** — needs a cluster credential this session does not hold, and\nprod is GitOps. The route, RBAC and registration ConfigMaps are all in\nplace; the live exchange is unproven.\n- The gate covers the `fuzefront` chart via the existing\n`values-local`/`values-prod` matrix. `deploy/helm/unleash` and\n`FuzeQuality/deploy/helm/fuzequality` — under the same AppProject — are\n**not** checked; neither renders a cluster-scoped kind today, so there\nis nothing for layer 1 to catch there yet. Extending it is the next\nincrement.\n- The gate is **pre-merge only**. It cannot see a cluster whose\nAppProject was replaced out from under it (§4).\n- Nothing enforces the kind→scope table''s *correctness*, only its\ncompleteness; a kind misclassified as namespaced would wrongly pass\nlayer 1. Known residual.\n\nFull analysis, evidence and limits:\n`docs/planning/workload-identity-layering.md`. Sibling, unrelated: #1202\n(untouched).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_014CG1GaTmY2tbc5DcHLVUSX)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwiOUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8nwQAC4yuS7eYxAKC4GuUvzlTTZm\n8UpRYZi1qFueIbuULLxF4keuij0YDl5eNchZV2sfr2kkX8NFE+zvPR4iWywGNmZc\nWwEVLHAS86j0F+Ae/OgSR/E0nL+jgVxv7WrX6QR0YGBOLmM+BLuJnZk47Zu6NS7q\nh5kaIBVJok8nUq4MWT06+Y6A8pKvGU2IGl7ablY6+UQNeRJ3RTefCskfDG9Gmpzw\nn1TXpJUYauW2YDWeHGv24hbd+RlGJUxFMAEdLvtTmg9nVPeSPl8V9N4S9y0CEXTp\n234xfW9LWfhzrZPn+8F1JGfvFRNxul6De6C1Oy/6YlpubxLkET8BQm3dwhY6X5Da\n9BmCk/Sc+sZqqfd5yIH4lIQSDmdgmSd38Z3p7rCz9tNMX